20261118-17: Fix: in Artica, The local DNS cache service no longer starts several copies of itself: the watchdog now starts it the right way, and the extra copies left running are stopped automatically.
20261118-17: Fix: in Artica, The notification bar no longer fills the PHP log with database errors on a freshly installed appliance that has not checked for updates yet.
20261118-17: Add: in Artica, The Samba file synchronization rules are now shown as cards that explain each rule in plain words, translate its schedule into a sentence, show the files copied, deleted and transferred by its last run, its safety settings, and a clearer live progress.
20261118-17: Add: in Artica Meta, The Scenarios page now explains what a scenario is with an example, shows each scenario as a card with its install order, the groups that follow it and the results of its nodes, and puts Apply now, Keep a group in line, Edit and State on each card.
20261118-17: Fix: in Artica Meta, The Scenarios page no longer shows placeholder codes instead of its labels.
20261118-17: Add: in Artica, The Documentary search Models tab now explains AI search in plain words, compares it with keyword search, and lists the five steps it needs with the next one to do and the share of documents already prepared.
20261118-17: Fix: in Artica, The certificate usage inventory no longer reports the cluster client certificate as a broken reference, and never returns the content of a setting that is not a certificate name.
20261118-17: Add: in Artica Reverse Proxy, The Docker Relay page now presents what the feature brings, guides the first setup in five steps computed from the appliance state, and highlights the connectors online, the open connections, the bandwidth saved by compression and self-publishing containers.
20261118-17: Fix: in Artica Proxy, On a load balancer, each nightly archive of the proxies' access logs no longer overwrites the previous one, so every day of legal logs is kept.
20261118-17: Add: in HaCluster, A proxy server can now tell the load balancer how much traffic it can take, from its system load, file descriptors, connected clients and CPU usage, so that a busy server receives fewer new connections before it has to be taken out of the cluster (disabled by default).
20261118-17: Add: in HaCluster, A proxy server taken out of the cluster now gives the reason to the load balancer, and its agent status reports its current weight and what limits it.
20261118-17: Fix: in HaCluster, A proxy server that had been set to a reduced weight now returns to full weight once it has recovered.
20261118-17: Fix: in HaCluster, A proxy server with too many clients whose proxy port no longer answers is now taken out of the cluster instead of being kept at half weight.
20261118-17: Fix: in HaCluster, The load limits of a proxy server are no longer ignored when the load period is set to an unexpected value.
20261118-17: Fix: in Artica, The WordPress Docker image is rebuilt with current security fixes for its system libraries and its management agent; existing sites receive it when their container is recreated.
20261118-17: Fix: in Artica, The Dolibarr Docker image now ships Dolibarr 24.0.3 and current security fixes for its system libraries and its management agent.
20261118-17: Fix: in Artica, Security scans of the Dolibarr Docker image no longer report vulnerabilities in libraries that the image does not contain.
20261118-17: Fix: in Artica Proxy, The web filtering rules page no longer reports a rule that allows only its always-allowed categories as blocking nothing, and shows a rule as waiting for counters instead of unused while the filter has not reported its traffic yet.
20261118-17: Add: in Artica Proxy, The web filtering rules page now reads each rule as a plain sentence (who, what is blocked, what is always allowed), shows how many people are filtered and which rules need attention, and points to the fix for a rule without source or category or with source errors.
20261118-17: Fix: in HaCluster, The Service events page now highlights the moments when no proxy server was available, and searching for a word containing a slash or a space no longer fails.
20261118-17: Add: in HaCluster, The Service events page now explains each event in plain words, summarizes outages, servers back online, configuration changes and automatic repairs, can be filtered by kind, and finds the events of a server from its name.
20261118-17: Fix: in Artica, Installing a Dolibarr site in a Docker container now completes: the administrator account, the company name, the country and the currency are created instead of the installation failing.
20261118-17: Fix: in Artica, A Dolibarr installation that stopped halfway can now be started again and finishes, instead of being reported as already installed with missing company settings.
20261118-17: Fix: in Artica, Upgrading the Dolibarr database of a Docker site now really migrates it, instead of reporting success without changing anything.
20261118-17: Fix: in Artica, A Dolibarr Docker site no longer stops serving pages for a moment when its address or name is changed, and keeps working after a Dolibarr upgrade.
20261118-17: Fix: in Artica, A Dolibarr Docker container no longer fails to start after a restart, and its database account is recreated when the database files were reset.
20261118-17: Fix: in Artica, A Dolibarr Docker site no longer serves hidden configuration files, and changing the password of an account that does not exist now reports that the account was not found.
20261118-17: Fix: in Artica Meta, The L2 fleet page, the L2 switching tab of a node and the switch alert setting now display their labels in every console language instead of raw placeholders.
20261118-17: Add: in Artica Meta, The L2 fleet page now explains in plain words what it watches, shows at a glance how many nodes need attention, and describes each switch problem with what it means and where to fix it.
20261118-17: Fix: in Artica Meta, A proxy policy sent to a node where the proxy service is not installed is now accepted: its settings are saved on the node and take effect when the proxy service is installed, instead of the policy being refused.
20261118-17: Fix: in Artica Meta, Detaching or deleting the last policy of a node whose delivery had been refused no longer leaves the node held by that policy, so its features (for example installing the proxy service) can be managed again.
20261118-17: Add: in Artica, A drive letter can now be chosen for each file share in the new Windows Client tab: Windows computers with the File Sharing client connect the share under that letter automatically, and move or remove the drive when the letter changes or is cleared.
20261117-17: Add: in Artica Meta, A policy can now be copied from the policies list and pasted as a new policy of the same type with the same content, ready to be attached and applied.
20261117-17: Add: in Artica Meta, APT updates (package lists refresh, upgrade of all packages, distribution upgrade or one named package) can be launched on all managed nodes or on one group, eight nodes at a time, with a per-node progress report; blacklisted, disabled and offline nodes are skipped.
20261117-17: Add: in Artica Proxy, The Caching - Expert Mode window of a reverse-proxy site has been redesigned: a plain explanation of what the cache does and never does, readable durations, the risk of each option stated before it is enabled, and clear Never cache and Cache longer rule lists with examples.
20261117-17: Fix: in Artica Proxy, Changing the expert cache of a reverse-proxy site now requires web administrator rights, refuses out-of-range values, and asks for confirmation before turning the cache off because its stored copies are deleted.
20261117-17: Fix: in Artica, When the browser stops a request because it asks again to trust the console certificate, the page now shows a yellow message inviting to refresh it, instead of the red "HTTP 0" error.
20261117-17: Fix: in Artica Proxy, In the parameters of a reverse-proxy site, the Optimization line lists the enabled optimizations and is only shown in red when one of them cannot work, instead of an error for a site with nothing enabled.
20261117-17: Fix: in Artica Proxy, In the parameters of a reverse-proxy site, clicking the Cipher suites line now opens the cipher suites instead of the SSL parameters.
20261118-17: Add: in Artica Meta, A new "Scenarios" menu describes the features a node must have installed and applies them strictly to nodes or groups: missing features are installed in order and features not in the scenario are uninstalled.
20261118-17: Add: in Artica Meta, A scenario attached to a group keeps every member in line with it, including nodes that join the group later.
20261117-17: Fix: in Artica, Changing the root password no longer sends it in the address of the internal API, so it no longer appears in the API request log, and the password now needs at least 8 characters.
20261117-17: Fix: in Artica, The Associated services column of the Certificates center no longer stays empty on appliances that have no running reverse-proxy, and shows Usage unknown instead of Not used when the inventory cannot be read.
20261117-17: Add: in Artica HaCluster, The cluster node dashboard now explains in plain language which checks keep the node in the load-balancer pool, shows when its client certificate expires, and lets you switch debug mode directly.
20261117-17: Fix: in Artica HaCluster, The cluster node settings now save only their own fields and require a system administrator, the dashboard is restricted to proxy and system administrators, and the Active Directory password is no longer sent back to the browser.
20261117-17: Add: in Artica, Restoring a Docker disk quota volume now offers the list of its backups with their date and size, instead of asking for a backup identifier.
20261117-17: Add: in Artica, The Docker disk quota tab shows the names of the containers a volume is attached to, and a running quota operation can be cancelled.
20261117-17: Fix: in Artica, The Docker disk quota tab no longer offers actions on a volume that needs repair, which the Docker manager refused anyway.
20261117-17: Fix: in Artica, Errors returned when creating a Docker volume with a size limit are now shown in the console language instead of English.
20261117-17: Add: in Artica, The disk quota tab of a Docker container now shows each size-capped volume as a card with a fill gauge that warns when it is almost full, the state in plain words, only the actions allowed in that state, and a history with the step and error of every operation.
20261117-17: Add: in Artica, The live statistics of a Docker container were redesigned: they show the container's state and health, processor and memory use explained in plain words, network and disk speeds instead of totals only, a warning when memory gets close to its limit, and a clear message when the container is stopped, paused or restarting instead of a flat chart.
20261117-17: Add: in Artica Meta, The new System users policy keeps the same accounts, groups, sudo rules and SSH access on a whole fleet of nodes; passwords are stored only as a sealed hash and are never shown again.
20261117-17: Fix: in Artica, Passwords of system accounts are no longer sent in the address of the internal API and therefore no longer appear in the API request log.
20261117-17: Fix: in Artica, Changing a system account, its password, its groups or its sudo rules now requires a system administrator account, and system accounts and protected groups can no longer be changed from the System users page.
20261117-17: Fix: in Artica, Every sudo rule of an account or group is now applied, not only the last one, and a sudo rule that sudo would refuse is no longer saved.
20261117-17: Fix: in Artica, Deleting a system account or group now removes its sudo rules and SSH access, so a new account that receives the same identifier no longer inherits them, and the password database keeps the permissions that su and sudo need.
20261117-17: Add: in Artica, Nodes managed by Artica Meta can receive the System users policy: accounts, groups, sudo rules and SSH access are applied next to the local ones, shown read-only on the System users page, and given back or removed when the policy is released.
20261117-17: Add: in Artica Reverse Proxy, The backend error window of a website now explains in plain words what failed, which internal server is concerned, what visitors experience and what to check, with the state of every server of the website.
20261117-17: Add: in Artica Reverse Proxy, The EdgeGuard page now explains what the web application shield brings, guides the link to the central console in three steps with its prerequisites checked, and shows the requests blocked, the attacking sources and the most targeted websites once linked.
20261117-17: Fix: in Artica Reverse Proxy, Linking or unlinking EdgeGuard and uploading its enrollment file now require a system administrator, and the EdgeGuard page is no longer reachable by accounts without web or system administration rights.
20261117-17: Add: in Artica, The Windows identities page of the file server was redesigned: it explains in plain words what is recorded and for how long, shows the retention actually configured, separates what the server confirmed from what the computer only reported, shows when an account last changed computer or Windows identity, and explains before forgetting a record that nothing is revoked and that it will be written again at the next sign-in.
20261117-17: Fix: in Artica, The texts of the File Sharing Windows client were reviewed in its eight languages: the same word is now used for the same thing everywhere, Windows terms match those of Microsoft, and several mistranslations were corrected.
20261117-17: Add: in Artica Reverse Proxy, The Backend SLA page now explains in plain language whether each server behind your websites is online, fast and keeping its availability promise, lists the servers that need attention first, and filters them in one click.
20261117-17: Add: in Artica Meta, The New policy window now presents policy types as clickable tiles grouped by theme (System, Proxy, Web filtering, DNS, Network and security, Directory and Meta), each with a short explanation, plus a search box.
20261117-17: Add: in Artica, The Samba Events page now shows who is connected right now, readable service journals with errors highlighted and repeated messages grouped, and the file-sharing service status in plain language.
20261117-17: Fix: in Artica, The Samba Events page now lists the people actually connected instead of an empty row, even with a file-sharing service that still returns its whole connection history.
20261117-17: Fix: in Artica, The Samba usage history over the last 24 hours now counts 24 whole hours instead of 25, and the other periods count exactly 60 minutes, 7 days of hours or 30 days.
20261117-17: Fix: in Artica, The Samba service health panel no longer fails with an internal error when the file-sharing daemon reports its version.
20261117-17: Add: in Artica, The Samba statistics page was redesigned: it shows the people and computers connected now, how busy the file server was over the last hour, day, week or month, how much data was read and written, which shared folders were used and who connected over the last 30 days, and it explains the quiet hours and the hours when the server was stopped instead of showing empty values.
20261117-17: Fix: in Artica, Text dragged or pasted into a note of the File Sharing Windows client from another application now arrives as plain text, and text can be dragged to another place inside a note.
20261117-17: Add: in Artica, The Samba file server statistics now measure the data read and written by each file server instance and the number of requests it served, so the usage history shows real transfer volumes instead of empty values.
20261117-17: Fix: in Artica, The Samba file server statistics now record every check even when nobody is connected, so usage history tells quiet hours from hours when the server was stopped, uses the appliance's local time, reports who connected and which shared folders were used, and the current session count no longer adds up a month of history.
20261117-17: Fix: in Artica Proxy, The proxy PAC service now also answers when it is requested through the proxy itself by its host name, instead of the proxy showing a "Connection refused" error.
20261117-17: Add: in Artica, The Samba live sessions page was redesigned: it shows which shared folders each computer has open, lists only the folders in use with a "Disconnect everyone" button, groups open files by folder, explains the consequences before disconnecting and reports a failed disconnection instead of hiding it.
20261117-17: Fix: in Artica Proxy, The statistics database of the load balancer is compacted again even when the daemon restarts every day, so it no longer grows until the disk fills up.
20261117-17: Fix: in Artica, The memory watchdog no longer restarts the daemon in the middle of a database compaction, and an interrupted compaction no longer blocks the following ones.
20261117-17: Fix: in Artica Proxy, The proxy statistics database is no longer readable by every local account.
20261117-17: Fix: in Artica, Pages that refuse an action now say "Access denied" instead of a message about tenants, and SIEM statistics pages explain that no SIEM tenant is granted to the account and who can grant one.
20261117-17: Add: in Artica, The semantic engine panel of the Samba documentary search now explains AI search in plain words, lists the five steps that make it ready with the next one to do, shows how many documents are waiting for AI processing, and warns in Semantic settings when the chosen storage would keep AI search from working.
20261117-17: Add: in Artica, The Models tab of the Samba documentary search now explains in plain words what the local AI model does, shows whether AI search is ready and why not, warns when the model in use is missing or damaged, and leads to Semantic settings to choose a model.
20261117-17: Fix: in Artica, When a local DNS record is invalid, the DNS cache service now regenerates or disables that single record and starts, instead of staying down.
20261117-17: Fix: in KasperskyTIP, The console language chosen with the EN/FR switch is now remembered across pages and sessions instead of reverting on the next click.
20261117-17: Add: in KasperskyTIP, A new About page shows the daemon version, build date and uptime, together with the legal notice: free software, independent from Kaspersky, provided without warranty.
20261117-17: Add: in Artica, The Dependencies tab of the Samba documentary search now says in plain words what the server can read (PDF files, scanned documents and images, remote Windows shares, AI search), only raises an alert for a feature that is in use, names the package to install, and checks that every text recognition language chosen in the settings is installed.
20261117-17: Fix: in KasperskyTIP, The feed statistics chart no longer flickers: each feed keeps its colour, points are shown in time order and a missed fetch is shown as a gap instead of a drop to zero.
20261117-17: Add: in Artica, A new Artica Meta policy "SSH" pushes the OpenSSH settings, client address rules and authorized public keys to a fleet of nodes, next to their local rules and keys, and refuses any change that would cut SSH access (requires debian-agent 1.2.7).
20261117-17: Add: in Artica, The My computers page now explains what the device inventory is for, counts devices with a fixed IP, a DNS name, unknown or recently updated ones in clickable tiles, lists friendly names and services per device, and asks for confirmation with the number of devices and the consequences before deleting.
20261117-17: Fix: in Artica, On the My computers page, the +fixed and +asc/+desc search keywords now filter and sort as documented, "order by name" sorts by name, the last update of a device no longer appears one or two hours too old, deleting the results of a search by hardware address no longer fails, and deleting devices now requires the right to manage computers.
20261117-17: Add: in Artica, The "All notes" window of the File Sharing Windows client now looks like the Sticky Notes list: its own title bar, a large rounded search box with a back arrow that clears the search, and airy tinted cards showing the date at the top right.
20261117-17: Add: in Artica, A new Artica Meta policy "Hosts file" pushes /etc/hosts entries to a fleet of nodes, next to the local entries each node keeps (requires debian-agent 1.2.6).
20261117-17: Add: in Artica, The hosts file page now explains what an entry does, shows whether each entry is applied, managed automatically or skipped (with the reason), and warns before saving an entry that will not be applied.
20261117-17: Fix: in Artica, Adding, editing or removing a hosts file entry now requires DNS or system administrator rights on the server side, and removing an older entry no longer deletes the other entries that share its address.
20261117-17: Add: in Artica, The DNS Firewall events page now tells in plain words what the service did: each DNS server is shown with its current state, outages, recoveries, restarts and security warnings stand out, repeated messages are grouped, and the log can be filtered by kind of event.
20261117-17: Fix: in Artica, The "Website forbidden access" tile of a reverse-proxy website now turns the deny-all option on and off directly, with a confirmation before blocking, instead of opening the general settings window.
20261117-17: Add: in Artica, The Samba file synchronization "Connections" page now opens with a plain-language introduction, shows one readiness status per connection and how many rules use it, guides the first setup and prevents removing a connection that a rule still uses.
20261117-17: Fix: in Artica Meta, A node no longer stays locked by Artica Meta for up to three minutes when its last policy of a type is detached or deleted while a delivery to that node was about to start.
20261117-17: Add: in Artica Meta, A new "RBL" policy pushes reputation rules and DNSBL server groups to many remote sites, where nginx, SSH and the DNS Firewall use them, and it can be created from the local reputation rules of an existing node, which Artica Meta then takes over without breaking the sites that already use them.
20261117-17: Add: in Artica Meta, An RBL policy can be linked to a DNS Firewall policy so that the Artica Meta DNS Firewall rules can use its reputation lists as a black list or a white list.
20261117-17: Add: in Artica, The reputation page now shows the rules and server groups held by an Artica Meta policy as read-only with an Artica Meta badge, and refuses to reset the reputation rules while Artica Meta manages some.
20261117-17: Fix: in Artica Proxy, The object items window now shows the object name with its real type, and its tab is labelled "Items".
20261117-17: Fix: in Artica Proxy, Changing the optimization of a reverse-proxy site now requires web administrator rights, and its form can only change the optimization settings of that site.
20261117-17: Add: in Artica, Notes of the File Sharing Windows client look like sticky notes: each note has its own color, text can be bold, italic, underlined, struck through or bulleted, and a screenshot can be attached in one click.
20261117-17: Fix: in Artica, The File Sharing Windows client no longer warns that it runs in an administrator session when the connection is made from an ordinary user's command prompt.
20261117-17: Add: in Artica Proxy, The Optimization window of a reverse-proxy site has been redesigned: a summary of every optimization, one card per feature with a plain explanation and its current values, and warnings when a module is missing or a setting is overridden.
20261117-17: Add: in Artica, The items tab of a rule object explains in plain words what the object contains and how its values are compared, shows its enabled and disabled item counts, and displays full values with who added them and when.
20261117-17: Fix: in Artica, Deleting an item of a rule object now asks for confirmation, and enabling or deleting an item now requires administrator rights and is refused on objects managed by Artica Meta.
20261117-17: Add: in Artica, The Index sources page of the Samba documentary search explains what a source is, shows each share's size on disk, the last scan as a readable age and the error reported by the last scan, filters the list by name or by errors, and lets you pick the share to index from cards.
20261117-17: Fix: in Artica, A share added to the Samba documentary search is now scanned right away instead of waiting for the next periodic check, and notes, mail archive or remote SMB sources can no longer be turned into local shares by editing them.
20261117-17: Fix: in Artica Proxy, Read-only proxy monitoring accounts can no longer link, unlink, invert, reorder or create the objects of a rule.
20261117-17: Add: in Artica Proxy, The Proxy objects tab of a rule now explains how its objects combine, sums the rule up in one readable sentence, shows disabled objects, descriptions and errors with their effect, asks for confirmation before inverting or unlinking an object, and opens New object, Link object (searchable, grouped by type) and New group of objects in windows.
20261117-17: Fix: in Artica Reverse Proxy, A new website now listens on the server's main network card when that card is not named eth0 (ens18, eno1, enp3s0...), so it no longer ends up reachable on port 80 only.
20261117-17: Fix: in Artica, Installing an application from the Docker store now uses the image already present on the server instead of failing when that image is not published on Docker Hub.
20261116-17: Add: in Artica, Network cards and bonds can now be grouped into VLAN-aware layer 2 switches with access and trunk ports, SVIs that give the appliance an address in each VLAN, LACP status of bond ports, STP, RSTP or MSTP spanning tree with BPDU guard, root guard and loop guard, err-disabled port recovery, and a confirmation window that restores the previous network if a change is not confirmed in time.
20261116-17: Add: in Artica, The DNS firewall rules page of the DNS load-balancing service shows each rule in evaluation order with what it matches, its action, its target and its share of requests, flags incomplete rules and rules not yet loaded, and pins the Default rule at the bottom.
20261116-17: Fix: in Artica, Deleting a DNS firewall rule now asks for confirmation and is recorded in the audit log, and enabling, moving or deleting a rule now requires DNS administrator rights.
20261116-17: Add: in Artica, Artica Meta shows the L2 switching state of each node and of the whole fleet, read-only.
20261116-17: Add: in Artica, Artica Meta notifies the administrator when a node gets an L2 problem (err-disabled port, unsynced MST tree, loop guard, conflicting transaction) and when it is resolved.
20261116-17: Add: in Artica, The L2 switching state of a node can be read in one call, so that Artica Meta can display it.
20261116-17: Add: in Artica, The DNS-over-HTTPS page of the DNS load-balancing service shows whether the service really answers, the addresses to give to clients with a copy button, the certificate and its expiry date, and the queries counted since the last restart.
20261116-17: Fix: in Artica, DNS-over-HTTPS can no longer be enabled without a certificate or without a network interface, which left it silently stopped, and its query counter now adds up every listening address.
20261116-17: Fix: in Artica, After a Kerberos keytab is imported on a cluster load balancer, a failed check is retried for 15 minutes while Active Directory replicates before an alert is raised, and a notification now reports when the keytab works again.
20261116-17: Fix: in Artica, On a cluster slave, the Web console now uses the certificate selected on the master once it is replicated, unless WebConsole parameters are excluded from replication, and reloads when that certificate changes.
20261116-17: Fix: in Artica, The Web console no longer sends the intermediate and root certificates several times in its TLS chain.
20261116-17: Fix: in Artica, The certificates center now counts a certificate expiring within 30 days as urgent, instead of only within 3 days.
20261116-17: Fix: in Artica, The certificates center now lists every service using a certificate (Web console, SMTP, proxy ports, HaCluster...), not only reverse-proxy web sites.
20261116-17: Fix: in Artica Proxy, Descriptions of proxy object items containing spaces or special characters are now saved and displayed as typed instead of showing encoded text such as "%20".
20261116-17: Add: in Artica, The DNS load-balancing global settings page groups its options into explained cards and warns before saving that the service restarts.
20261116-17: Fix: in Artica, The DNS load-balancing minimum TTL sent to clients now takes effect, port sharing shows its real state and can no longer be turned off while the service needs it to answer, and the cache size shows the 300 MB really used by default with the number of answers it holds.
20261116-17: Fix: in Artica, The EDNS client subnet option of the DNS load-balancer can be edited again from its settings page.
20261116-17: Fix: in Artica, A local DNS record of type A or AAAA holding a host name instead of an address no longer prevents the DNS cache service from starting: it is refused when saved and skipped when the configuration is built.
20261116-17: Fix: in Artica, Changing the ClamAV scan limits (Stream MAX Length, Maximal size of files) now restarts the antivirus so the new limits apply at once, instead of keeping the previous limits until the next restart.
20261116-17: Add: in Artica, The DNS load-balancing status page shows each pool with its health, cache fill and hit rate, and asks for confirmation before a server is set down, set up or returned to its health checks.
20261116-17: Fix: in Artica Proxy, Disconnecting a proxy from its HaCluster load balancer now always completes, even when the cluster client service was already partly removed.
20261116-17: Fix: in Artica, The file sharing service no longer returns the domain administrator and domain join passwords of an instance when its settings are read.
20261116-17: Add: in Artica Meta, A new "DNS Firewall" policy pushes the same DNS Firewall settings, DoH settings and rules to many remote sites, with a status and graphs view per node.
20261116-17: Add: in Artica DNS Firewall, The status center and the server up/down actions now run through the Artica daemon.
20261116-17: Fix: in Artica, The DNS Firewall now enforces the minimum DNS TTL when it is enabled in the console, instead of ignoring the setting; appliances where the setting was enabled start raising short TTLs to this minimum after the update, and the settings page now shows the setting as it is really applied.
20261116-17: Add: in Artica, The DNS Firewall rules, settings and DNS-over-HTTPS options held by an Artica Meta policy are shown as read-only with an Artica Meta badge, and refusing to delete one keeps its row.
20261116-17: Fix: in Artica, The Restore button of the Backup snapshots list asks for confirmation again instead of doing nothing when clicked.
20261116-17: Fix: in Artica, A file sharing instance can no longer use the appliance's own IP address, which made the web console and SSH unreachable after a restart; an appliance already in this state gets its access back automatically.
20261116-17: Fix: in Artica, The DNS Firewall no longer lets its category caches grow without limit, which used up the memory of DNS servers after a few weeks and kept outdated categories until a restart.
20261116-17: Fix: in Artica Proxy, Cluster members no longer receive the master proxy's name and unique identifier, which could take a member out of the load-balancer after a Squid restart.
20261116-17: Fix: in Artica Proxy, A cluster member no longer sends its access logs to the wrong server when a settings read briefly fails, which made the load-balancer reject them and lose that member's statistics.
20261116-17: Fix: in Artica Proxy, The logging service of a cluster member is no longer restarted several times per hour because its configuration flipped between two versions.
20261116-17: Fix: in Artica, The system scheduler no longer crashes every 30 minutes when the PHP session cleanup task prints warnings; its output is no longer mailed.
20261116-17: Fix: in Artica, The DHCP service fills in the manufacturer of each leased computer again, without overwriting a manufacturer entered by the administrator.
20261116-17: Fix: in Artica, The automatic console zoom no longer shrinks pages too much on scaled displays: it now keeps half of the display scaling (90 % at 125 %, 85 % at 150 % and above) instead of cancelling it.
20261116-17: Fix: in Artica, Upgrading the File Sharing Windows client by double-click no longer stalls when the service cannot be stopped by the user account, and a restart requested afterwards can no longer delete the newly installed program when an antivirus briefly locked the old one.
20261116-17: Fix: in Artica, The DHCP server tab of the dashboard no longer shows an untranslated column title for the lease end, and no longer carries a leftover "empty cache" action copied from the DNS filter page.
