20261108-17: Add: in Artica Meta, An RDS Proxy policy now manages its access rules (rights, members, targets, source networks, time periods, web exit) and its members, local accounts or Active Directory groups picked in a node's directory tree, in two new tabs of the policy editor.
20261108-17: Add: in Artica Meta, An RDS Proxy policy now manages the connection targets (RDP, VNC, SSH and web applications, with their passwords and keys stored encrypted and never displayed) and the TLS policies for older servers, in two new tabs of the policy editor.
20261108-17: Add: in Artica, The Artica tab of a Meta agent lists every tracked software with its installed version and the newer version available in the Meta repository, with an Update button on each outdated package.
20261108-17: Add: in Artica, A Meta proxy policy can now define the listening ports of its nodes (interfaces through virtual network cards, TLS or SSL decryption with a certificate found by name); existing ports keep their identity so port-bound rules still apply, and transparent or special ports are left untouched.
20261108-17: Add: in Artica, The features tab of a Meta agent now shows the DHCP server, the DNS cache and the RDP Proxy as cards with their state, and can activate or deactivate the RDP Proxy of an Artica node.
