20261106-17: Fix: in Artica Proxy, The web filtering error page now withstands a program that requests a blocked site in a loop: background requests get a short refusal, identical pages are served from a 30-second cache, a computer sending too many requests is slowed down, and the page no longer crashes under simultaneous requests.
20261106-17: Add: in Artica AI, The assistant can list the WAF false-positive proposals of the reverse-proxy and, after an administrator approves, apply or reject one; an applied proposal succeeds only once its exceptions are in the published WAF rules, and both decisions can be undone.
20261106-17: Fix: in Artica Reverse Proxy, Publishing WAF rule exceptions through Artica AI is no longer refused once a per-field exception exists.
20261106-17: Fix: in Artica, The RDS proxy no longer appears in the pending software updates, nor in the notification bell, when it is not installed or not enabled.
20261106-17: Add: in Artica, The Incidents tab of the system monitoring page is redesigned: incident counts for the last 24 hours and 30 days, a daily chart, the report storage against its 1,000 MB limit, and each report can be unfolded to list the files of its archive and read why it was created before downloading it.
20261106-17: Add: in Artica Proxy, The HaCluster backends list now shows the memory used by each proxy node as a progress bar, orange above 75% and red above 90%.
20261106-17: Fix: in Artica, The load average, CPU and memory incident reports now appear in the Incidents tab of the system monitoring page, including those recorded before this update.
20261106-17: Add: in Artica Proxy, On a HaCluster load balancer, the network map now shows the load-balancing farm (state, sessions, traffic and alerts of every proxy node) and, for each client computer, its activity through the farm over the last 15 minutes: requests, volume, user and most visited sites.
20261106-17: Add: in Artica Reverse Proxy, The service status page is redesigned as a health and traffic dashboard: service health banner, request, bandwidth, error-rate and cache tiles with trends, a traffic chart with 4xx/5xx errors per period, response and cache breakdowns, a top web sites ranking that adds up to 100 %, backend server health and the statistics memory gauge.
20261106-17: Fix: in Artica, The Network entry of the left menu unfolds its sub-menu again when it is clicked.
20261106-17: Fix: in Artica Proxy, The real-time statistics pages use much less processor and memory on a load balancer: repeated views are served from a one-minute cache, and a request for more than 6 hours of 5-minute detail is answered from the hourly data instead of loading gigabytes of memory.
20261106-17: Fix: in Artica Proxy, The real-time statistics database can no longer fill the disk: it keeps the 5-minute detail for 3 days by default instead of 15, and shortens it automatically when the database exceeds 20% of its disk or would leave less than 10% free.
20261106-17: Fix: in Artica Proxy, The Browse button of the LDAP suffix in the load-balancer Active Directory settings no longer reports invalid credentials when the saved password is kept.
20261106-17: Fix: in Artica Proxy, Browsing the Active Directory LDAP suffix no longer fails randomly depending on the characters of the account, password or server name.
20261106-17: Fix: in Artica Proxy, A failed LDAP suffix detection no longer saves the value "false" as the load-balancer suffix and sends it to the cluster nodes.
20261106-17: Fix: in Artica Proxy, The memory rule that restarts the go-shield service now leaves the same headroom as the service itself (one eighth of the RAM, between 512 MB and 2 GB), so a healthy go-shield is no longer restarted once its cache fills up.
20261106-17: Fix: in Artica Proxy, In an Artica cluster, an IT charter created or changed on the master now reaches the slaves with the next cluster package instead of waiting for an unrelated proxy configuration change.
20261106-17: Fix: in Artica Proxy, On a HaCluster whose proxies also form an Artica cluster, the IT charters created on the cluster master are no longer erased by the empty charter list of the load balancer.
20261106-17: Fix: in Artica Proxy, The log helpers no longer keep rejected log batches forever: quarantined batches are kept one day, 1000 at most, and no longer make each helper re-read the whole queue directory after every batch.
20261106-17: Fix: in Artica Proxy, A HaCluster load balancer whose IT charter table is found empty no longer erases the charters of every node: it restores them from the cluster copy, unless an administrator deleted them from the console.
20261106-17: Fix: in Artica Proxy, Repeated IT charter reconfiguration requests are now merged into a single rebuild instead of reloading the proxy once per request.
20261106-17: Fix: in Artica Proxy, Opening the HaCluster Backends page from its direct address now shows its title, its buttons and its tabs.
20261106-17: Add: in Artica Proxy, The Backends page of the HaCluster load-balancer shows a farm summary (in production, warning, error, drained, disabled) and one card per node with its state in words, its load history against the configured maximum, its sessions, requests, weight and traffic, refreshed every 3 seconds without closing an open menu or dialog.
20261106-17: Fix: in Artica Proxy, On the HaCluster Backends page, starting, stopping, enabling, rebooting, reconfiguring or deleting a node now checks the administrator privilege on the server, and the outgoing traffic of a node is no longer computed from its incoming traffic.
20261106-17: Add: in Artica, The Metrics tab of the HaCluster backends has been redesigned: response times are shown in milliseconds and averaged by requests, a single Backends table combines ranking and health with explicit thresholds, HTTP codes are grouped by class, and the backend detail now shows how sessions ended (termination states).
20261106-17: Add: in Artica, The HaCluster Backends page now has a page header, and the buttons of the backends table and the period, backend, Refresh and Live controls of its Metrics tab are in that header.
20261106-17: Fix: in Artica Proxy, The Go Shield web-filtering cache is now sized from the server memory (one sixteenth, between 256 MB and 2 GB) instead of reserving 2 GB on every proxy, and its memory watchdog no longer restarts it in a loop.
20261106-17: Fix: in Artica Proxy, The access-log helpers now size their in-memory buffer from the server memory, which saves several hundred megabytes per helper on small proxies.
20261106-17: Add: in Artica Proxy, The statistics tab of the proxy dashboard has been redesigned: each tile now shows its trend over the period, a new chart shows requests and bandwidth over time, the Top 10 is a ranked list with its share of all traffic, and the categories donut is measured against the total volume; the period and the Top 10 filters are now in the page header.
20261106-17: Add: in Artica Proxy, The Parameters tab of the HaCluster load-balancer has a search engine that also finds the settings stored inside each dialog, filters for enabled, disabled and items needing attention, and a banner listing the settings that need attention.
20261106-17: Fix: in Artica Proxy, On the HaCluster load-balancer, resetting the agents service certificate now asks for confirmation and checks the administrator privilege, and the Parameters tab refreshes after creating or resetting this certificate.
20261105-17: Fix: in Artica Proxy, On an HaCluster load-balancer, the real-time statistics no longer consume more than one processor core and no longer drop most of the requests they receive from the nodes.
20261105-17: Fix: in Artica, The system monitor no longer restarts the Artica daemon on busy multi-core appliances: its CPU limit now depends on the number of processors, and no CPU limit can be set below 40% of the machine.
20261105-17: Fix: in Artica Proxy, On a node of an HaCluster farm, the Active Directory and Kerberos join forms are now locked with a notice explaining that these settings are managed on the load-balancer.
20261105-17: Fix: in Artica Proxy, A proxy that joins an HaCluster farm now drops the Active Directory settings of an earlier standalone join and aligns with the other nodes, which stops LDAP and machine account errors on that node.
20261105-17: Fix: in Artica Proxy, The Kerberos ticket renewal service no longer fails to start every minute on appliances still carrying the start script of an older version: Artica rewrites it, or removes it when the service is not used.
20261105-17: Fix: in Artica Proxy, With Kerberos authentication, the Active Directory connection test and the Kerberos tasks no longer use an empty password when the console saved only the LDAP password, which raised an "Empty password not allowed" LDAP alert.
20261105-17: Add: in Artica Reverse Proxy, The backend statistics page has a new design: a header with the backend state and any ongoing incident, four key cards (availability, SLA, latency, security), incident bands on the availability chart, a security report with the certificate lifetime, an incident timeline and a clearer health-check table.
20261105-17: Fix: in Artica, The PHP2Shell fix on Debian 10 no longer fails and restores PHP 7.4 on appliances that keep an old PHP 7.0 extension directory, so the security warning goes away once the fix has run.
20261105-17: Fix: in Artica, The PHP2Shell fix on Debian 10 repairs the PHP 7.3 program that older versions had replaced by a link to PHP 7.4, and stops the unused Debian PHP-FPM service on appliances without systemd.
20261105-17: Fix: in Artica, The status task no longer replaces the PHP 7.3 program with a link to PHP 7.4.
20261105-17: Add: in Artica Proxy, The options of a website are now presented as feature cards showing how many header, rewrite and replace rules are active with a preview, the latency alert threshold, and which error pages are customized.
20261105-17: Add: in Artica Proxy, The backends of a website are now shown as searchable tiles with their state, 24-hour availability, latency, security grade and last error, and the website settings are grouped in one menu that shows their current values.
20261105-17: Fix: in Artica Proxy, Website access rules written as an address range no longer prevent the website configuration from being built, and access rules now work on TCP stream websites instead of blocking their configuration.
20261105-17: Add: in Artica Proxy, The access rules of a website now show what happens to unlisted clients and warn when the rules are not applied, use an unsupported address range or target a TCP website; address ranges and duplicate addresses are refused.
20261105-17: Add: in Artica Proxy, The listen port dialog of a website now previews the address nginx will really serve and explains why HTTPS, HTTP/2 or PROXY protocol would not apply.
20261105-17: Add: in Artica RDS Proxy, The NLA listener of the RDS bastion has a list of allowed sources: only these IPv4 addresses or networks can reach its port through the firewall, and the status card warns when every source is allowed.
20261105-17: Add: in Artica Reverse Proxy, The Ports tab of a website now shows how each port is really served (HTTP or HTTPS, HTTP/2, PROXY protocol) and explains why an option is not applied, such as a missing certificate or a globally disabled feature.
20261105-17: Fix: in Artica Reverse Proxy, Changing the port or the interface of a website listening port no longer leaves the old port in place, and a new port is applied immediately.
20261105-17: Fix: in Artica, The small buttons above tables and in forms keep their alternating colors on appliances whose console stylesheet has not been updated yet, instead of turning grey.
20261105-17: Add: in Artica Reverse Proxy, The Server names tab of a website now shows its certificate with its issuer, expiry date and remaining validity, tells for each domain whether the certificate covers it (including wildcard certificates), and no longer shows the DNS resolution and availability columns that were always red.
20261105-17: Add: in Artica RDS Proxy, Domain workstations that require NLA can now sign in to the bastion with Kerberos on a dedicated listener (port 3390 by default).
20261105-17: Fix: in Artica, A service whose old PID file now points to a thread of another program is no longer considered running, so the watchdog restarts it instead of leaving it stopped (the status collector stayed down for days).
20261105-17: Add: in Artica Sandbox, A performance page shows how long attachments wait in the queue and run in each analysis machine, by file type and by machine, to help size the analysis machines.
20261105-17: Add: in Artica AI, The new command artica-ai -check-catalog checks the console action skills of an installed catalog (risk, permission, verification, rollback) and reports every inconsistency.
20261105-17: Add: in Artica Proxy, The Proxy.pac/WPAD status page now shows the requests, unique clients, PAC served ratio and top rule of the last 24 hours with their trend, warns when statistics are unavailable or incomplete, and only proxy administrators can change its settings.
20261105-17: Fix: in Artica Sandbox, Files dropped by a malicious attachment are marked malicious only when they are programs or scripts and have no verdict yet, so decoy documents and standard Windows libraries are no longer blocked.
20261105-17: Fix: in Artica Sandbox, Heuristic, potentially unwanted and phishing antivirus detections no longer make an attachment malicious on their own: the file is analysed in the sandbox instead.
20261105-17: Fix: in Artica Sandbox, Scripts padded with comments, WSF jobs, encoded scripts and HTML or SVG pages carrying a script are now analysed instead of being reported as an unsupported file type.
20261105-17: Fix: in Artica Sandbox, Analysis tasks the sandbox lost track of are now removed from the CAPE engine with their copies of the attachment, and a virtual machine still busy with an abandoned task is no longer given a new one.
20261105-17: Fix: in Artica Proxy, The Proxy.pac service no longer stops when the web error page uses the same port: the error page now forwards Proxy.pac and WPAD requests to it instead of the two services killing each other.
20261105-17: Fix: in Artica Proxy, When no Proxy.pac rule applies, browsers now receive a valid script that connects directly instead of an error.
20261105-17: Add: in Artica, A stopped service card now has a thick red border so it stands out from running services.
20261105-17: Add: in Artica, Button bars now alternate five colors: green, light blue, blue, orange and emerald.
20261105-17: Fix: in Artica, Active buttons are colored again and alternate green, light blue, blue and orange in button bars as before; white is now kept for disabled buttons only, red for deletions.
20261105-17: Fix: in Artica, The page header buttons keep their colors and spacing even when the browser still holds an older console stylesheet, and the main button no longer turns dark green with an inner shadow when clicked.
20261105-17: Add: in Artica Sandbox, Submitted attachments are now analysed in the CAPE engine and receive a clean, suspicious or malicious verdict based on proven malicious behaviour, a detected malware family or an antivirus match.
20261105-17: Fix: in Artica, The "Optimizations for Virtual machines" notification now comes back when the disk settings drift again (new disk, partial optimization), and no longer appears for a setting the system cannot change.
20261105-17: Fix: in Artica, After clicking Optimize in the "Optimizations for Virtual machines" notification, the notification and its counter now disappear from the bell at once, and an error is shown if the optimization could not be started.
20261105-17: Add: in Artica, The buttons and the wiki help shown next to an Active or Inactive state on card lines now use the console button design and the same size as the other line buttons.
20261105-17: Add: in Artica, The buttons and the wiki help shown next to a value on card lines now use the console button design and the same size as the other line buttons.
20261105-17: Add: in Artica, The edit pencil on card lines and table rows now uses the console button design, is announced to screen readers, and shows a padlock with the reason when the administrator cannot edit.
20261105-17: Add: in Artica, A new Network map page (Network menu) shows the appliance, its interfaces and the computers seen on each network, with their proxy traffic and tracked connections, built from local data only; it is also available to the AI assistant.
20261105-17: Fix: in Artica, The button bar of status and information cards no longer disappears for administrators without the required privilege: the buttons stay visible with a padlock that explains why they are locked.
20261105-17: Add: in Artica, The action button on each line of status and information cards now uses the same design as the buttons of table rows, sized to its label, with deletions in red.
20261105-17: Add: in Artica, The action buttons at the bottom of status and information cards now use the same design as the settings form buttons, sized to their label instead of a fixed width.
20261105-17: Add: in Artica, Each download of a DNS cache threat list (RPZ) now writes a syslog line naming the list, its URL and the address contacted, and identifies itself with an Artica User-Agent, so security teams can link the outbound connection to its cause.
20261105-17: Add: in Artica, The buttons at the bottom of every settings form now use the console button design: Apply is the main button, extra buttons take their color from their action instead of rotating colors, and a locked form shows a padlock on its button.
20261105-17: Add: in Artica, The HaCluster load period choice is now a proper option group: the selected period is filled and checked, and the arrow keys move between periods.
20261105-17: Fix: in Artica, The passive network discovery (ARP listener) now uses a single lightweight socket instead of one capture buffer per interface, no longer puts interfaces in promiscuous mode, and keeps a bounded list of hosts, which greatly reduces its memory use.
20261105-17: Fix: in Artica, The network discovery and DHCP lease statistics no longer erase the aliases, DHCP reservations, PXE and gateway settings of known computers, and no longer refresh every computer in the database and the DNS service every five minutes.
20261105-17: Fix: in Artica, The documentation search of the console now goes through the configured outbound proxy, so it also works on appliances that reach the Internet only through a proxy.
20261105-17: Fix: in Artica, The web console Kerberos file, the boot loader apt hook and the HotSpot Active Directory file are no longer rewritten when their content has not changed.
20261105-17: Add: in Artica, The small button bars above about a hundred tables now use the console button design: the color tells the action instead of rotating between four colors, buttons no longer stay pressed after a click, and locked actions show a padlock with the reason.
20261105-17: Add: in Artica, Table toolbars, action menus, upload buttons and small status buttons now share the console button design: their color tells the action (main, neutral, destructive), a colored dot next to the label shows a service or backend state, and locked actions show a padlock with the reason.
20261105-17: Add: in Artica Proxy, The AI assistant can rebuild the ICAP antivirus configuration and purge its temporary files, with an explicit destructive wipe option, after approval.
20261105-17: Add: in Artica Proxy, The LDAP authentication of the proxy can now be read and disconnected through the REST API and the AI assistant, and disconnecting it now reloads the proxy.
20261105-17: Fix: in Artica Proxy, Temporary files of the ICAP antivirus service older than the configured delay are now actually removed; before, only an oversized temporary folder was ever emptied.
20261105-17: Fix: in Artica Proxy, When the ICAP antivirus service reports a full disk, its temporary folders are now emptied automatically.
20261105-17: Fix: in Artica Proxy, Reloading the ICAP antivirus service while it is stopped no longer breaks its control channel.
20261105-17: Fix: in Artica Proxy, The ICAP request simulator now encodes the answers of the tested ICAP server before displaying them.
20261105-17: Fix: in Artica Proxy, The unused ICAP deferred download options were removed from the ICAP service settings; their download link had never worked.
20261105-17: Fix: in Artica Proxy, The Active Directory status page now offers a button to disconnect the LDAP authentication, which could not be turned off once a Kerberos or NTLM connection was declared.
20261105-17: Add: in Artica, The small buttons in CrowdSec decision tables and the proxy active requests cards now use the console button design and can be reached with the keyboard; an IP already trusted is shown as a status badge instead of a dimmed button.
20261105-17: Fix: in Artica, The notifications page now requires the system administrator privilege for every action, including SMTP, Mattermost and notification rule settings and the SMTP settings export.
20261105-17: Fix: in Artica, The Kerberos authentication forms no longer send the Active Directory administrator password to the browser; leaving the password field empty keeps the saved password for the same account.
20261105-17: Fix: in Artica, The Kerberos authentication page now requires the proxy or system administrator privilege to change the Active Directory account, view its password, renew or upload the keytab, edit the configuration or manage SPNs.
20261105-17: Fix: in Artica Proxy, On the parent proxies status page, accounts with monitoring rights only can no longer edit or view the parent proxies configuration file, switch to direct mode or remove the feature.
20261105-17: Fix: in Artica, Copied websites of the reverse proxy mirror are now displayed in an isolated frame, so scripts from a copied site can no longer act within the administrator session.
20261105-17: Fix: in Artica, The website copy page of the reverse proxy now requires the web administrator privilege for every action, including synchronizing, deleting and viewing copied sites.
20261105-17: Fix: in Artica, The cluster node listener no longer exposes the retired statistics appliance endpoints, which accepted unchecked values in their database queries, and keepalived node reports are now stored safely.
20261105-17: Fix: in Artica, The internal service that runs system commands no longer reveals the size, type, permissions or link target of files outside the folders it actually needs, and 21 unused commands were removed from it.
20261105-17: Add: in Artica Sandbox, The CAPE malware analysis engine is installed and updated in one click from the Sandbox page, which checks the prerequisites, downloads a signed package, shows the progress of each step and offers Retry on the step that failed.
20261105-17: Fix: in Artica, Editing a Docker Store application's stack by hand now requires the Docker secrets privilege, since that stack holds passwords generated by Artica.
20261105-17: Add: in Artica, Authelia can now be installed from the Docker Store in a few fields, and its users and access rules are managed from the console afterwards.
20261105-17: Add: in Artica, Inline buttons (help links under page titles, table row actions, card footers) now use the console button design and can be reached with the keyboard; WordPress templates show a real Enabled/Disabled switch and HaCluster backends show their weight with an explicit In service or Drained state.
20261105-17: Fix: in Artica, A link or form on another web site can no longer make the console change a setting, delete an item or run an action on behalf of a logged-in administrator.
20261105-17: Fix: in Artica, Console pages and background handlers no longer read, copy, overwrite or delete a file outside their own folder when given a crafted file name, and several of them no longer pass unchecked values to system commands.
20261105-17: Fix: in Artica, Uploads to the cluster node listener can no longer write files outside the upload folder.
20261105-17: Fix: in Artica, Windows Update now retries a Microsoft catalog request once after a network error and reports the real cause when the synchronization still fails.
20261105-17: Add: in Artica, Action buttons inside pages now follow the same design as the page header: the color reflects the action (main, neutral or destructive) instead of the page author's choice, locked actions show a padlock and explain why on hover, long labels wrap instead of overflowing, and large setup buttons become clear wizard cards.
20261105-17: Fix: in Artica Proxy, The SquidAnalyzer report viewer now shows each report in an isolated frame, so a URL or user name recorded in the proxy logs can no longer run a script in the console.
20261105-17: Fix: in Artica, Rule, task, interface and field identifiers received in console links are now limited to safe characters, closing a family of script injections in many pages.
20261105-17: Fix: in Artica, Chart labels no longer show &amp; instead of an ampersand, and a few read-only form fields no longer display encoded characters.
20261105-17: Add: in Artica AI, The assistant can now report the state of the CAPE malware sandbox engine and, once approved, install it, update it or resume a failed installation, following the job to its end.
20261105-17: Fix: in Artica, Many console pages no longer build their database queries from values received from the browser, read from logs or typed in forms without escaping them, which allowed SQL injection.
20261105-17: Fix: in Artica, The console search box no longer lets a crafted search add its own SQL to the query through a column name.
20261105-17: Fix: in Artica, About two hundred console pages that show mail, proxy and web requests, DHCP leases, DNS queries, IDS alerts, VPN and SSH logins or system logs no longer run a script hidden in that data, such as a mail subject, a URL, a client hostname or a log line.
20261105-17: Fix: in Artica Messaging, The quarantine and backup viewers now display the HTML body of a message in an isolated frame where its scripts cannot run.
20261105-17: Fix: in Artica, Values saved to PostgreSQL that contain an apostrophe are now escaped correctly, which also closes an injection path in the queries that relied on this escaping.
20261105-17: Add: in Artica, Page header buttons now follow their role instead of their position: one main action in the brand color, neutral secondary actions, destructive actions in red at the end, locked actions explained on hover, and a More menu when a page has many actions.
20261105-17: Fix: in Artica, Console form fields, drop-down lists, text areas, value tables, status tiles and charts no longer run a script contained in a stored or received value, such as a group name, a rule name, a hostname or a log entry.
20261105-17: Fix: in Artica, Several console fields (e-mail, LDAP suffix, color, text buttons) no longer add a backslash before double quotes in the value they save.
20261105-17: Fix: in Artica, About two hundred console pages no longer copy values received in their address into the page without encoding, which let a crafted link run a script in an administrator's session.
20261105-17: Fix: in Artica, Console dialog titles, error and confirmation messages, tabs and read-only form fields no longer run a script contained in the text they display, such as a name, a log line or a value from a link.
20261105-17: Fix: in Artica, The picture, video and text dialogs of the console no longer display or run content supplied in their link.
20261104-17: Fix: in Artica, Console pages no longer let a crafted link run a script through the row and refresh-function parameters of their tables and dialogs.
20261104-17: Fix: in Artica, The Let's Encrypt certificate wizard only runs the refresh script prepared by the console, not one supplied in the link.
20261104-17: Fix: in Artica, About fifty console pages (RADIUS, MIMEDefang, SpamAssassin, strongSwan, SSH portal, WordPress, DHCP routing, ICAP DNSBL, proxy ports and others) no longer insert values received from the browser directly into their database queries.
20261104-17: Fix: in Artica, Eight console pages no longer send back HTML received in their address, which could run a script in the console.
20261104-17: Fix: in Artica, An empty list of SSH allowed groups no longer adds the members of the root group to the users allowed to connect.
20261104-17: Fix: in Artica Proxy, The error page template file manager now requires the proxy administrator privilege and refuses a file name that points outside its upload folder.
20261104-17: Fix: in Artica Proxy, The error page template pages no longer insert the requested file name into database queries.
