20261104-17: Fix: in Artica Reverse Proxy, The expert TLS cipher field no longer lets a console user run system commands, and the page now requires the web administrator privilege.
20261104-17: Fix: in Artica, The system events, scheduled task events and Python packages pages no longer accept SQL code in their parameters.
20261104-17: Fix: in Artica Proxy, The GreenSQL rules page only works on its own two rule tables and now requires the proxy or firewall administrator privilege.
20261104-17: Fix: in Artica Proxy, Importing an error page template can no longer write files outside its working folder or read appliance files through links.
20261104-17: Fix: in Artica Proxy, Exporting an error page template no longer runs system commands built from the template name.
20261104-17: Fix: in Artica, The system events, DHCP pools, hosts file and event pages no longer reflect script code sent in their parameters.
20261104-17: Fix: in Artica, Database errors on the scheduled task events and Python packages pages no longer display the SQL query.
20261104-17: Fix: in Artica, SSH servers configured by an older version without an authentication timeout are now corrected automatically, so unauthenticated connections can no longer block SSH access.
20261104-17: Fix: in Artica Reverse Proxy, The edit button of a website connection limits now opens the general settings window instead of the XML Sitemap one.
20261104-17: Add: in Artica Reverse Proxy, The website parameters are now shown as searchable feature tiles grouped by section, with a section menu, and enabling maintenance mode now asks for confirmation.
20261104-17: Fix: in Artica, Downloaded Docker image SBOMs (CycloneDX and SPDX) now name the image and its tag instead of an internal temporary file.
20261104-17: Fix: in Artica, The search in the SBOM tab of a Docker image report now covers every component of the image, not only the page shown.
20261104-17: Fix: in Artica, A new Docker image no longer creates a failed analysis job when neither Syft nor the CVE scanner is available.
20261104-17: Fix: in Artica, Building and reading the SBOM of a very large Docker image now uses bounded memory and disk, and an oversized inventory is reported as too large instead of an empty tab.
20261104-17: Fix: in Artica, The SBOM analysis is now guaranteed to stay offline, and Go build flags or credentials found in package metadata are no longer stored.
