20261031-17: Add: in Artica Proxy, The TimeOuts tab now groups its settings into client, origin server, parent proxy, service and kernel cards, marks every value that differs from its default, shows when the uploads timeout replaces the read timeout, and edits each group in its own dialog. Saving now reloads the proxy so the new timeouts and TCP settings take effect at once.
20261031-17: Add: in Artica Proxy, The proxy General settings tab is now a dashboard of cards with an attention banner for debug mode, FTP access and Microsoft Connected Cache, and the caching, Windows Updates and FTP switches now ask for confirmation.
20261031-17: Add: in Artica RDS Proxy, The SIEM page now opens on a live status banner, the delivery chain from the bastion through the authentication service to the SIEM (showing where it stops and why), indicators for events waiting to be sent, certificate validity and last acknowledged sending, and a certificate lifetime bar with its renewal thresholds; disconnecting now asks for confirmation in a styled dialog.
20261031-17: Add: in Artica RDS Proxy, The session recordings page now opens on indicators (recordings, space used, archive types, interrupted sessions), the most recorded users and targets and the retention period, and its table shows who connected to which target, when, for how long and what was recorded, with filters by content and labelled actions.
20261031-17: Add: in Artica RDS Proxy, The sessions page now refreshes itself every 10 seconds and opens on indicators (open sessions, protocols, longest and median duration, sessions to watch) and the most used targets, with filters by state and protocol and a labelled Disconnect button on each session.
20261031-17: Fix: in Artica RDS Proxy, The state of a connected session no longer reads "Connection success" on the sessions page.
20261031-17: Add: in Artica RDS Proxy, The web proxies tab now shows the path of the web traffic, indicators for upstream proxies and PAC files, a warning when a disabled proxy still serves policies (their sessions are refused), and one card per proxy or PAC file with its freshness, last download error and labelled actions.
20261031-17: Add: in Artica RDS Proxy, Changing the port or the listening interface of the tunnel receiver now applies immediately without restarting it, and connected agents stay connected.
20261031-17: Add: in Artica RDS Proxy, The tunnel agent downloads are now shown as one tile per program, grouped by Windows and Linux, with the installer signature, a copy button for the file name and the SHA-256 fingerprint, and the ready-to-copy command that checks the fingerprint.
20261031-17: Add: in Artica RDS Proxy, The tunnel receiver can listen on a single network interface instead of all of them, and its firewall rule then opens the port on that interface only.
20261031-17: Add: in Artica RDS Proxy, The Agents tab of the tunnel agents now opens on four indicators (connected agents, open sessions, certificates to renew, pending enrollment codes), and its table can be filtered by state, shows the days left on each certificate, lets you copy a serial number, and uses labelled action buttons.
20261031-17: Add: in Artica RDS Proxy, The Status tab of the tunnel agents now shows the receiver state with the address to give to the agents and a copy button, the connected agents with their sessions and certificate validity, and a warning when every address can reach the receiver port.
20261031-17: Fix: in Artica, The console no longer shrinks its pages further when the browser is already zoomed out below 100%.
20261031-17: Add: in Artica, The retention page now opens on a dashboard showing each retention duration on a common scale, the result of the last database cleaning with a chart of the recent runs, and a summary of the cleaning log.
20261031-17: Fix: in Artica, The Events tab of the retention page now lists the database cleaning log, it always showed an empty table.
20261031-17: Add: in Artica RDS Proxy, The support package now includes the RDS Proxy logs, the tunnel receiver and agent state, the upstream proxies and PAC files, the access refusals and a reachability test of every target, without any private key or password.
20261031-17: Add: in sftpSync, A connection can now relay its files to a second SSH server right after a local <-- remote sync, with its own history, host-key check and deletion confirmation.
20261031-17: Fix: in Artica, The SSH server now writes the CIS-recommended cipher, MAC and key-exchange lists and a 60-second login grace time when the administrator has not chosen other values.
20261031-17: Fix: in Artica, The system journal is now kept on disk across reboots, within the existing size limit.
20261031-17: Fix: in Artica, Log files under /var/log are now restricted to their owner and group, without touching files that another service reads or writes.
20261031-17: Fix: in Artica, Idle interactive shells are now closed after 15 minutes.
20261031-17: Fix: in Artica RDS Proxy, Deleting an upstream web proxy that is still cited by the PAC file of a policy is now refused with a clear message.
20261031-17: Fix: in Artica RDS Proxy, The tunnel receiver now writes its SIEM delivery messages in English.
20261031-17: Fix: in Artica RDS Proxy, The tunnel agents list no longer reports the receiver as stopped right after the receiver is enabled.
20261031-17: Fix: in Artica RDS Proxy, The tunnel agents table now fits the screen on 1440-pixel wide displays.
20261031-17: Fix: in Artica RDS Proxy, The enrollment instructions now explain that an agent installed with the Windows installer starts and connects on its own.
20261031-17: Fix: in Artica RDS Proxy, The target status column now shows a latency instead of a TCP connection time for web targets reached through a proxy or a PAC file.
20261031-17: Fix: in Artica RDS Proxy, A web target reached through an upstream proxy is no longer reported as unreachable when the proxy is slow to answer the first test.
20261031-17: Fix: in Artica RDS Proxy, The Members and Settings labels are capitalized again in English, and help texts no longer break words in the middle.
20261031-17: Add: in Artica, The retention parameters now show as a read-only summary, and the values are changed in a dialog that refreshes the summary once saved.
20261031-17: Fix: in Artica, Service accounts no longer point to a home directory that does not exist, and accounts with a shell get theirs created, which clears the CIS home directory check.
20261031-17: Fix: in Artica, The OS web console home directory is no longer readable by every local user.
20261031-17: Fix: in Artica, The FUSE, CIFS, WebDAV and Kerberos ksu helpers no longer keep a setuid bit that the appliance never uses.
20261031-17: Fix: in Artica, The Docker engine no longer leaves a world-writable state file in its data directory.
20261031-17: Add: in Artica AI, The assistant can attach the Unix socket of an application installed from the Docker Store on the same server (such as a WordPress site) to a reverse-proxy site, with the same proof and undo as the other backend changes.
20261031-17: Fix: in Artica RDS Proxy, Updating an upstream web proxy through the API without the enabled field no longer re-enables a disabled proxy.
20261031-17: Fix: in Artica RDS Proxy, Installing the Windows tunnel agent service without the MSI package is now refused when ordinary users can modify the program or its folder, instead of only showing a warning; the message tells how to fix it.
20261031-17: Fix: in Artica RDS Proxy, Uninstalling the Windows tunnel agent no longer recreates or changes the configuration folder of the agent.
20261031-17: Fix: in Artica RDS Proxy, The enrollment command shown for the Windows tunnel agent MSI now uses %ProgramW6432%, so it works on servers where Windows is not installed on drive C and from a 32-bit command prompt.
20261031-17: Fix: in Artica RDS Proxy, The console only says that the Windows tunnel agent MSI is unsigned when the package really is unsigned.
20261031-17: Fix: in Artica RDS Proxy, The warnings of the connection policy window no longer show the word Warning twice.
20261031-17: Fix: in Artica RDS Proxy, The labels and explanations of SSH targets, SSH transcripts and second factor messages are now translated instead of showing raw text codes.
20261031-17: Add: in Artica, Several WordPress sites can now be installed from the Docker Store on the same server, each with its own stack and its own Unix socket for the local reverse proxy; the Store tile lists the installed sites.
20261030-17: Fix: in Artica RDS Proxy, Active Directory logins now use the port configured in the Active Directory connection, so domain controllers reached over LDAPS (port 636) authenticate users again.
20261030-17: Fix: in Artica RDS Proxy, The reachability status of an http:// web target behind an upstream proxy no longer reports it unreachable when the proxy only allows CONNECT to HTTPS ports.
20261030-17: Add: in Artica Reverse Proxy, A site can now use as backend a Docker application installed on the same server, reached through a local Unix socket without opening any port.
20261030-17: Add: in Artica RDS Proxy, A web target policy can now route its traffic with a PAC file, and each web session shows the name of its target in a banner at the top.
20261030-17: Fix: in Artica RDS Proxy, The Debug switch of the authenticator settings now really enables the detailed authentication log; it previously saved a setting that the authenticator never read.
20261030-17: Add: in Artica, The Docker volumes page now shows how many volumes are used, unused, anonymous or attached to a Compose stack, with small charts, filters, the stack of each volume, and how many volumes the purge would remove.
20261030-17: Add: in Artica, The Docker Store search tab has a larger search field with suggestions, warns about an unreachable source above the results, shows the number of applications found and ranks trust labels with Artica recommendations first.
20261030-17: Add: in Artica, The Docker Store can now install a ready-to-use WordPress site with its own database and its administrator account already created, reachable only through the Artica reverse proxy without opening any port.
20261030-17: Add: in Artica, The Docker Store shows the applications Artica installs turnkey (Vaultwarden and WordPress) when the search is empty or finds nothing, with their state and a one-click install, including with an older Docker manager.
20261030-17: Add: in Artica, The Docker images page no longer shows tabs, and when no image is on the server it invites the administrator to open the Docker Store to find one.
20261030-17: Add: in Artica RDS Proxy, The Windows tunnel agent now installs as a Windows service from an MSI package that can be deployed silently, runs under a dedicated limited account, protects its configuration and logs to the Windows event log.
20261030-17: Add: in Artica, The AI assistant can create or remove a swap file and move the large system directories to another partition, always after an administrator approval and with checks on free space and boot persistence.
20261030-17: Fix: in Artica RDS Proxy, The target list no longer shows a web target as unreachable when it is reached through the upstream proxy of its policy, and shows the agent state for targets reached through a tunnel agent.
20261030-17: Fix: in Artica RDS Proxy, Active Directory users who log in with a UPN that differs from their account name, or who belong to an allowed group through a nested group, are now recognized instead of being rejected as unknown users.
20261030-17: Fix: in Artica, Creating and removing a swap file is now handled by the Artica daemon, and only an existing swap area can be removed.
20261030-17: Fix: in Artica, Moving the large system directories to another disk now shows its progress, only targets a mounted partition, and keeps a directory in place when its copy fails.
20261030-17: Fix: in Artica, Removing a monitored directory from the disk usage page can no longer delete any other file.
20261030-17: Add: in Artica Proxy, The bulk Categorize tab now fits on a single screen: drop or choose a file, pick the destination category and the add mode, then follow the import progress in place.
20261030-17: Fix: in Artica Proxy, The bulk category import now only accepts a file from the upload directory: a crafted file name could make the daemon load another file of the appliance into a category.
20261030-17: Add: in Artica Proxy, The Categorize tab has been redesigned: the website list comes first with a live domain counter, the category list can be filtered, and the add mode is now an explicit choice between checking for duplicates and adding without checking.
20261030-17: Add: in Artica, The AI assistant can read and manage the Winbind, Kibana, File System Monitor and CGuard services and the system RESTful API, with an administrator approval for every change.
20261030-17: Fix: in Artica, The obsolete Bugzilla, Munin, Intel Wi-Fi firmware, TCP multipath, SafeGuard and Fetchmail features have been removed from the console.
20261030-17: Fix: in Artica, The File System Monitor, Kibana, Winbind and system RESTful API services are now installed, started and monitored by the Artica daemon.
20261030-17: Fix: in Artica Proxy, Validating and removing the CGuard categories service is now handled by the Artica daemon and reports its errors.
20261030-17: Fix: in Artica, The scheduled tasks list now shows whether each task is really installed in cron.
20261030-17: Add: in Artica Proxy, The Test categories tab now lists every category found for a website by every source (categories service, flat files, personal categories, filtering service, remote service, Artica Cloud), and highlights the one the proxy actually uses.
20261030-17: Add: in Artica Proxy, The Test categories tab has been redesigned with a clear test bar, a result card, and collapsible engine details showing what each source answered.
20261030-17: Fix: in Artica Proxy, The Test categories tab no longer shows an uncategorized website in red like a blocked one, nor "Do not use" in place of "no answer".
20261030-17: Add: in Artica, The AI assistant can read the proxy switches, the HyperCache status and the proxy keytab entries, and, with approval, apply the reply-access, outgoing-mark and dynamic ACL rules or change fake NTLM, the MAC-to-user emergency mode, the disk cache, the RESTful API and the read-only configuration lock.
20261030-17: Fix: in Artica Proxy, The Browser extension tab of the categorization window no longer shows raw line-break tags and an untranslated label: the option now has a short title followed by its explanation.
20261030-17: Fix: in Artica Proxy, Applying HTTP reply access or outgoing mark rules now also defines the proxy objects they use and no longer writes an invalid mark, which could stop the proxy.
20261030-17: Fix: in Artica Proxy, Each dynamic ACL group file now contains only its own entries.
20261030-17: Fix: in Artica Proxy, The Google Safe Browsing events viewer displays the service events again.
20261030-17: Fix: in Artica Proxy, The DNS settings page no longer offers an "Install" load balancer button that actually uninstalled it.
20261030-17: Fix: in Artica Proxy, Importing a global blacklist no longer accepts an arbitrary file name and is applied to the proxy at the end of the import.
20261030-17: Fix: in Artica Proxy, Editing the Kerberos or parent proxies configuration files directly is refused with a clear message when the proxy configuration is locked read-only.
20261030-17: Fix: in Artica Proxy, Fake NTLM authentication, the proxy cache and RESTful API switches, read-only configuration, MAC-to-user emergency exit and HyperCache status are now handled by the Artica daemon.
20261030-17: Add: in Artica, A console zoom level can now be chosen in My account (70 % by default); it is kept in the browser and applied to every page, including the login screen.
20261030-17: Add: in Artica RDS Proxy, Tunnel agents are now managed from the console: enrollment with a one-time code that keeps the agent private key on the server, live status, revocation, automatic firewall opening and agent events sent to the SIEM.
20261030-17: Add: in Artica, The AI assistant can test the DNS filter, read the proxy build features and the legal logs status, and, with approval, connect or disconnect the legal logs server and rebuild member aliases.
20261030-17: Add: in Artica, The My account page has been redesigned: an identity card with the account type and remaining session time, the display preferences, and a clear read-only view of the rights and groups granted to the account.
20261030-17: Fix: in Artica, On the My account page, the Display certificate button no longer regenerates the Manager client certificate, and creating a new one now asks for confirmation.
20261030-17: Fix: in Artica, Saving the display preferences of the My account page now closes the dialog and refreshes the page.
20261030-17: Fix: in Artica Proxy, The "Verify rules" test of the DNS filter returns its verdict again.
20261030-17: Fix: in Artica Proxy, The proxy status widgets no longer fail on PHP 8 when computing the number of connected members.
20261030-17: Fix: in Artica Proxy, Connecting to and disconnecting from a legal logs server, renaming members from their MAC address, and the proxy, cache, ZipProxy and cluster log viewers are now handled by the Artica daemon.
20261030-17: Add: in Artica, The Artica backup settings tab has been redesigned: schedule, remote storage and encryption tiles with clear warnings, a local snapshots card, and a separate data retention section that explains the Corporate license limits.
20261030-17: Fix: in Artica, Saving the snapshot schedule now refreshes the backup settings immediately.
20261030-17: Fix: in Artica, The Debian agent no longer replays the whole system boot sequence every 6 hours on sysvinit appliances, which briefly took the network down and sent a "rebooted network" notification.
20261030-17: Add: in Artica, The Status tab of the CIS Benchmark page has been redesigned: a compliance gauge with a plain-language verdict, one-click access to the latest report, and clear tiles for the daily audit, the audit scripts and the running audit.
20261030-17: Fix: in Artica, Enabling or disabling the daily CIS Benchmark audit now confirms the change and reports any error instead of doing nothing visible.
20261030-17: Fix: in Artica, The syslog TLS buttons work again: enabling and disabling TLS reception, creating an encrypted client package and importing it on the client appliance.
20261030-17: Fix: in Artica, The Artica daemon no longer crashes when syslog TLS certificates are configured, and appliances that only send their logs now use their TLS certificates.
20261030-17: Fix: in Artica, Saving the log sink backup settings updates the backup schedule again, and the backup itself is now run by the Artica daemon.
20261030-17: Fix: in Artica VPN Client, The status now shows why a connection is not established (server reset, authentication refused, TLS failure, unknown server name…) even while the client keeps retrying.
20261030-17: Add: in Artica, The settings tab of the System health monitor page has been redesigned: status tiles for the watchdog, incidents and monitoring coverage, then one card per family of thresholds with clear explanations and edit buttons.
20261030-17: Fix: in Artica, The Realtime Daemons monitor card of the System health monitor page now shows the real state of the service instead of an empty status.
20261030-17: Fix: in Artica, The 5-minute system load alert now passes its threshold value correctly to the alert script.
20261030-17: Fix: in Artica Proxy, The scheduled "Proxy status" task now refreshes the proxy status through the Artica daemon instead of an obsolete script that did nothing.
20261030-17: Fix: in Artica VPN Client, Reinstalling the same connection now restarts its service so its status is reported correctly again.
20261030-17: Fix: in Artica, A server migration no longer copies the old server's settings storage choice (Memcached) and Debian version, which could leave the new server unable to read its settings after the reboot.
20261030-17: Fix: in Artica, The Artica Memcached service no longer fails to start when the maximum item size is larger than half of its memory, and its startup error is now logged.
20261030-17: Fix: in Artica, Restarting the Artica Memcached service now starts it again instead of leaving it stopped.
20261030-17: Fix: in Artica RDS Proxy, An RDP session through a policy that does not record sessions no longer fails when another unrecorded session was opened a few minutes before.
20261030-17: Fix: in Artica RDS Proxy, An RDP or VNC target can now be saved without a username and password. Users then type the target credentials on the Windows logon screen inside the session.
20261030-17: Fix: in Artica, The memory Processes tab no longer fails with the error relation ps_mem does not exist.
20261030-17: Add: in Artica, Memory used by each program is now recorded every 5 minutes and kept for 7 days, with a ranking per period (last hour, today, yesterday, 24 hours, 7 days) and a curve per program.
20261030-17: Fix: in Artica, The Disks page no longer keeps refreshing in the background after you leave it, which could raise script errors on the next pages of the console.
20261030-17: Fix: in Artica, The Legal logs events page now shows the searched term in its title instead of a fragment of internal search pattern, and the obsolete search engine behind it has been removed.
20261030-17: Fix: in Artica, Hidden links of about 150 console pages that pointed to removed functions no longer end in a server error.
20261030-17: Fix: in Artica RDS Proxy, The SSH, video, second factor and event labels added recently are now translated in every console language instead of showing their internal name.
20261030-17: Fix: in Artica, A network service that Artica disables on purpose no longer stays listed as failed by systemd until the next reboot.
20261030-17: Add: in Artica, The System users page now explains SSH, file sharing and sudo, shows group and SSH counters, and hides protected system groups by default with a one-click switch to show them.
20261030-17: Add: in Artica RDS Proxy, An RDP or VNC target can now be reached through an agent installed on the server, which connects out to the bastion so the server needs no inbound port.
20261030-17: Fix: in Artica, The Docker Manager update event now shows the previous version, or reports a first installation, instead of an empty "from v".
20261029-17: Add: in Artica RDS Proxy, When the RDS Proxy is enabled, the home dashboard shows its card instead of the DNS resolver one, with the service state, the active sessions, the active and recorded policies, the listening port and the number of video recordings.
20261029-17: Add: in Artica RDS Proxy, The Template tab now shows a preview of the login screen and of the target list built from the configured colors, flags color pairs with a low contrast and displays the welcome text, the charter and the error messages in full.
20261029-17: Add: in Artica RDS Proxy, The video recording tab now explains how sessions are recorded, converted and purged, shows the units of the quality settings and warns that applying a change restarts the service.
20261029-17: Add: in Artica RDS Proxy, The service settings of the status tab are grouped into four cards (network listening, encryption, bastion and detection, session behaviour) with full values and a "Reduced security" warning on the options that lower the protection.
20261029-17: Add: in Artica RDS Proxy, The customization of the error messages shown to remote users now sits in the Template tab, next to the login screen texts.
20261029-17: Fix: in Artica, Error messages, logs and notifications produced by the Artica service are now written in English.
20261029-17: Fix: in Artica, At the end of a server migration, the restart of the new server is retried and forced if it does not happen within two minutes, even if the Artica service was restarted in the meantime.
20261029-17: Fix: in Artica, A server migration no longer fails at 15% when the source server holds a symbolic link pointing outside its data folder: the link is skipped and the migration goes on.
20261029-17: Fix: in Artica, Server migration error messages are now displayed in English.
20261029-17: Fix: in Artica, Saving a failover secondary node opened from the failover services list no longer shows "div layer primary_node_save not found", and the list is refreshed after the change.
20261029-17: Add: in Artica, The Artica AI assistant can now check whether a failover secondary node uses network card names that do not exist on the server, and adapt them after an administrator approves it.
20261029-17: Fix: in Artica, A failover secondary node now adapts the network card names sent by its primary node to its own cards, so the failover service keeps running when the two nodes use different card names (for example eth0 and ens192).
20261029-17: Fix: in Artica, After migrating a failover secondary node whose network cards were renamed, the migration now tells the administrator which card to set as "Rewrite interface" on the primary node.
20261029-17: Fix: in Artica Proxy, On a categories server, the "Compile" button of a personal category now also rebuilds the web-filtering database sent to the proxies, so websites added to the category reach the proxies.
20261029-17: Fix: in Artica Proxy, A categories server no longer drops unchanged categories from the list it publishes, so proxies always see every category and download the updated ones.
20261029-17: Add: in Artica, The Artica AI assistant can now tell whether the Synology Active Backup agent may compile its own snapshot driver, and switch that option on or off after an administrator approves it.
20261029-17: Add: in Artica, A new Synology Active Backup option controls whether the agent may compile its own snapshot driver; it is off by default, because that driver crashes on Artica and blocks every backup at 0%.
20261029-17: Fix: in Artica, The Disconnect button of the Synology Active Backup page now closes the session with the NAS instead of reconnecting it.
20261029-17: Fix: in Artica, Synology Active Backup no longer stays stuck at 0% when the agent compiled its own snapshot driver on the appliance: the driver shipped by Artica is now always the one loaded, including at boot.
20261029-17: Fix: in Artica, The four summary tiles of the Docker containers page are now shown on a single line.
20261029-17: Fix: in Artica Proxy, Searching a URLs database object can no longer run system commands through a crafted search.
20261029-17: Fix: in Artica Proxy, Removing a site or a URL from the proxy cache can no longer run system commands through a crafted name.
20261029-17: Fix: in Artica Proxy, Removing a URL from the proxy cache now also removes it when the object was cached over HTTPS.
20261029-17: Fix: in Artica Proxy, The watchdog button of the proxy status page now applies the watchdog settings.
20261029-17: Fix: in Artica, Saving the colors or the logo of the RDS bastion no longer restarts the gateway, so the open sessions are no longer cut; the new look applies from the next connection.
20261029-17: Fix: in Artica, The RDS Proxy console now previews the logo on the background color of the gateway, so a light logo is no longer invisible.
20261029-17: Fix: in Artica, The session limit of the RDS bastion Community edition now follows the real license state: licensed appliances are no longer capped, and Community appliances are limited as intended.
20261029-17: Fix: in Artica, Without an Artica license, the RDS bastion now accepts 3 simultaneous sessions instead of 5.
20261029-17: Add: in Artica, Customizing the look of the RDS bastion (colors, background, logo, welcome text) now requires an Artica license; without it the gateway keeps the default Artica look, and the usage charter stays available.
20261029-17: Fix: in Artica Proxy, Saving the proxy watchdog settings now applies the URL checking and the network analysis options.
20261029-17: Fix: in Artica Proxy, The option that reconfigures the proxy services after a reboot works again.
20261029-17: Add: in Artica, The RDS bastion login screen can show a welcome text to every user before sign-in, and now uses the gateway's standard login page with the Artica logo instead of the bare "Target information required" dialog.
20261029-17: Add: in Artica, The screens of the RDS bastion now use the Artica green background (#005447) by default, and the background color chosen in the console applies even when the custom template is off.
20261029-17: Fix: in Artica Proxy, The Empty DNS cache button of the proxy dashboard now really empties the DNS cache before restarting the proxy.
20261029-17: Fix: in Artica, The DNS watchdog no longer restarts the DNS cache in a loop when the cache refuses queries from the appliance itself.
20261029-17: Fix: in Artica, Sending DNS cache events to a Statistics Appliance now survives the periodic rebuild of the system log configuration.
20261029-17: Fix: in Artica, Allowing a domain from the DNS events now reloads the DNS cache service instead of failing silently.
20261029-17: Fix: in Artica, The DNS cache settings no longer show a DNS blacklists option that had no effect.
20261029-17: Fix: in Artica, A snapshot schedule inherited from an older version now keeps the time chosen by the administrator instead of falling back to the default schedule.
20261029-17: Fix: in Artica, Migrating a failover (keepalived) node to a new server now installs and prepares the failover service, so it starts after the final reboot.
20261029-17: Fix: in Artica, The Web Application Firewall deployment wizard now completes instead of stopping at 70%, and also installs the proxy.pac service.
20261029-17: Fix: in Artica, The IPsec deployment wizard no longer fails on an appliance where strongSwan has never been configured.
20261029-17: Fix: in Artica, The simple proxy and the cache deployment wizards now reach the end of their progress bar and remove the services they announce.
20261029-17: Fix: in Artica, The deployment wizards can now only be run by a system administrator.
20261029-17: Fix: in Artica, The web filtering error page wizard now publishes the page with TLS 1.2 and TLS 1.3 only.
20261029-17: Fix: in Artica, Restoring a snapshot from the installation wizard no longer corrupts the administrators and proxy databases.
20261029-17: Fix: in Artica, A snapshot restore now replaces a corrupted database instead of stopping, and restores the remaining databases.
20261029-17: Add: in Artica, The RDS bastion can show a usage charter that every user must accept after signing in, before choosing a target; declining closes the session and each answer is recorded in the access events.
20261029-17: Fix: in Artica, A logo uploaded for the RDS Proxy login screen is now checked, resized and re-encoded, so an oversized image can no longer exhaust the memory of the bastion.
20261029-17: Fix: in Artica, The disk quota tabs of a Docker container no longer fail with an internal server error.
20261029-17: Fix: in Artica, The packages update list now offers new versions of the RDP proxy even when the service is installed but disabled.
20261029-17: Add: in Artica, The SSH targets of the RDS bastion now show their messages, status bar and file explorer in English or French, following the language of the session, while the transfer and command logs stay in English.
20261029-17: Fix: in Artica, Pasting files from a Windows Remote Desktop client (mstsc) into an SSH target of the RDS bastion no longer fails with "the workstation did not send the file".
20261028-17: Fix: in Artica, The RDS Proxy console now mentions SSH targets in the page descriptions and in the policy evaluation steps.
20261028-17: Fix: in Artica, The RDS Proxy target form no longer shows an empty unlabeled field under the user name when the protocol is SSH.
20261028-17: Fix: in Artica, The RDS Proxy SSH session trace now shows small sizes in bytes instead of 0 KB, and no longer rounds file sizes down.
20261028-17: Fix: in Artica, The RDS Proxy console no longer shows internal label names instead of text on the SSH target, policy, pattern and second factor screens: 97 English and French labels lost by an earlier language file update are back.
20261028-17: Add: in Artica, The RDS Proxy can transfer files with SSH targets when the policy allows clipboard files: paste files in the terminal to drop them into the account's home directory (an existing file is never overwritten), press Ctrl+Alt+F to browse the target and copy files or folders to the Windows clipboard, and press Ctrl+Alt+X to cancel a drop in progress. Each file is fingerprinted with SHA-256 and logged in the session recording and in the access events. When the policy has command patterns that refuse or kill, a file or folder whose name starts with a dot is refused at the top of the home directory. Requires ReDemPtion Artica 12.3.19 and the authentication hook 1.6.1.
20261028-17: Add: in Artica, The RDS Proxy recordings page has a Files view listing each file uploaded to or retrieved from an SSH target (direction, path, size, SHA-256 fingerprint and outcome), the access log shows these transfers, and the policy page tells whether the RDS proxy engine applies the clipboard file rights to SSH targets.
20261028-17: Add: in Artica, The firewall general settings now appear as a protection board with one tile per protection, showing at a glance which ones are active.
20261028-17: Fix: in Artica, The web console PHP service is now refreshed when Debian updates PHP, so the console no longer stays stuck on "loading its PHP components" after a PHP security update.
20261028-17: Add: in Artica, The packages update list now also offers new versions of the Keepalived failover service.
20261028-17: Fix: in Artica, The web console no longer restarts its PHP service every minute when the PHP curl extension is missing; the cause is now reported instead.
20261028-17: Fix: in Artica, Updating the Failover service (keepalived) now installs the system libraries it needs before downloading the package, so the new version no longer fails to start on appliances where they are missing.
20261028-17: Fix: in Artica, The waiting message and percentage shown on the login page while the API service starts are now displayed in white so they remain readable on the dark background.
20261028-17: Add: in Artica, keepalived (Failover) is now built for Debian 10, 12 and 13 from the official 2.x releases, automatically for Debian 12 and 13, with SNMP, D-Bus, JSON, BFD and content checks (regex) in HTTP health checks.
20261028-17: Fix: in Artica, On Debian 10 appliances, the firewall rebuild is no longer refused with "Bad argument FIN,SYN,RST,ACK" when old rules have to be removed, which left the previous firewall rules in place.
20261028-17: Fix: in Artica, The server migration window of the console now shows which network card of the new server replaces each card of the old one; it was only shown in the installation wizard.
20261028-17: Fix: in Artica, A migration from a server without the latest hotfix now moves every network card of its configuration to the new server, not only the card carrying its address, so the default gateway is no longer lost.
20261028-17: Fix: in Artica, The Failover service no longer stays stopped after a migration to a server whose network cards have other names; the floating IP label now follows the renamed card.
20261028-17: Fix: in Artica, On Debian 10 consoles still running the former dedicated PHP 7.4, the Fix PHP2Shell button now switches to the official, patched PHP 7.3 (CVE-2026-109618, CVE-2026-109619), and puts PHP 7.4 back if the console does not answer afterwards.
20261028-17: Fix: in Artica, The System information page no longer offers the obsolete upgrade to PHP 7.4, which no longer worked.
20261028-17: Fix: in Artica, The Synology Active Backup agent is now started and stopped only through its own systemd service, so a second copy can no longer remove its control socket and make the console show version 0.0.0.
20261028-17: Fix: in Artica Proxy, The daily and weekly PDF statistics reports are generated and sent again instead of stopping on a chart error.
20261028-17: Fix: in Artica Proxy, The blocked sites statistics now count only web filtering blocks and 403 answers, instead of counting redirects, cached answers and errors as blocked requests.
20261028-17: Fix: in Artica Proxy, The nightly categorization of unknown websites now records the category found instead of treating every successful lookup as a failure, and no longer floods the system log.
20261028-17: Fix: in Artica, A disabled proxy.pac service no longer leaves a monitoring rule that tried to restart it every minute.
20261028-17: Fix: in Artica, The swap cleaning event now reports the swap size in the right unit.
20261028-17: Add: in Artica, Older PHP versions left behind by a system upgrade (such as PHP 8.2 next to PHP 8.4) are now removed automatically once nothing uses them anymore, so security scanners no longer report them.
20261028-17: Fix: in Artica, The "Download client certificate" button of the server migration page no longer answers with a 404 error.
20261028-17: Fix: in Artica, The server migration service now listens only on the address it publishes instead of every interface, and by default publishes the web console interface rather than the interface of the default route.
20261028-17: Add: in Artica, The server migration page lets you choose the network interface on which the source server waits for the destination appliance.
20261028-17: Add: in Artica, The AI assistant can now read the state of the server migration service (listening address, chosen and active interface, available interfaces) and change its listening interface with your approval.
20261028-17: Fix: in Artica, Importing the server migration certificate on the new server no longer fails with "no such file or directory" when the uploaded file was renamed because an earlier copy was already there, for example to "client (4).gz".
20261028-17: Fix: in Artica, Migrating to a server whose network cards have other names (for example eth0 on Debian 12 and ens192 on Debian 13) now takes over the address of the source server instead of stopping at the end: the wizard asks which card of the new server replaces each card of the source, and the whole imported configuration follows.
20261028-17: Add: in Artica, The network interfaces page now lists the interfaces that the configuration still cites but that the server no longer has, and either moves their whole configuration to a card of the server that has none yet, or removes them together with their routes, routing rules, NAT, firewall and DHCP entries.
20261028-17: Fix: in Artica, On the network interfaces page, a card named with the Debian 13 scheme (such as ens192) can now be opened and configured before it is registered.
20261028-17: Add: in Artica, The AI assistant can now list the ghost network interfaces and, with your approval, move the configuration of one of them to a present card or remove it.
20261028-17: Fix: in Artica, On the firewall interfaces page, a click anywhere on an interface card now opens its settings, not only a click on its name.
20261028-17: Fix: in Artica, Installing the IPv6 gateway (NAT64/SIIT) no longer fails on Debian 13 with "jool.ko: file does not exist", the compressed kernel modules built by DKMS are now recognized.
20261028-17: Fix: in Artica, Starting the IPv6 gateway while it is disabled, or installing it while IPv6 is disabled, is now refused at once with the reason instead of reporting a success, and a start or stop waits for a running check instead of failing.
20261028-17: Add: in Artica Reverse Proxy, The web services page now warns when nginx still publishes sites that were deleted or disabled, and offers a button that removes their configuration and reloads nginx.
20261028-17: Fix: in Artica Reverse Proxy, The automatic cleanup of deleted sites now also removes the configuration of deleted TCP/UDP stream services, which kept their listening port open.
20261028-17: Add: in Artica, The AI assistant can now read the NAT64/SIIT gateway (state, instances, translation sessions) and propose, with approval, adding, changing or removing instances, pool4 and EAM entries, and starting, stopping, installing or uninstalling the gateway, each change verified and undoable.
20261028-17: Fix: in Artica, The bonding option of the network interfaces page now shows its explanation text in every language.
20261028-17: Fix: in Artica, The ISP prefix label of the IPv6 interface page is now translated in every language, and a correction to that label now applies to every page that shows it.
20261028-17: Fix: in Artica Reverse Proxy, The "Listen address and port" tab of a TCP/UDP stream service no longer fails with a blank panel, so its listening ports can be listed and added again.
20261028-17: Fix: in Artica, A web console panel that fails to load now shows the error instead of retrying endlessly, which sent tens of thousands of requests per hour to the appliance.
20261028-17: Fix: in Artica KSC Installer, After restoring the certificate of an old server, signing in no longer fails with "Administration Server uses an untrusted certificate".
20261028-17: Fix: in Artica, Stopping the IPv6 gateway (NAT64/SIIT) from the console now holds, the watchdog no longer restarts it three minutes later.
20261028-17: Fix: in Artica, The IPv6 gateway watchdog now repairs a lost or extra IPv4 pool or address mapping, not only a changed IPv6 prefix, and a temporary read error no longer recreates a live translator and cuts its sessions.
20261028-17: Fix: in Artica, One IPv6 gateway instance refused by the kernel no longer keeps the other instances down, and invalid IPv6 prefixes, overlapping IPv4 pools and overlapping address mappings are refused when they are saved.
20261028-17: Fix: in Artica, The IPv6 gateway pages are now reserved to system administrators, refresh the IPv4 pool and mapping lists after a change, can enable or disable an instance, and propose the safe 61001-65535 port range for a new IPv4 pool.
20261028-17: Add: in Artica, The Docker status page has been redesigned as a dashboard showing the service and engine health, container and image counts, host capacity, storage, runtime, image sources and engine versions at a glance.
20261027-17: Add: in Artica, The network interfaces status page now shows each interface, VLAN, bond, kernel-only interface and Samba instance as a card with its gateway, MAC address, options and traffic, and can be filtered by name, IP or tag.
20261027-17: Fix: in Artica, On a virtual machine, the console of a newly installed Artica system and of its rescue system is no longer flooded with "systemd-ssh-generator: Failed to query local AF_VSOCK CID" messages.
20261027-17: Add: in Artica, The IPv6 widget of the network interfaces page now enables or disables IPv6 in one click and applies it at once to the kernel, the network interfaces and the services that use it, with a progress bar. Disabling is refused while NAT64 is enabled. The IPv6 option of the kernel network settings applies the same way.
20261027-17: Fix: in Artica Proxy, Upgrading the reverse-proxy engine from the Artica repository no longer overwrites the appliance's nginx configuration with the files shipped inside the package, which stopped nginx with an unknown "geoip2_data_country_code" variable error.
20261027-17: Fix: in Artica Proxy, The reverse-proxy service now repairs its GeoIP country definition before each start, so nginx starts even when that file was damaged or emptied.
20261027-17: Fix: in Artica Proxy, After an nginx upgrade, the reverse-proxy service detects the modules of the new nginx binary immediately instead of reusing those of the previous one.
20261027-17: Fix: in Artica Proxy, Building the WAF rules no longer logs an error for each published site that has no host name.
20261026-17: Fix: in Artica, The SSH terminal of the RDS bastion no longer leaves stray marks and dark lines on screen when used from the Windows Remote Desktop client.
20261026-17: Add: in Artica, Each action button of the certificates center now shows a tooltip explaining what it does (view, PFX, PEM download, export, renewal, deletion).
20261026-17: Add: in Artica, The Artica AI assistant can read the Web console session debug log and turn it on or off with your approval, to diagnose a login that keeps returning to the login screen.
20261026-17: Add: in Artica, The Web interface menu of the system console can turn the session debug log on or off and display its last lines, to diagnose a login that keeps returning to the login screen.
20261026-17: Add: in Artica, The RDS Proxy sessions page shows the protocol of each session (RDP, VNC or SSH), lists SSH sessions, and tells that a disconnected session ends within 30 seconds.
20261026-17: Add: in Artica, The RDS Proxy recordings page marks recordings holding an SSH trace and lets you read the commands typed and the terminal transcript as plain text, page by page, or download the transcript file; synchronization stays available for SSH transcripts when video support is missing.
20261026-17: Add: in Artica, The RDS Proxy status page now explains why SSH targets are unavailable: missing SSH module in the engine, or an authentication hook that is too old, with its running version.
20261026-17: Add: in Artica, The RDS Proxy target list shows a short SSH host key fingerprint, and the access log links a connection refused for a changed host key to the target, where the recorded key can be checked and forgotten.
20261026-17: Fix: in Artica, Reading, downloading or deleting RDS Proxy session recordings and disconnecting a session now require the proxy administrator privilege.
20261026-17: Add: in Artica, The RDS Proxy second factor messages (code prompt, enrollment, invalid code, locked account, unavailable) can now be customized from the console.
20261026-17: Fix: in Artica, The RDS Proxy policy and pattern pages no longer show the recording and window-title OCR warnings for SSH command patterns, and state that SSH sessions are always recorded and which session rights apply to SSH targets.
20261026-17: Add: in Artica, The RDS Proxy SIEM page states that SSH session commands and transcripts are not sent to the SIEM yet.
20261025-17: Add: in Artica, The RDS Proxy console can now register SSH targets, with the password typed at connection time or kept in an encrypted vault as a password, a private key or the bastion key. Opening SSH sessions through the bastion requires the next RDS Proxy engine update.
20261025-17: Add: in Artica, The RDS Proxy console can create the bastion SSH key, show its fingerprint, regenerate it, and deploy it in one click on a Linux server or an Artica appliance; the password typed for the deployment is never kept.
20261025-17: Add: in Artica, The RDS Proxy console stores the host key fingerprint of each SSH target, with a button to forget it, and lets you prepare session patterns for SSH commands, which will apply once the next RDS Proxy engine update is installed.
20261026-17: Add: in Artica, The RDS Proxy opens SSH sessions to Linux servers and Artica appliances from any RDP client, with the same access rules as other targets, a check of the server host key, typed or vault authentication, and text copy and paste allowed by the policy (requires ReDemPtion 12.3.18 and the authentication hook 1.6.0).
20261026-17: Add: in Artica, RDS Proxy session patterns can now apply to SSH commands: a matching command is refused before it runs, reported, or ends the session, and every SSH session keeps a command log and a terminal transcript next to its recording.
20261026-17: Fix: in Artica, Disconnecting an RDS Proxy session from the console now really ends a session that is already open, within 30 seconds.
20261026-17: Fix: in Artica, The RDS Proxy Community Edition limit now stops at five simultaneous sessions instead of six.
20261026-17: Fix: in Artica, The RDS Proxy access log no longer records a normal end of session as a disconnection by the administrator.
20261026-17: Add: in Artica AI, New read-only skills report the RDS Proxy state, the open sessions, the recordings and the SSH commands of a recording, with passwords masked.
20261026-17: Fix: in Artica KSC Installer, The Web Console now reaches the authentication service by the name in its certificate, which fixes the "Authentication service unavailable" login error when Kaspersky Security Center was installed with a host name.
20261026-17: Add: in Artica KSC Installer, The installer detects a Web Console left on a previous IP address or server certificate, explains why login fails and offers to configure it again.
20261026-17: Add: in Artica KSC Installer, The Certificate menu can now restore the server certificate of an old server from its klbackup folder, after saving the current one, and then reconfigures the Web Console.
20261026-17: Add: in Artica KSC Installer, A new --health option prints the health check without changing anything.
20261026-17: Fix: in Artica KSC Installer, The database checks no longer fail when the installer is started with su without a login shell.
20261026-17: Add: in Artica, The AI assistant can now read the snapshot backup schedule, detect when its cron file is missing or stale, and rewrite it after approval.
20261026-17: Add: in Artica, The AI assistant can now destroy the Kerberos tickets of the appliance after approval, without touching the Active Directory machine account.
20261026-17: Fix: in Artica, Web console pages no longer receive empty system information when the appliance runs PHP 8.0 or 8.1.
20261026-17: Fix: in Artica, Revalidating the license API key from the license page now actually contacts the licensing server instead of silently doing nothing.
20261026-17: Fix: in Artica, The "Destroy Kerberos tickets" action of the Active Directory page now really destroys the tickets and reports an error when it fails.
20261026-17: Fix: in Artica, When the Web console loses its connection to the system framework, the automatic service restart now runs, at most once per minute.
20261026-17: Fix: in Artica, Saving a kernel parameter through the generic field editor now requires system administrator rights and never runs a command supplied by the browser.
20261026-17: Fix: in Artica, The scheduled snapshot backup is now applied when saved from the console and repaired automatically on appliances where it was saved but never ran.
20261026-17: Add: in Artica, The AI assistant can list the trusted relays declared in "Follow source addresses" and, with your approval, add or remove one; it refuses a source wider than a /8 network.
20261026-17: Fix: in Artica Proxy, A trusted relay entered as an IP range in "Follow source addresses" is now taken into account; it was silently ignored.
20261026-17: Fix: in Artica Proxy, Adding, enabling or deleting a trusted relay in "Follow source addresses" now reloads the proxy instead of restarting it, so connections in progress are no longer cut.
20261026-17: Fix: in Artica Proxy, The global settings page shows the trusted relays whatever the outgoing X-Forwarded-For mode; they were hidden unless that mode was "Enabled".
20261026-17: Add: in Artica, The AI assistant can read the ClamAV signature exclusions and signature databases, and, with your approval, add, switch on or off, or remove a signature exclusion, each change being checked on the antivirus and reversible.
20261026-17: Fix: in Artica, A ClamAV signature exclusion containing a line break is refused, so it can no longer slip a second ignored signature into the antivirus.
20261026-17: Fix: in Artica, The dialog that adds a ClamAV signature exclusion now explains what to paste and that the .UNOFFICIAL suffix is handled, instead of showing a truncated title.
20261026-17: Add: in Artica, The ClamAV signature exclusions page shows how many exclusions are active, which ones come from third-party databases and who changed the list last, with filters, a search field and advice on choosing between excluding a signature and excluding a site.
20261026-17: Fix: in Artica, The ClamAV signature exclusions page shows its buttons in the page header and refreshes the list after an exclusion is edited.
20261026-17: Add: in Artica, The ClamAV signature databases view now shows the total number of signatures, the freshness of the databases with a clear warning when they are out of date, and lets you enable third-party databases in one click.
20261026-17: Add: in Artica, The AI assistant can now read and switch the option that takes the proxy user name from the X-Authenticated-User header of the declared relays, with a check and an automatic undo.
20261026-17: Add: in Artica Proxy, The proxy can take the user name from the X-Authenticated-User header sent by the relays declared in "Follow source addresses" (a VirtualBrowser cluster, for example), so requests, logs and statistics show the real user; the header is ignored from any other address.
20261026-17: Fix: in Artica, The notification bell no longer shows false alerts, such as "End of support for your OS" on Debian 13, while the Artica REST service is stopped or the system version is unknown.
20261026-17: Fix: in Artica Proxy, Applying a change to the antivirus exclusions now reloads the proxy instead of restarting it, so downloads in progress are no longer interrupted.
20261026-17: Fix: in Artica Proxy, Disabling the antivirus exclusions list now really sends all traffic to the antivirus again.
20261026-17: Fix: in Artica Proxy, The forms of the antivirus, global and SSL whitelists show the help for the selected entry type again, with the exact syntax of domain patterns.
20261026-17: Add: in Artica, The routing page has a new Gateway groups tab to create groups of gateways ranked by tier, see the live state, latency and loss of each gateway, and their quality over the last 24 hours.
20261026-17: Add: in Artica, The routing page shows a banner while a routing change is under watch, and a new Watch tab lists the automatic rollbacks and sets the watch duration.
20261026-17: Add: in Artica, The Internet access load balancer page shows the links of its gateway group once migrated, and offers to go back to the former balancer or resume the group.
20261026-17: Fix: in Artica, Reading the last lines of a service log from the console no longer leaves a temporary file behind on each request.
20261026-17: Add: in Artica Proxy, The integrated antivirus settings now show the threats blocked in the last 24 hours, the affected devices and the active exclusions at a glance, with a clear warning when the proxy runs without antivirus protection.
20261026-17: Fix: in Artica Proxy, An antivirus exclusion added from the console is now created enabled, and its window closes after saving.
20261026-17: Add: in Artica Proxy, The antivirus exclusions page shows counters of active exclusions, trusted domains and exempted networks, the global state of the list, filters by type and a guided screen when the list is empty.
20261026-17: Fix: in Artica Proxy, The antivirus exclusions list again offers the button to turn the whole list on or off.
20261026-17: Add: in Artica, The multi-WAN link balancer now takes its links, weights, health and backup links from the "wan" gateway group, migrated automatically from the existing links, with a way back to the previous behavior.
20261025-17: Add: in Artica, The Load-Balancer objects page has a new layout with indicator tiles (orphan objects included), a type filter, a preview of each object values, its rules and a button to create an object.
20261025-17: Fix: in Artica, Saving the items of a Load-Balancer ACL object no longer stores the whole list as a single URL-encoded item.
20261025-17: Fix: in Artica, The Load-Balancer service is started, reloaded and rotated through the lightweight Artica launcher, and is no longer restarted every few minutes while no balancing service is defined.
20261025-17: Add: in Artica, The Load-Balancer access rules page shows each rule as a card with its evaluation order and the sentence it reads as, and the rule editor chooses the action from cards with a live preview of the rule.
20261025-17: Fix: in Artica, The Load-Balancer objects page and the backend servers tab of a service work again with the new table layout, and their changes go through the Artica service.
20261025-17: Fix: in Artica, The Load-Balancer services page works again with a new layout (indicator tiles, publication templates, type filter), and creating, editing, duplicating, enabling and deleting a service go through the Artica service.
20261025-17: Fix: in Artica, The Load-Balancer access rules page no longer fails with an internal server error, and its rules, objects and items are now edited through the Artica service.
20261025-17: Add: in Artica, The Load-Balancer status page has a new layout with large service buttons, the result of the last operation and a description of each global parameter.
20261025-17: Add: in Artica, The Load-Balancer servers status page groups each server under its service, with indicator tiles (active services, servers online, servers in error, total requests), the health check result of each server and a pause or resume button.
20261025-17: Add: in Artica, After a change to the routing, the routing engine watches the gateways that answered before for a few minutes: if one stops answering, it puts the last valid configuration back on its own and tells why, and if the gateway stays silent anyway it restores the change, since the cause is elsewhere.
20261025-17: Fix: in Artica, A routing rule added without a priority now takes a free priority of the range instead of being refused when the highest one is already used.
20261025-17: Add: in Artica, The Load-Balancer status page shows its global parameters as a summary card, edited in a dialog.
20261025-17: Fix: in Artica, The Load-Balancer realtime requests page decodes the log lines the Load-Balancer actually writes, and shows the client, the site, the status, the backend server, the size and the latency of each request.
20261025-17: Fix: in Artica, The Load-Balancer status page shows the service state again, and its start, stop, restart and reload buttons, the server pause and resume actions and the log search work again.
20261025-17: Add: in Artica, The NAT tab of the routing engine shows counters, filters, the packets, bytes and connections translated by each rule, whether each enabled rule is really in the kernel, and the rules found in its kernel chain that the engine does not manage.
20261025-17: Add: in Artica, The window of a routing NAT rule only shows the translation address for SNAT and displays a summary of the rule.
20261025-17: Fix: in Artica, Installing the Load-Balancer feature no longer fails with "haproxy.cfg no such file" when no balancing service is defined yet.
20261025-17: Add: in Artica, The Routing rules tab shows the kernel evaluation order, counters, filters, the criteria and the decision of each rule, an on/off switch and arrows to change the order.
20261025-17: Add: in Artica, A routing rule can now select traffic by protocol and ports, with ready-made templates for Teams, Zoom, SIP and RTP, and send it to a gateway group; its window shows a summary of the rule.
20261025-17: Add: in Artica, The Routes tab of the routing engine shows counters, filters and how each route is forwarded (gateway, next hops, gateway group, direct link or blackhole), with an on/off switch per route.
20261025-17: Add: in Artica, A route of the routing engine can now be sent through a gateway group from the console, and its window only shows the fields of the chosen forwarding mode.
20261025-17: Add: in Artica, The Routing tables tab shows counters (tables, main table, custom tables, IP families, unused tables), filters, a hint when only the main table exists, and links that open the routes or the rules of a table.
20261025-17: Add: in Artica, The Routing rules tab can be filtered by routing table from its header.
20261025-17: Add: in Artica, Policy rules of the routing engine can now select traffic by protocol and ports (for example UDP 3478-3481 for Teams), so video calls and VoIP can be sent through a chosen link or gateway group, and the path tester simulates such a flow.
20261025-17: Fix: in Artica, A gateway group member added without weight, probe or tier now gets 1, ping and tier 1 instead of being refused.
20261025-17: Fix: in Artica Proxy, When the monitoring service restarts the web-filtering server, after a crash or for excessive memory use, it now comes back under its own system unit.
20261025-17: Fix: in Artica, The routing page no longer shows a separate banner saying that its configuration belongs to this appliance only: the sentence now ends the page description, leaving more room for the content.
20261025-17: Fix: in Artica Proxy, When the monitoring service restarts the web-filtering file watcher, it now comes back under its own system unit.
20261025-17: Add: in Artica, The Migration tab of the routing engine has a new layout: a status banner telling what to do next, the migration cycle step by step, the engine, dates and path equivalence cards, six counters, and report tables filtered by result that now also list the kernel routes the engine takes over.
20261025-17: Add: in Artica, The Path test tab of the routing engine has a new layout: the verdict first, with the gateway group used, then the decision path step by step with the blocking step in red, a session history to run a test again, and a button to copy the diagnostic.
