20261025-17: Add: in Artica, The Measures tab of the routing engine has a new layout: tracked connections with their table usage, forwarded packets, cumulated volume and gateway states at a glance, NAT rules with the share of connections of each one, the interface traffic, and one card per gateway with its latency, loss and 24-hour history.
20261025-17: Add: in Artica, The Kernel state tab of the routing engine has a new layout: kernel figures at a glance, the last apply and the differences with the model side by side, rules, routes per table, NAT chains with their iptables lines, and the reverse path filter of each interface.
20261025-17: Add: in Artica, The Forwarding tab of the routing engine has a new layout: forwarded packets and tracked connections, one card per IP family showing whether the kernel follows the saved choice, the reverse path filter as four choices, and the filter the kernel applies on each interface.
20261025-17: Fix: in Artica, The Network traffic page is now fully translated, and on a server with less than 2500 MB of memory it explains why its statistics are turned off instead of showing empty tabs.
20261025-17: Fix: in Artica, A server with less than 2500 MB of memory no longer runs the display-only statistics (network traffic, disk I/O, proxy Kerberos authentication, automatic disk usage scan), so that its memory stays available to the services and the console.
20261025-17: Add: in Artica, The System information page warns that a server with less than 2500 MB of memory does not have all Artica features, and lists the ones turned off.
20261025-17: Add: in Artica, The assistant can tell when a server runs without its display-only features because it has less than 2500 MB of memory.
20261025-17: Add: in Artica, Gateway groups: each gateway is probed every second, marked up, degraded or down from latency and loss thresholds, with notifications and a 24-hour history shown in the routing Measures; the AI assistant can create and change these groups.
20261025-17: Fix: in Artica, The routing Measures no longer show an empty interface list as "no interface" when the interface counters cannot be read, and a gateway that loses most of its probes is no longer counted as available.
20261025-17: Fix: in Artica, A NAT rule of the routing engine that Artica cannot read is now listed in the Measures tab with its counters, instead of silently shifting its connections to the next rule.
20261025-17: Fix: in Artica, The routing tabs now rebuild themselves when the routing engine was switched from another tab or by another administrator, and the old routing tab keeps the Apply, Multipath and Refresh buttons.
20261025-17: Fix: in Artica, Form fields whose name matches their label (such as a "type" list) no longer clash with their label, so their drop-down list works and the right value is saved.
20261025-17: Fix: in Artica, The "New route" and "New NAT rule" windows of the routing engine no longer raise a script error, and their type list is read correctly when the form is saved.
20261025-17: Add: in Artica, The buttons and filters of every routing tab are now in the page header, next to a Refresh button.
20261025-17: Add: in Artica, The routing page has a new Measures tab, also available to the assistant, with the traffic of each NAT rule, the tracked connections, the interface counters and the state of the gateways.
20261025-17: Fix: in Artica, A service whose process has died is now restarted under its own system unit instead of being launched outside it.
20261025-17: Fix: in Artica Proxy, The web-filtering file watcher now runs under its own system unit and is moved back there when it was started outside it.
20261025-17: Fix: in Artica, A routing rule that matches all traffic through 0.0.0.0/0 or ::/0 now needs the same confirmation as a rule without any criterion, so a blocking rule of this kind can no longer cut all traffic by mistake.
20261025-17: Fix: in Artica, On the routing page, enabling a rule that blocks all the traffic now asks for a confirmation, and IP forwarding that was never decided is shown as such with the kernel state instead of as disabled.
20261025-17: Add: in Artica, The Web console routing page manages the routing engine: tables, routes, rules, NAT, IP forwarding, kernel view, path finder and the migration from the previous routing.
20261025-17: Fix: in Artica, The previous routing pages no longer change the old routing configuration once the routing engine is active.
20261025-17: Fix: in Artica, Firewall "Forward to" and "Next hop" rules now really send the traffic they mark through their gateway: enabled rules of this kind that had no effect before take effect after this update, and a notification lists them at the first firewall rebuild.
20261025-17: Fix: in Artica, A transparent proxy port, NAT rule or firewall routing rule whose routing table would fall on a system or reserved table is now skipped instead of flushing the main routing table.
20261025-17: Fix: in Artica, A firewall "Forward to" rule whose mark is already used by another rule or by the transparent proxy is now refused and reported instead of diverting that traffic.
20261025-17: Fix: in Artica, Firewall mark routing rules now get their own priority, and cleaning them no longer removes the main routing table rule.
20261025-17: Fix: in Artica, Forced-gateway tables of virtual IP addresses no longer collide with each other and no longer empty the main routing table.
20261025-17: Fix: in Artica, Rebuilding the network now keeps the routing rules of other services: HaCluster, transparent proxy, load balancer, namespaces and virtual IP addresses.
20261025-17: Fix: in Artica, The Squid transparent proxy mark rule, which never worked and could pile up, is removed.
20261025-17: Fix: in Artica, The per-interface IP forwarding settings are now read correctly and no longer overwritten by the global switch, except forwarding off while the appliance is a gateway.
20261025-17: Fix: in Artica AI, The network reconfigure action of the assistant now rebuilds the routes as well.
20261025-17: Fix: in Artica, The routing pages of the console are now protected against SQL injection.
20261025-17: Fix: in Artica, Firewall next-hop rules no longer write into the tables of the routing engine.
20261025-17: Add: in Artica, Routing tables, routes, source and destination rules, NAT rules and gateway settings of the routing engine can now be created, changed and removed through the API: each change is applied to the system at once, put back if it fails, and can be undone for 24 hours.
20261025-17: Add: in Artica AI, The assistant can create, change and remove routing tables, routes, rules, NAT rules and gateway settings; every change except an empty table or a disabled NAT rule waits for a confirmation and is undone when nobody confirms it.
20261025-17: Fix: in Artica, Unit routes added or removed by the assistant now go through the new routing engine once it is active, instead of being written beside it.
20261025-17: Fix: in Artica, IP forwarding can again be turned off from the routing engine when no other service needs it.
20261025-17: Fix: in Artica, DNS servers set from the text console on tty1 are now saved in the Artica settings and kept after the next resolv.conf rebuild, and an error is shown when they cannot be applied.
20261025-17: Fix: in Artica, The text console on tty1 now reports errors returned by the system instead of always showing success, and tells that advanced routing is handled by the routing engine once it is active.
20261024-17: Fix: in Artica, The PHP engine of the web console is again reported as active by systemd: restarts from the command line, the system console or the init script now go through systemd, and a watchdog puts back under systemd an engine found running outside of it.
20261024-17: Add: in Artica, The Web Console menu of the system console has a new PHP entry that rebuilds the PHP configuration, restarts the PHP engine and checks that the extensions the web console needs are loaded.
20261024-17: Fix: in Artica, Starting the REST service from the command line no longer reports it as already running when it is stopped.
20261024-17: Fix: in Artica, After an update, the web console no longer refuses every login with "curl_init No such function available": reloading the PHP service no longer removes the curl, posix and ctype extensions from its configuration.
20261024-17: Fix: in Artica, Switching to the new routing engine no longer removes the firewall's mark-based routing (NAT to a node, transparent forwarding, marked routes).
20261024-17: Fix: in Artica, On appliances using systemd-networkd, the switch to the new routing engine now waits for the administrator's decision, and the network files are regenerated when switching and when going back.
20261024-17: Fix: in Artica, Once the new routing engine is active, firewall, virtual interface and virtual IP routing tables can no longer overwrite its tables.
20261024-17: Fix: in Artica, The new routing engine no longer turns IP forwarding off.
20261024-17: Fix: in Artica, The AI assistant now reads the routing engine migration when routes are taken over, and no longer reverts a good switch because of objects the engine deliberately leaves in place.
20261024-17: Add: in Artica, The new routing engine now applies its routes, policy rules, NAT and gateway settings to the system, and applies them again after a network or firewall rebuild.
20261024-17: Add: in Artica, The existing routing is now migrated automatically to the new routing engine when the result is equivalent, with a report of every change and a way back to the previous routing.
20261024-17: Fix: in Artica, Once the new routing engine is active, advanced routing routes are no longer placed in a table that no rule uses.
20261024-17: Fix: in Artica, Once the new routing engine is active, global routing rules are now applied in standard mode.
20261024-17: Fix: in Artica, Once the new routing engine is active, source routing rules keep their type, so blackhole and prohibit rules are now applied.
20261024-17: Fix: in Artica, Once the new routing engine is active, source routing rules no longer require the output interface as input interface, so traffic from the local network now matches them.
20261024-17: Fix: in Artica, Once the new routing engine is active, obsolete NAT policy rules are no longer created.
20261024-17: Fix: in Artica, Once the new routing engine is active, a 0.0.0.0 netmask is no longer read as /8.
20261024-17: Fix: in Artica, The old routing and firewall cleanup no longer delete the rules and tables of the new routing engine.
20261024-17: Fix: in Artica Proxy, Copies of rotated logs left behind by older versions in the log rotation working directory are now removed once their compressed archive is verified, instead of being kept for the whole retention period.
20261024-17: Add: in Artica, The AI assistant now reports memory pressure (verdict, stall time, swap activity and last cache purge) when asked about memory.
20261024-17: Add: in Artica, The system memory page has been redesigned: RAM usage over the last hour with average, peak and free reserve, RAM and swap gauges, a memory stall indicator read from the kernel, and one card per memory setting with a Purge now button.
20261024-17: Fix: in Artica, The shared memory limit (kernel.shmall) is now shown and edited as a number of pages instead of being displayed as bytes.
20261024-17: Fix: in Artica, The automatic cache purge threshold now only offers values from 20% to 95%, the range the system actually applies, instead of accepting lower values that were silently ignored.
20261024-17: Fix: in Artica, Changing the memory settings, zRam or the cache purge threshold now requires the system administrator privilege.
20261024-17: Fix: in Artica Proxy, The antivirus exclusions list uses the new table design, with type icons, sorting by date and pages, and its search no longer shows an unstyled table.
20261024-17: Add: in Artica, The AI assistant can now compute a dry-run report of the routing engine migration, switch to the new routing engine with a deferred confirmation, and go back to the previous routing; it never does it on its own.
20261024-17: Fix: in Artica, When the REST API service is started by another service or by an administrator, it now always runs under its own system service, even after a failed start at boot.
20261024-17: Fix: in Artica Proxy, The nightly Kerberos renewal no longer fails and raises a notification on proxies where Kerberos authentication was turned off but an old keytab remained.
20261024-17: Fix: in Artica Proxy, The proxy service monitor now has a working stop command; its start and stop commands were merged into one malformed line.
20261024-17: Fix: in Artica, The console session is now really closed after the inactivity delay when the page only pings the server, instead of failing with an error and staying open.
20261024-17: Fix: in Artica, The OpenLDAP version check no longer runs the directory server every 3 minutes on Debian 10, which filled the OpenLDAP log with "slapd stopped" lines.
20261024-17: Fix: in Artica, The rejected certificates list of the trust store shows the short name, the issuer with its country and the full rejection date instead of raw distinguished names and a time of day.
20261024-17: Fix: in Artica, The DNS Firewall is no longer started twice when the monitoring service tries to start it while it is being restarted.
20261024-17: Add: in Artica, The trusted certificates window has been redesigned: counters per tab, a search on name, issuer or country, an origin filter, the key type and expiry of each authority, and pagination.
20261024-17: Add: in Artica, The trust store in force on the system can be downloaded as a single PEM file from the trusted certificates window.
20261024-17: Fix: in Artica Proxy, The DNS servers check no longer reports "does not answer" for a server that replies but refuses the test query, such as the categorization server; a server Squid relies on that refuses to resolve is reported as refusing queries.
20261024-17: Fix: in Artica, Applying a cluster synchronization or new rules on the DNS Firewall now restarts dnsdist through its own system service, instead of leaving it attached to the Artica service and leaving a dead process behind at each synchronization.
20261024-17: Fix: in Artica, The DNS Firewall no longer triggers a false "not running" alert from the monitoring service right after each restart.
20261024-17: Add: in Artica Proxy, The SSL status page shows the signing authority tile in red with "Incompatible certificate" when the certificate loaded on a decrypting port is not a certificate authority, since browsers reject the certificates generated from it.
20261024-17: Add: in Artica Proxy, The SSL protocol status page has been redesigned with live indicators for the signing helpers, the generated certificates, the inspection state and the signing certificate expiry, and the main settings can be switched on or off directly from their card.
20261024-17: Add: in Artica Proxy, The SSL status now reports the signing certificate loaded on each decrypting port (expiry, fingerprint, key type) and the disk usage of the generated certificates database, also visible to the AI assistant.
20261024-17: Fix: in Artica, Clearing the SSH keys of an account other than root can no longer be redirected to another file through a link, and the AI assistant no longer gives up undoing a key removal when the appliance cannot read its trash for a moment or when the key came back disabled.
20261024-17: Fix: in Artica, When an undo of the AI assistant fails for a passing reason, it keeps retrying until that change is undone, even if another change of the same operation was refused for good, and reports the refusal at the end.
20261024-17: Add: in Artica, The VPN client page now redraws each tunnel's traffic graph every 5 seconds with the live throughput.
20261024-17: Fix: in Artica, When the SSH server configuration is managed by hand, the AI assistant can still undo the disabling or removal of a key of an account other than root, and an undo the appliance refuses no longer blocks the rest of the rollback.
20261024-17: Add: in Artica, The AI assistant can add a pasted SSH public key, enable, disable or remove an authorized key after approval; disabling or removing a key must be confirmed in the Web console, otherwise it is undone.
20261024-17: Add: in Artica, The SSH server API can now add, enable, disable and remove an authorized key, refuses to remove the last key that still lets an administrator in, and can undo a removal for 24 hours.
20261024-17: Fix: in Artica, Disabling or removing the last SSH key of an account other than root now really removes it from that account's authorized_keys file, so the key can no longer be used to log in.
20261024-17: Add: in Artica, The AI assistant can read the routing tables, policy rules, NAT and gateway state of the appliance and resolve which way a packet goes.
20261024-17: Add: in Artica, The AI assistant can read the traffic of the VPN client connections: tunnel state, current, average and peak rates and volume over the requested period.
20261024-17: Add: in Artica, The VPN client page shows one card per connection with its state, tunnel address, remote gateway, account validity, current download and upload rates, volume and a two-hour traffic graph, with a search box and the number of connected and offline tunnels.
20261024-17: Fix: in Artica, The traffic of VPN client connections is now measured every minute (it was always recorded as zero) and these measurements are deleted together with the connection.
20261024-17: Add: in Artica Proxy, The AI assistant can read the SSL inspection state of the proxy: emergency mode, SSL ports, outgoing TLS policy, certificate database and trusted authorities.
20261024-17: Fix: in Artica, The routing rules table no longer stays empty when no routing rule has been created in Artica: it now also lists the routing rules loaded in the system, with the routes of each table.
20261024-17: Fix: in Artica, The traffic mirroring of a network interface now refuses a probe address that is not on a directly connected network, which made the copies reach their real recipients a second time.
20261024-17: Add: in Artica, The Mirror tab of a network interface shows whether the kernel applies the mirror, live counters and throughput of the copied traffic, and a probe reachability test.
20261024-17: Fix: in Artica, The Meta policies list and the virtual network cards page no longer fail with an internal error as soon as a policy or a card exists, so attaching a node to a policy refreshes the list correctly.
20261024-17: Fix: in Artica Proxy, An ACL rule created by the AI assistant and placed first no longer fails its verification when another rule is created at the same time: proxy ACL changes of the assistant now run one after the other.
20261024-17: Add: in Artica Proxy, The AI assistant can delete a proxy ACL rule together with its linked objects, keeping every object still used by another rule or object group.
20261024-17: Fix: in Artica, Deleting an IP alias now removes its address from the system at once; it used to stay active until the next network rebuild.
20261024-17: Fix: in Artica, Creating an IP alias now really checks that the address is not already used by another host of the network.
20261024-17: Add: in Artica, The IP aliases tab of a network interface now shows one card per alias with its address, prefix, gateway and broadcast address, whether the system carries it, an Activate button for an inactive alias, and a search and sort bar.
20261024-17: Fix: in Artica, Adding a multipath gateway to a network interface no longer removes the default route of the appliance when the interface metric is 0 or above 256.
20261024-17: Fix: in Artica, Multipath gateways defined for an interface that uses its own routing table are now really installed in that table.
20261024-17: Fix: in Artica, A multipath gateway can now be edited, its weight is checked (1 to 256) and a gateway outside the network of the interface is refused.
20261024-17: Add: in Artica, The Multipath tab of a network interface now shows one card per gateway with its weight, its real share of the connections, its latency and losses measured by ping, whether the kernel applies it, and an Apply button when the configuration is not applied.
20261024-17: Add: in Artica, The Features tab of a network interface now groups the hardware features by family (checksums, segmentation, GRO, VLAN, tunnels), explains each one, shows which ones the driver locks, and lets you filter them.
20261024-17: Add: in Artica Proxy, The AI assistant can now create a complete proxy access rule in one approved step (client addresses, web sites, allow or deny, first or last position), verified after compilation and fully reversible.
20261024-17: Fix: in Artica, The AI assistant no longer proposes non-existent "console" steps for a configuration change: it now looks up the actions really available before building its plan.
20261024-17: Fix: in Artica, When the API service is not yet available (for example just after the installation), the login page now shows a progress bar, checks the service at every 10% step and reloads by itself as soon as the service answers. While the web console is still loading its PHP components, it shows a waiting message instead of asking to restart the API service.
20261023-17: Fix: in Artica, At the end of the installation, the Artica partition labels of an older installation found on another disk are removed, so that only the new system can be started or repaired.
20261023-17: Fix: in Artica, The installer now warns when an NVMe disk is hidden by the Dell "RAID On" storage mode, and the boot menu no longer starts an older Artica installation left on another disk.
20261023-17: Add: in Artica, OpenVPN 2.7 is now built for Debian 12 and 13 with its own private libraries, so installing it can no longer replace system libraries used by other services such as PostgreSQL.
20261023-17: Fix: in Artica, The Apply buttons of several console pages, such as Address Rewriting, no longer report "This link has expired or was altered" after installing Service Pack 10.
20261023-17: Add: in Artica, The settings panel of a network interface is reorganized into four sections (general, advanced features, IP and routing, connectivity) and shows whether the stored address is the one the system runs.
20261023-17: Add: in Artica, The AI assistant can now switch the network offloads of an interface on or off (with approval, verified and reversible), and explains why the offloads of a card are off.
20261023-17: Add: in Artica, Network offloads (checksum, TSO, GSO, GRO) are now on by default on physical network cards for the best throughput, and can be switched off per interface from the interface settings.
20261023-17: Fix: in Artica, Saving the settings of a network interface no longer silently switches off its TCP/IP checksum offloading.
20261023-17: Fix: in Artica, A cluster member no longer fails to synchronize, nor loses part of its web filtering categories, when the master's category list contains a duplicate category key.
20261023-17: Fix: in Artica, Purging obsolete packages no longer reports success when packages are left behind: the progress bar now names what remains and why the purge stopped.
20261023-17: Add: in Artica, The Purge obsolete packages button now opens a window listing each package that will be removed, with its version and the reason it is obsolete, and shows why the previous purge did not remove everything.
20261023-17: Fix: in Artica, The network interface page now shows TCP/IP checksum offloading as always on for VMware vmxnet3, virtio and virtual e1000 network cards instead of offering a switch that the system would not apply.
20261023-17: Add: in Artica, At startup, servers already installed on VMware vmxnet3, virtio or virtual e1000 network cards switch their network offloads back on when an earlier configuration had turned them off.
20261023-17: Fix: in Artica, Applying the network configuration no longer disables TCP segmentation, scatter-gather and receive offloads on virtual network cards: they are now always switched on for VMware vmxnet3 and virtio cards, and for e1000 cards emulated by a hypervisor, and left to the driver on Hyper-V and Xen, which restores full network speed on virtual appliances.
20261023-17: Add: in Artica KSC Installer, A new Restore option imports the migration export of an old Kaspersky Security Center server (groups, devices, policies and tasks) into the new server, from the management menu or with --restore, with an optional backup beforehand.
20261023-17: Fix: in Artica, The Artica REST API service is no longer reported as failed when the system stops another process for lack of memory, and a service state left failed that way is repaired automatically.
20261023-17: Fix: in Artica Proxy, The category service started by Artica now runs in its own system unit or scope, so a memory kill of it no longer affects the Artica REST API service.
20261023-17: Fix: in Artica Proxy, A categories server now republishes its databases and its categories table to the proxies as soon as the web-filtering repository is enabled, instead of reporting the table as unavailable until a category is recompiled.
20261023-17: Add: in Artica DNS, The new DNS record dialog shows one tile per record type, with a short explanation of each type and a search box, instead of a drop-down list.
20261023-17: Fix: in Artica Proxy, The category service no longer rebuilds its table of category names for each request, which reduces its memory use.
20261023-17: Fix: in Artica, The DNS Firewall cache can no longer be sized beyond what the server memory can hold: all DNS caches together are kept under 70% of the RAM.
20261023-17: Fix: in Artica, Archived logs copied to another disk are now removed after the retention period counted from their archive date, not from the date of the copy.
20261023-17: Fix: in Artica, Archives left in the former backup directory are removed once an identical copy exists in the configured backup directory, which frees the system disk.
20261023-17: Fix: in Artica, A single failed system unit no longer makes Artica start every other service outside systemd.
20261023-17: Fix: in Artica Proxy, The PAC server started outside its system unit is now restarted under it automatically, so the unit no longer stays in the failed state.
20261023-17: Fix: in Artica, The DNS Firewall service no longer leaves defunct dnsdist processes behind each time dnsdist stops, and no longer keeps its console output in the Artica API memory.
20261023-17: Fix: in Artica, The left menu no longer keeps every visited entry highlighted in white: only the entry of the page currently displayed stays highlighted.
20261023-17: Fix: in Artica, Restarting a stopped Zabbix agent no longer reports a failure while the agent actually starts.
20261023-17: Fix: in Artica, Searching the Zabbix agent events no longer passes the search text to a system command, and lists the newest events first.
20261023-17: Add: in Artica, The AI assistant can read the last bulk categorization test and, after approval, run it again, export a personal category, and perform the emergency removal of ClamAV.
20261023-17: Fix: in Artica, Uploading ClamAV signatures as a zip file no longer needs the unzip command, installs the incremental databases (.cld) too, and fails clearly when the archive holds no signature.
20261023-17: Fix: in Artica, The emergency removal of ClamAV now purges only the packages actually installed and refuses to run while another package operation is in progress.
20261023-17: Fix: in Artica Web Filtering, Testing a list of websites against the categories is now done by the Artica daemon, accepts URLs and proxy log lines, and no longer builds its result page from unescaped site names.
20261023-17: Fix: in Artica Web Filtering, Exporting the websites of a category no longer goes through a system command.
20261023-17: Fix: in Artica, The DHCP configuration file is now shown read-only with its DDNS and OMAPI keys masked, and is no longer copied to a folder served by the web console.
20261023-17: Add: in Artica, The AI assistant can now search ten service logs and see which parent-proxy rules are applied, and, after approval, apply the AppArmor boot setting and the TFTP server settings, test the FTP account of the console and export the event tables.
20261023-17: Fix: in Artica Proxy, The web filtering service no longer uses up to 1 GB of extra memory within a minute when it categorizes many IP addresses, which could make the system stop it or the DNS service on servers with 4 GB of memory.
20261023-17: Fix: in Artica Proxy, The IP addresses of Blizzard game servers are now categorized as Games; a typo in the first address range had disabled the whole list.
20261023-17: Fix: in Artica, The AppArmor protection switch of the System information page works again: it updates the boot loader instead of leaving its progress bar stuck.
20261023-17: Fix: in Artica, Searching the events of a service (Redis, SNMP, Rsync, ITCharter, Wazuh agent, web error page, mail filter, DNS backends, statistics retention, Active Directory API) no longer passes the search text to a system command, and lists the newest events first.
20261023-17: Fix: in Artica, Saving the TFTP server settings no longer reinstalls the service each time, and the server listens on all addresses when the chosen interface has none.
20261023-17: Fix: in Artica, Exporting a database table to CSV no longer requires the sqlite3 command to be installed.
20261023-17: Fix: in KasperskyTIP, The installation ISO no longer stores the root password in clear text; only its hash is written to the installer configuration.
20261023-17: Add: in Artica, The AI assistant can read the certificate of a Docker Store application and propose, for approval, the installation of a hardened Vaultwarden server.
20261023-17: Add: in Artica, The Docker Store can now install a ready-to-use Vaultwarden password server in one step: HTTPS certificate generated for your host name, public sign-up closed, administration page protected by a hashed token, optional mail server, and a certificate authority to download for the client devices.
20261022-17: Fix: in Artica, The Web console PHP engine now loads only the extensions the console uses (about 46 modules instead of 61, without FFI, XML-RPC or Phar), and no longer depends on the extensions enabled by the operating system packages.
20261022-17: Fix: in Artica, PHP extensions are no longer loaded twice by the Web console: duplicates are removed when the configuration is written, then checked against PHP itself and disabled if any remain.
20261022-17: Fix: in Artica, Two unused PHP-FPM pools with permissive settings were removed, and the PHP engine no longer writes memory dumps of its administrator processes or loads extensions at runtime.
20261022-17: Fix: in Artica, The root back-end of the console no longer ships about 1,000 unused request handlers and 35 unused scripts, reducing the code that runs with administrator privileges.
20261022-17: Add: in Artica Proxy, ACL objects listing user names go back to the native Squid user list when the installed proxy includes the Artica letter-case fix, and keep the pattern-based match on any other proxy version.
20261022-17: Fix: in Artica, Installing a system package from the console now reports a failure when the package could not be installed, instead of always ending with a success.
20261022-17: Fix: in Artica, The system checks that follow a Service Pack installation now run again; they called a file that did not exist.
20261022-17: Fix: in Artica, The Apply button of the web console no longer fails with "This link has expired or was altered" when several pages load at the same time, for example on the Address Rewriting page after a hotfix update.
20261022-17: Add: in Artica AI, The assistant can now check which disk the boot loader will be written to and warns when the next GRUB update could leave the server unable to start.
20261022-17: Add: in Artica, The appliance now warns when the boot loader is configured for the wrong disk, including on VMware, and apt displays a warning before a system update would leave the server unable to restart.
20261022-17: Add: in Artica, A watchdog now closes forgotten idle statistics database connections before the connection limit is reached, and names the program that opens too many of them.
20261022-17: Fix: in Artica, The statistics database now closes sessions left idle for 15 minutes and reports session states again, which lets idle connections be cleaned up automatically.
20261022-17: Fix: in Artica Proxy, Updating the proxy logging helper no longer leaves a moment where the helper is missing, which made a proxy reload fail during Artica updates.
20261022-17: Fix: in Artica Proxy, Blocking rules restricted to plain HTTP no longer make the new configuration be refused right after an Artica update.
20261022-17: Fix: in Artica, A reboot no longer leaves the Motorcomm YT6801 network card armed for Wake-on-LAN; wake-up stays enabled only after a power-off.
20261022-17: Fix: in Artica Proxy, ACL objects of type "Is Authenticated" now match any authenticated user instead of being checked as an Active Directory group of the same name, which matched nobody.
20261022-17: Add: in KasperskyTIP, Blocklists are saved to disk after each update and reloaded at startup, so the data port serves the last known lists immediately after a restart.
20261022-17: Add: in KasperskyTIP, A new Manual entries page lets administrators add IP addresses and URLs by hand; they are served on their own lists and merged, without duplicates, into the Dangerous IPs and Malicious URLs lists.
20261022-17: Add: in Artica SIEM, New DHCP pages show requests, leases and a dashboard, and the address sheet now lists the DHCP leases of an address.
20261022-17: Add: in Artica, On Debian 10, the System information page warns when PHP is exposed to PHP2Shell (CVE-2026-109618, CVE-2026-109619) and offers a button that installs the fixed PHP 7.3 from the Freexian Extended LTS repository, then restarts PHP.
20261022-17: Fix: in Artica, Two nodes that each declare the other as their cluster master no longer make Meta send a policy back and forth between them every three minutes; the policy is held and the editor explains why.
20261022-17: Add: in Artica, The delivery status of a Meta policy now lists the cluster slaves reached through their master and flags those whose master is not managed by Meta.
20261022-17: Add: in Artica, The AI assistant can now list Meta policies, check their delivery to each node and apply, attach or detach them with confirmation.
20261022-17: Add: in Artica, The Meta console can define virtual network cards and map each one to the real interface of every node, and the old per-group proxy page is replaced by the Policies page.
20261022-17: Add: in Artica, The Meta console has a policy editor: each proxy setting can be left to the node or defined by the policy, with the Artica default shown for reference, plus the general whitelist and blacklist, the targeted nodes and groups, and the delivery report of every node.
20261022-17: Add: in Artica, The Meta console now has a Policies page to create named sets of proxy settings and apply them to nodes and groups of nodes, with the update status of each policy.
20261022-17: Add: in Artica Proxy, The Certificate Center can now remove root authorities from the system trust store and refuse specific compromised certificates, and the change is replicated to every proxy of the cluster.
20261022-17: Add: in Artica, The AI assistant can read the system trust store and, with an administrator's approval, remove or restore trusted roots, add authorities, refuse a compromised certificate and apply the policy.
20261022-17: Fix: in Artica Meta, Opening the web console of a managed server through the Meta console no longer logs the administrator out of the Meta console.
20261022-17: Fix: in Artica Meta, Opening the web console of a managed Artica server through the Meta console no longer returns a 404 error on servers where the Artica AI remote terminal verifier is configured.
20261022-17: Add: in Artica, The network agent status page now shows the state of the tunnel to the Meta server when the agent is enrolled in reverse mode, and its status tiles all have the same height.
20261022-17: Fix: in Artica, A failed enrollment with the Meta server no longer keeps any data from the enrollment file on the agent, and an earlier unfinished enrollment no longer blocks a new enrollment file.
20261022-17: Fix: in Artica, Enrollment failures with the Meta server now show their real cause instead of always reporting a certificate error.
20261022-17: Fix: in Artica, Installing a hotfix no longer breaks the connection point used by agents to enroll with the Meta server, which made every enrollment fail with a 502 error.
20261022-17: Fix: in Artica, Enrolling an agent with a Meta server from the enrollment file no longer fails with a certificate error when "Allow self-signed certificates" is checked and the Meta server uses a publicly trusted certificate.
20261021-17: Fix: in Artica Proxy, A web-filtering category with no name no longer turns every official category into "Unknown" in the filtering rules.
20261021-17: Add: in Artica, The DNS records page shows whether each record is actually served by the DNS cache, its TTL, and can filter by record type.
20261021-17: Add: in Artica, The DNS cache can stop answering IPv6 (AAAA) records, for every domain or for a list of domains, without emptying the cache.
20261021-17: Add: in Artica, Each DNS firewall policy (RPZ) can limit the size and duration of its list download, so an oversized or slow source can no longer exhaust memory or stall the update.
20261021-17: Fix: in Artica, Adding an Active Directory DNS record no longer empties the DNS cache.
20261021-17: Fix: in Artica, Editing a local DNS record no longer rebuilds the DNS firewall zones, which could restart the DNS cache.
20261021-17: Fix: in Artica, Deleting one DNS record of a host no longer stops the DNS cache from answering the other records of that host.
20261021-17: Add: in Artica, The disk details now offer a "Format disk" button on a disk with no mounted partition: after a warning, it erases every partition and creates a single unmounted ext4 partition.
20261021-17: Fix: in Artica, The DHCP install button of the dashboard no longer fails with a "404 Not found" error.
20261021-17: Add: in Artica, On a physical server without smartmontools, the disk details and the SMART monitoring page offer an "Install SMART" button with an installation progress bar.
20261021-17: Fix: in Artica, The installer no longer offers disks smaller than 10 GB, which are too small to hold an Artica system.
20261021-17: Fix: in Artica, The installer now recognizes the internal SD modules of servers, such as the Dell Internal Dual SD, and offers them as installation disks instead of treating them as external USB keys.
20261021-17: Fix: in Artica, The cache rate and queries tiles of the DNS cache service show the real counters again instead of staying at 0.
20261021-17: Add: in Artica, The PostgreSQL status page now says when the database service is disabled and offers an "Enable PostgreSQL" button that enables and installs it.
20261021-17: Fix: in Artica, After the system clock is corrected backwards at boot, the scheduled maintenance tasks resume at once instead of stopping for as long as the correction.
20261021-17: Fix: in Artica, After the system clock is corrected backwards, the service status pages no longer show an outdated state for as long as the correction.
20261021-17: Fix: in Artica, A freshly installed DNS cache service answers on the network interfaces right away instead of listening on the loopback only.
20261021-17: Fix: in Artica, The DHCP configuration, leases and reservations pages no longer fail with an internal error when the PostgreSQL service is not running.
20261021-17: Fix: in Artica Reverse Proxy, The maintenance mode switch is back in the web services list (action menu of each website) and in the settings of each website.
20261021-17: Fix: in Artica Reverse Proxy, "Compile your rules" in the Web Application Firewall rules no longer fails with an error on appliances where GeoIP is enabled, so custom firewall rules are applied again.
20261021-17: Fix: in Artica Proxy, When the disk holding the system logs stops responding, the reverse-proxy service keeps running and only loses log lines instead of freezing until the disk recovers.
20261021-17: Fix: in Artica Proxy, The web application firewall audit index is no longer written to the system logs disk, so a stalled logs disk no longer stops the reverse-proxy from serving websites.
20261021-17: Add: in Artica AI, The assistant can read whether the Web console client-certificate authentication is enabled and really enforced, the state of the console certificate authority and which accounts hold a certificate.
20261021-17: Fix: in Artica, Web console client certificates are no longer stored in a public folder of the web server, and the password chosen for a certificate is no longer saved in the settings.
20261021-17: Fix: in Artica, The "Authenticate SSL Clients" option of the web console is now enforced by the web server: browsers without a client certificate issued by the console are refused before reaching the login page.
20261021-17: Fix: in Artica, The PHP configuration of the web console and of published PHP sites now applies the recommended mitigation for the PHP2Shell remote code execution flaws (CVE-2026-109618, CVE-2026-109619) until patched PHP versions are installed.
20261021-17: Fix: in Artica, Removing an OpenVPN client connection now also removes its watchdog entry, so the deleted tunnel is no longer restarted automatically.
20261021-17: Fix: in Artica, A load-balancer used as the DNS server of its proxy farm now answers DNS on its failover virtual IP, so member proxies no longer lose name resolution and Internet access when they point to that address.
20261021-17: Fix: in Artica, The installer now wipes old LVM volumes, RAID metadata and partition tables from the target disk before partitioning, so a disk that held a previous installation no longer stops the setup.
20261021-17: Fix: in Artica, The installer now removes the Artica labels left on other disks by an older installation, so the machine can no longer boot the old system after the first restart.
20261021-17: Add: in Artica, External USB disks are no longer offered anywhere during the installation, including manual partitioning and boot loader selection.
20261021-17: Fix: in Artica Proxy, Strict deny rules edited on the master of a proxy cluster are now replicated to the other members again; until now they stayed on the master.
20261020-17: Add: in Artica SIEM, The firewall events can now be searched by source MAC address, written in any common form and optionally followed by a destination port.
20261020-17: Fix: in Artica SIEM, Filtering firewall events by MAC address is now refused to accounts that are not allowed to see MAC addresses, which could otherwise check whether a hidden address was on the network.
20261020-17: Fix: in Artica Proxy, ACL objects listing user names now match a member whatever the letter case of the login, where Squid 6 and later only recognized logins written entirely in lowercase.
20261020-17: Fix: in Artica SIEM, Saving or deleting a firewall source now reports its errors in a translated error message instead of an untranslated line at the top of the form.
20261020-17: Fix: in Artica SIEM, The FortiGate menu entry and tab for firewall policies are now named Policies, like their page.
20261020-17: Add: in Artica Proxy, The Web-filtering categorization service now always recognizes sites hosted on Cloudflare Pages, Vercel, Wix Studio, GitHub Pages, Webflow, Netlify and Typedream as individual tenants when filing phishing reports.
20261020-17: Add: in Artica Proxy, The Web-filtering categorization service now imports the PhishDestroy blocklist into the Phishing category.
20261020-17: Fix: in Artica, The SIEM description in the product choice of the installation wizard is now short enough to fit inside its tile.
20261020-17: Add: in Artica, The AI assistant can now report how much traffic and how many sessions went through the FortiGate firewalls over a period, for one tenant if needed, and which machines and destinations account for most of it.
20261020-17: Add: in Artica SIEM, A new FortiGate General data page shows, per tenant and FortiGate over 15 minutes to 90 days, the data downloaded and uploaded and the number of sessions, next to the top clients, destinations and flows.
20261020-17: Add: in Artica SIEM, In every FortiGate chart legend, a client, destination or policy name now opens its details, on top of the window already open.
20261020-17: Fix: in Artica SIEM, A FortiGate client whose announced name is only a control character is now shown by its address instead of an unreadable symbol.
20261020-17: Add: in Artica SIEM, The event tables (firewall, proxy, DNS and web server requests) now show the name of the machine that held the DHCP lease on an address at the time of the event, unless a local host name is already known.
20261020-17: Add: in Artica, DHCP requests, leases and reservations are now sent to the SIEM when the appliance serves DHCP and is connected to a SIEM.
20261020-17: Add: in Artica, The AI assistant can tell whether the DHCP events reach the SIEM and, after approval, turn them on or off.
20261020-17: Add: in Artica, The AI assistant can now tell where the traffic of the machines behind a FortiGate goes, which clients talk to a given destination, and when the biggest transfers happened.
20261020-17: Add: in Artica, The AI assistant can now tell which FortiGate policies let the most traffic through or refuse the most, and which clients cross a given policy.
20261020-17: Add: in Artica SIEM, A new FortiGate policies page shows the traffic, logs and denials of each firewall policy, Internet sources included, with the top policies, a searchable list and per policy its clients, destinations, largest flows and bandwidth over 1 hour to 21 days.
20261020-17: Add: in Artica SIEM, A new FortiGate destinations page shows what internal devices download from and upload to each destination, with the top destinations, a searchable list with trend lines and per destination its clients, largest flows and bandwidth.
20261020-17: Add: in Artica, The AI assistant can now show where an internal machine seen by a FortiGate sends and receives the most traffic, and when its biggest transfers happened.
20261020-17: Add: in Artica SIEM, Clicking a FortiGate client opens its details: top destinations, largest 10-minute flows, a bandwidth chart per 10 minutes and a searchable list of every destination with data received and sent, over 1 hour to 21 days.
20261020-17: Add: in Artica, The AI assistant can now tell when an internal machine seen by a FortiGate used the network, with its peak hours over the last week.
20261020-17: Add: in Artica SIEM, The FortiGate client list now shows a 24-hour trend line and a relative bar for received and sent data, the device type, the operating system and whether the device is active, with page navigation.
20261020-17: Add: in Artica SIEM, The FortiGate clients statistics now show large rings with the total received or sent in the centre, and each card opens the full ranking of the top 100 clients.
20261019-17: Add: in Artica SIEM, The FortiGate status view has a new layout with ranked bars, the share of each value and a link on every card to its full ranking.
20261019-17: Add: in Artica SIEM, The first-installation wizard can now set up a SIEM appliance: it downloads ClickHouse from the ArticaTech repository, then installs and enables the SIEM, with progress shown both in the wizard and in the SIEM feature section.
20261019-17: Fix: in Artica, Importing a p7r or p7b certificate answer no longer erases the private key of the request it completes, and a certificate that does not match that key is refused.
20261019-17: Fix: in Artica, Restoring a certificates database backup now replaces the certificates in a single safe step instead of overwriting the database file in use, and older backups restore correctly.
20261019-17: Fix: in Artica, The PFX password is no longer kept in the web session during a certificate import, and PFX, p7r and backup imports now report their result immediately.
20261019-17: Fix: in Artica, Generating a self-signed certificate from its settings now also records its validity dates and its PFX file.
20261019-17: Fix: in Artica Proxy, The listening-port certificate wizard now names the authority after the unit entered in the form and applies the new port settings without a full proxy restart.
20261019-17: Fix: in Artica, The default web-filtering certificate is no longer regenerated each time the setup wizard runs.
20261019-17: Add: in Artica, The AI assistant can now tell which internal machines a FortiGate sees, how much they download or upload, and when they were last seen.
20261019-17: Add: in Artica SIEM, A new Fortigate entry in the SIEM menu, shown only when FortiGate data is recorded, gathers the FortiGate status view and a FortiGate clients page with the top clients by data received and sent and a searchable client list filtered by tenant and FortiGate.
20261019-17: Add: in Artica SIEM, Each FortiGate client now records the tenant and the FortiGate that saw it, so identical internal addresses at two sites are no longer merged.
20261019-17: Add: in Artica SIEM, FortiGate traffic now builds an inventory of internal clients (MAC address, host name, operating system, address, bytes received and sent, last seen) with their traffic per destination in 10-minute slices; clients silent for more than three weeks are removed with their history.
20261019-17: Add: in Artica, The agent groups page can now show each group as a tile with its first agents, their state and version, and highlights groups with offline agents or alerts; a switch in the header returns to the table view.
20261019-17: Fix: in Artica, The help text about issuing one certificate for several hosts in the Let's Encrypt DNS request form is now translated.
20261019-17: Fix: in Artica, When the server cannot reach Let's Encrypt, certificate creation and renewal now stop immediately with a clear message saying that outbound traffic to Let's Encrypt is not open.
20261019-17: Fix: in Artica Proxy, The proxy auto-configuration (PAC) service now relays Let's Encrypt validation requests when it listens on port 80, so certificates can be issued and renewed on the same server.
20261019-17: Fix: in Artica, Let's Encrypt certificates are again issued and renewed on servers without the reverse-proxy web service: the validation is now answered directly on port 80 instead of waiting for a web server that is not running.
20261018-17: Add: in Artica, Monit 6 is now built automatically for Debian 12 and 13 from each new official release, with SSL, PAM and IPv6 support, ready to replace the older Debian package.
20261018-12: Add: in Artica, The settings of an existing firewall rule are now shown as a summary grouped by theme, and each setting is changed on its own in a small dialog.
20261018-12: Add: in Artica, The proxy and firewall objects page has been redesigned: filters by object type with counts, description of each object, on/off switches and the rules that use each object.
20261018-12: Add: in Artica, The firewall services page shows how many rules use each service, filters by protocol and status, and enables or disables a service with a switch.
20261018-12: Add: in Artica, The firewall rules page has been redesigned with a filter bar (search, interface, status), on/off switches, colour-coded directions and a count of the rules shown.
20261018-12: Fix: in Artica, The firewall rules list can be filtered by interface again, and moving a rule up or down now shows the new order immediately.
20261018-12: Fix: in Artica, The firewall rules page no longer fails to load when the firewall counters cannot be read.
20261018-12: Add: in Artica, The firewall services page uses the new table design, with a search box, the ports of each service shown as tags and its own address.
20261018-12: Fix: in Artica, The Suricata IDS service now reads and writes its settings through the Artica REST service instead of opening the cache database directly, so setting changes made in the Web Console are taken into account immediately.
20261018-12: Add: in Artica, The Suricata IDS package is now rebuilt automatically for Debian 12 and 13 whenever a new Suricata 8 release or a new Debian kernel is published, so its PF_RING driver always matches the latest kernel.
20261018-12: Fix: in Artica Proxy, The silent authentication page now shows accented chart labels and a capitalised time column.
20261018-12: Add: in Artica, The Artica Meta status dashboard has been redesigned: fleet health index, ring charts for the repository, agent and Debian versions and pending updates, and a live overview of the agents that need attention first.
20261018-12: Fix: in Artica Proxy, Silent authentication now presents users of the declared Active Directory domains without the domain prefix, so the user lists of the proxy rules match them as with NTLM and Kerberos.
20261018-12: Fix: in Artica Proxy, The silent authentication challenge now announces a valid NetBIOS computer name, as the NTLM specification requires.
20261018-12: Fix: in Artica Proxy, The authentication challenge now always returns a lightweight page, so browsers no longer drop the Windows sign-in handshake and show a login popup when user or Active Directory group rules are used.
20261018-12: Fix: in Artica, The GlusterFS storage pool now shows the real name of this node instead of "localhost".
20261018-12: Fix: in Artica, The last step of the GlusterFS volume creation wizard shows a clear summary and the full equivalent command, which was cut off on the right.
20261018-12: Fix: in Artica, When adding bricks to a GlusterFS volume, the proposed path is now on a dedicated disk not yet used by the volume instead of the system disk, and the help text explains that Use adds the disk to the list.
20261018-12: Fix: in Artica, The GlusterFS Status and Usage tabs no longer count the space of a volume deleted during the last hour.
20261018-12: Fix: in Artica, Disabling GlusterFS now asks for a clear confirmation listing what will be stopped, instead of a generic deletion message with an untranslated text.
20261018-12: Fix: in Artica, On an appliance with a single processor under load, the status of the services (uptime, running state) is no longer frozen on an old value.
20261018-12: Fix: in Artica, Active Directory LDAP connections now always use the recorded IP address of the domain controller instead of switching at random between its host name and its IP address.
20261018-12: Fix: in Artica Proxy, The Silent authentication page now shows the Active Directory groups of each recently identified user instead of an always empty column.
20261018-12: Fix: in Artica, Installing GlusterFS no longer needs access to a Debian package mirror: the GlusterFS package now carries the libraries it requires.
20261018-12: Fix: in Artica Proxy, HaCluster nodes no longer keep a replica of the IT charter database: they check and record the acceptances, and read the charters, directly on the load balancer, which ends the endless replication failures when the load balancer runs a newer database version.
20261018-12: Fix: in Artica Proxy, The web filtering service no longer opens a new connection to the IT charter database for every check: one connection is kept and reused, with bounded timeouts.
20261018-12: Fix: in Artica, A HaCluster failover master that starts while the backup node holds the floating IP address no longer records itself as the owner of that address.
20261018-12: Add: in Artica, The AI assistant can read the clock skew of the HaCluster nodes and, after approval, resynchronize a node on the load balancer.
20261018-12: Fix: in Artica Proxy, The HaCluster Windows console keeps showing the IT charter acceptances when the local socket of the charter database has disappeared, by reading the database on the loopback address instead.
20261018-12: Add: in Artica Proxy, The load balancer measures the clock of every cluster node and shows a yellow "Clock out of sync" label when it differs by 30 seconds or more, with a dialog to resynchronize the node from the web console or the Windows console.
20261018-12: Fix: in Artica Proxy, Cluster nodes without the chrony package now install it, so that they keep their clock synchronized on the load balancer instead of drifting until Kerberos fails.
20261018-12: Add: in Artica Proxy, Silent authentication identifies Windows users through NTLM without joining the domain and applies Active Directory group rules from the LDAP connection.
20261018-12: Fix: in Artica Proxy, A global blacklist holding both a domain and one of its subdomains no longer makes the proxy refuse every new configuration.
20261018-12: Fix: in Artica, Opening the GlusterFS Encryption tab after the Usage tab no longer leaves the Usage period selector, unstyled, in the page header: the Encryption tab now shows its own title, explanation and refresh button.
20261018-12: Fix: in Artica Proxy, After the Kerberos keytab is replaced, cluster nodes reload their authentication helpers, which kept the old key in memory and made browsers show a login popup.
20261018-12: Fix: in Artica, The GlusterFS mount wizard names its options in plain words (read-only, POSIX access control lists, do not record file access times) instead of showing the raw mount flags.
20261018-12: Fix: in Artica Proxy, The HaCluster status page now shows the address the load balancer really listens on: with failover it is the floating IP, flagged as such, instead of the configured interface that made clients aim at an address answering with a connection reset.
20261018-12: Add: in Artica Proxy, The HaCluster status page has a new design: four summary tiles, period selector, period totals that pick the chart to display, curve or raw view, CSV export, and a node table with state, weight share and last health check duration.
20261018-12: Add: in Artica, The AI assistant can read where the HaCluster load balancer really listens, to explain a connection reset on the proxy port.
20261018-12: Add: in Artica, The GlusterFS mount wizard gets the same design as the volume creation wizard: step indicator, source chosen between two cards showing which node serves the volume, live check of the mount point, backup servers and options as toggles, and a clearer summary.
20261018-12: Add: in Artica, The AI assistant can check the Kerberos authentication of a HaCluster again at once, on the operator's request and after approval, to confirm an Active Directory fix without waiting up to 10 minutes.
20261018-12: Add: in Artica Proxy, The HaCluster Windows console has a "Check now" button on its Kerberos alerts: the load balancer keytab and the nodes in alert are checked again at once, instead of up to 10 minutes after a fix.
20261018-12: Fix: in Artica Proxy, The HaCluster Windows console no longer gives up after 4 seconds when the load balancer takes longer to apply the distribution rules.
20261018-12: Add: in Artica, The bricks step of the GlusterFS volume creation wizard shows which host is this appliance and which are the pool peers, tags every line as local, peer or outside the pool, checks each brick path as you type, and gains a step indicator.
20261018-12: Fix: in Artica, When the Artica daemon answers that an item does not exist (for example a GlusterFS volume deleted meanwhile), the console now shows that reason instead of a misleading "404 Not found, did you use the correct version of the Web API service?" error.
20261018-12: Add: in Artica, Bricks are added to a GlusterFS volume through a list: pick a node of the pool and a directory, review the bricks grouped by replica set, delete any line, then send them in one go.
20261018-12: Add: in Artica, The GlusterFS Usage tab now shows its period selector and its explanation in the page header, leaving the whole tab to the gauges and charts.
20261018-12: Add: in Artica, The GlusterFS Encryption tab is now a dashboard: setup progress, management encryption, pool nodes, volumes and external clients in tiles that open their own dialogs, and the certificate authority and node certificate in a settings card.
20261018-12: Add: in Artica, The GlusterFS client networks allowed through the firewall are now managed in a table: add one address or network at a time and delete any row, instead of editing a free-text list.
20261018-12: Add: in Artica, The GlusterFS Status tab is now a dashboard: service, version, pool nodes, volumes, storage used and self-heal in separate tiles, plus a firewall tile showing the open ports and the nodes and networks allowed to reach them.
20261018-12: Fix: in Artica Proxy, The HaCluster menu now shows "Windows console" instead of an untranslated label.
20261018-12: Fix: in Artica Proxy, The HaCluster Windows console certificate page now says that a certificate can also take a node out of Active Directory emergency mode and read the IT charter acceptances.
20261018-12: Fix: in Artica Proxy, The "Source IP address" label is no longer misspelled.
20261018-12: Fix: in Artica Proxy, The HaCluster Windows console names the web console page that issues its certificates as it appears in the menu.
20261018-12: Fix: in Artica Proxy, A cluster load balancer no longer ends up running two load-balancing engines after a reboot, and an existing duplicate is stopped automatically.
20261018-12: Fix: in Artica Proxy, With load balancer failover, the proxies now use the floating address of the active load balancer for DNS, time and reports, instead of an address that disappears after a failover.
20261018-12: Fix: in Artica Proxy, IT charter acceptances and charters now survive a load balancer failover and its return, and enabling the IT charter now also reaches the backup load balancer.
20261018-12: Add: in Artica Proxy, The HaCluster Windows console shows an "ITCharter" menu while the cluster IT charter is enabled, listing which user accepted which charter and when, with a filter, in every language of the console.
20261018-12: Add: in Artica, The AI assistant can now summarize the firewall configuration export and import a firewall configuration exported by another appliance into a draft, always with an administrator approval and without applying anything until the draft is applied.
20261018-12: Add: in Artica, The firewall configuration can now be exported to a file and imported on another appliance: interfaces are matched by hand, object groups are recreated, and the imported configuration opens as a draft to preview before it is applied with confirmation.
