20261018-12: Fix: in Artica Proxy, Visitors connecting over IPv6 now appear in the web statistics (Top IP, number of clients, countries and providers) with the same counters and geolocation as IPv4 visitors.
20261018-12: Fix: in Artica Proxy, Web Application Firewall reports are now recorded for IPv6 clients, and an audit file whose header cannot be read is kept in quarantine instead of being deleted.
20261018-12: Fix: in Artica Proxy, The "Deny access" button now really blocks an IPv6 address, and an IPv6 entry no longer prevents the IPv4 entries of the inbound block list from being applied.
20261018-12: Fix: in Artica Proxy, Access lists (stream access, WebDAV, directories) now accept a single IPv6 address.
20261018-12: Fix: in Artica Proxy, Searching for a full or partial IPv6 address now works in the Threats and CrowdSec pages.
20261018-12: Fix: in Artica Proxy, Bots seen from IPv6 addresses are now listed with their own address instead of being merged under 0.0.0.0.
20261018-12: Fix: in Artica Proxy, IPv4 /18 and /28 networks added to the inbound block list are now applied instead of being silently ignored.
20261018-12: Fix: in Artica Proxy, The Top IP counters no longer count a 10-minute window twice after a failed database insert.
20261018-12: Fix: in Artica Proxy, Enabling the central error page on a cluster load balancer now publishes the page immediately instead of up to ten minutes later, and refuses HTTPS without a certificate.
20261018-12: Fix: in Artica Proxy, Cluster proxies whose agent is older than 1.1.32 now also redirect blocked users to the load balancer's central error page.
20261018-12: Fix: in Artica Proxy, In a load-balancing cluster using the central error page, the web error page service of each proxy can no longer be disabled by a configuration replication or from the console, and it re-enables itself when the load balancer needs it.
20261018-12: Fix: in Artica Proxy, The web error page service no longer answers an internal error (500) on proxies where its page templates had never been generated.
20261018-12: Fix: in Artica Proxy, Blocked users of a load-balancing cluster are now redirected to the load balancer's central error page instead of each proxy's own page.
20261018-12: Fix: in Artica Proxy, Uninstalling the web error page service no longer leaves it running without supervision.
20261018-12: Fix: in Artica, A GlusterFS mount that has lost its connection to the volume is now remounted automatically within five minutes instead of staying broken.
20261018-12: Add: in Artica, GlusterFS now warns before the TLS certificates of the pool expire, and snapshots keep and restore the pool encryption material.
20261018-12: Add: in Artica, GlusterFS traffic can now be encrypted with TLS: a pool certificate authority is created on one node and imported on the others, management and data encryption are switched on from the console, and certificates can be issued for external clients.
20261018-12: Add: in Artica, Firewall changes can now be prepared in a draft, previewed (configuration changes, kernel rules added or removed, rules iptables would refuse) and then applied with confirmation or discarded in one step.
20261018-12: Fix: in Artica, Uninstalling a service on a system without systemd now also removes its boot links, and the leftover start script of the deprecated Tailon log viewer is removed.
20261018-12: Fix: in Artica, Service Pack rollback backups no longer pile up on the disk: only the three most recent rollback points of the current version are kept, checked every 4 hours.
20261018-12: Fix: in Artica, The capacity of a GlusterFS volume whose bricks have different sizes is now the size of its smallest copy, so fill alerts fire before the smaller disk is full.
20261018-12: Fix: in Artica, A GlusterFS brick that was replaced or removed no longer appears as offline in the usage view for an hour.
20261018-12: Fix: in Artica, Installing GlusterFS on Debian 13 no longer fails with "missing libraries": the libaio and liburing libraries required by the storage bricks are now installed automatically.
20261018-12: Add: in Artica AI, The assistant checks the Kerberos keytab of the HaCluster load balancer first and gives the right steps to rebuild a keytab that does not match the account of the service name.
20261018-12: Add: in Artica Proxy, The HaCluster Windows console shows the Kerberos state of the cluster keytab held by the load balancer, and explains how to rebuild it when it does not match the account of the service name.
20261018-12: Add: in Artica Proxy, The HaCluster load balancer now checks its own Kerberos keytab, the only one of the cluster, and shows a red alert on its Kerberos page and above the node list when browsers cannot use it.
20261018-12: Fix: in Artica Proxy, The Kerberos alert no longer suggests moving the service name between accounts: it explains that the keytab does not match the account owning the name and gives the commands to rebuild it on the load balancer.
20261018-12: Add: in Artica AI, The assistant can check the Kerberos service name of a proxy, read the Kerberos state of each HaCluster node and, with approval, take a node out of the Active Directory emergency mode.
20261018-12: Fix: in Artica Proxy, The load balancer shows the current state of a node right after its report, instead of a state up to 10 minutes old (for example a node that has just left the Active Directory emergency mode).
20261018-12: Add: in Artica Proxy, The HaCluster Windows console shows a red Kerberos alert on a node whose service name cannot get a usable ticket, with the steps to fix it.
20261018-12: Add: in Artica Proxy, The Active Directory status page shows a red tile when the Kerberos service name of the proxy cannot get a usable ticket (name held by another account, not registered, or keytab rejected), with the steps to fix it.
20261018-12: Add: in Artica Proxy, Each HaCluster node now checks its Kerberos service name and reports a failure to the load balancer, which shows it on the node in the web console.
20261018-12: Fix: in Artica Proxy, A Kerberos ticket error logged by the proxy now triggers an immediate check that tells the administrator why single sign-on fails.
20261018-12: Add: in Artica SMTP, A new SMTP protocol hardening page protects against SMTP smuggling, using the strongest protection the installed Postfix release supports and the official workaround on older releases.
20261018-12: Add: in Artica SMTP, The SMTP protocol hardening page controls command pipelining: unauthorized pipelining is rejected and the PIPELINING and CHUNKING extensions can be withdrawn from the EHLO reply.
20261018-12: Fix: in Artica, A RDS Proxy session pattern set to disconnect now really ends the session and shows the reason to the user, instead of only reporting it.
20261018-12: Add: in Artica Proxy, The HaCluster Windows console can take a node out of Active Directory emergency mode, after a confirmation explaining that its proxy currently lets everyone through without authentication.
20261018-12: Fix: in Artica Proxy, A Kerberos helper that reads the keytab while it is being rewritten no longer switches the proxy into Active Directory emergency mode.
20261018-12: Fix: in Artica Proxy, The Active Directory emergency mode caused by an unreadable keytab is now lifted automatically once the keytab is valid again.
20261018-12: Fix: in Artica Proxy, In an HaCluster, the nodes no longer alternate every three minutes between two different Kerberos keytabs, which reloaded the proxy twenty times per hour.
20261018-12: Fix: in Artica Proxy, The Active Directory emergency state of the cluster master is no longer replicated to the other proxies.
20261018-12: Add: in Artica Proxy, A node in Active Directory emergency mode can now be returned to normal authentication from the HaCluster nodes page.
20261018-12: Add: in Artica SMTP, A new Per-client limits page caps how many connections, messages and recipients one client address may submit per minute, including hosts of the trusted networks.
20261018-12: Add: in Artica SMTP, A new Volume alerts page warns when one client address submits an unusual volume of mail and when a provider such as Microsoft 365 or Gmail starts rate-limiting the server.
20261018-12: Add: in Artica, Trusted networks can now be declared in IPv6 and are honoured by the IPv6 firewall rules.
20261018-12: Add: in Artica, Country-based firewall rules now also apply to IPv6 traffic when the GeoIP database provides IPv6 ranges.
20261018-12: Add: in Artica, The firewall packet tester now evaluates IPv6 packets.
20261018-12: Fix: in Artica, Adding an IPv6 trusted network in the console no longer stores an empty network address.
20261018-12: Add: in Artica, The Service Pack update now displays a percentage while checking file integrity, while installing files and while compressing the backup.
20261018-12: Fix: in Artica, A corrupted Service Pack is now rejected before any file is replaced, so the system is never left partially patched.
20261018-12: Add: in Artica Proxy, Web-filtering database downloads now resume where they stopped after a network cut, instead of starting over, which makes large categories such as Malwares update reliably on slow or unstable links.
20261018-12: Add: in Artica, The RDS Proxy pattern detection now reads window titles on Windows 10, Windows 11 and Windows Server 2016 and later.
20261018-12: Fix: in Artica Compilator, Stopping the build daemon during a kernel module rebuild no longer sends a false failure report, and the interrupted rebuild is retried as soon as the daemon restarts instead of a day later.
20261018-12: Add: in Artica, The firewall now filters IPv6 with the same rules and interface policies as IPv4; each rule can apply to IPv4, IPv6 or both, and IPv6 filtering is enabled on update once the administrator confirms it.
20261018-12: Fix: in Artica Proxy, The HaCluster source-IP distribution rules page now says that a rule name is already used instead of showing an internal error.
20261018-12: Fix: in Artica Proxy, The HaCluster source-IP distribution rules page can save a rule again when the list of nodes cannot be loaded and the node identifiers are typed by hand.
20261018-12: Add: in Artica Proxy, The HaCluster Windows console has a new Distribution menu to write, order, enable and apply the source-IP distribution rules of the load balancer, with a confirmation listing the rules before HAProxy reloads.
20261018-12: Fix: in Artica Proxy, Applying the source-IP distribution rules from the HaCluster Windows console reports whether the load balancer accepted the new configuration, and refuses rules targeting nodes that do not exist.
20261018-12: Add: in Artica Proxy, The node dialog of the HaCluster Windows console is split into a Proxy tab (traffic and service) and a System tab (CPU load, load average and memory of the node).
20261018-12: Add: in Artica Proxy, The node dialog of the HaCluster Windows console shows live charts of traffic, requests, CPU load, load average, memory and proxy clients, updated at each refresh.
20261018-12: Add: in Artica, Published servers (destination NAT) can now be reached from the internal network with their public address (NAT reflection), enabled by default and adjustable per publication.
20261018-12: Add: in Artica, Firewall objects can now hold host names, resolved every 5 minutes so that a rule follows the addresses of a partner's site or service.
20261018-12: Add: in Artica, The firewall rules list now shows when each rule was last used, and flags rules unused for 30 days or hidden by a rule placed above them.
20261018-12: Add: in Artica, The firewall can automatically ban, for a configurable time, sources outside trusted networks whose packets to the appliance are rejected too often, with a list of banned addresses and an unban button.
20261018-12: Add: in Artica Proxy, The HaCluster Windows console shows the proxy nodes as tiles; clicking a node opens a dialog with its traffic, cache, service times, resources and versions.
20261018-12: Add: in Artica Proxy, The HaCluster agent of each proxy node now sends to the load balancer, every minute, the proxy metrics already collected on the node, so the HaCluster Windows console can display them.
20261018-12: Add: in Artica Proxy, The HaCluster Windows console program and window now carry the Artica web console icon.
20261018-12: Add: in Artica Proxy, The HaCluster Windows console shows the nodes running in Active Directory emergency mode with the same red label as the web console.
20261018-12: Add: in Artica Proxy, The HaCluster Windows console has a new Settings menu that shows, read only, a summary of the general parameters of the load balancer.
20261018-12: Fix: in Artica Proxy, Node operations performed from the HaCluster Windows console are recorded in the administrators journal under the same conditions as every other administration operation, and name the certificate holder.
20261018-12: Fix: in Artica Proxy, The events journal of the HaCluster Windows console no longer overlaps the event code with the node name.
20261018-12: Add: in Artica Proxy, The HaCluster Windows console is now available in every language of the Artica web console: French, English, German, Spanish, Italian, Polish, Portuguese and Brazilian Portuguese.
20261018-12: Fix: in Artica Proxy, Empty rotated web-filtering log files are now purged automatically, instead of piling up by the hundreds of thousands in the log directory.
20261018-12: Fix: in Artica, A disabled Dynamic DNS agent no longer leaves the system monitor trying to start it every minute and a half.
20261018-12: Fix: in Artica Proxy, A leftover IDS monitoring rule from an earlier version is now removed when the IDS is disabled, instead of failing to start the IDS every minute and a half.
20261018-12: Fix: in Artica Proxy, Re-enabling a load-balancing node that was disabled now puts it back into service even when source-based routing rules still use it.
20261018-12: Fix: in Artica Proxy, A load-balancing node put back into service without restarting the load balancer is no longer reported down by its health checks until the next reload.
20261018-12: Fix: in Artica, The firewall events page no longer shows a wrong date (such as the 6th instead of the 16th) for firewall log lines written after the 9th of the month.
20261018-12: Fix: in Artica, Reloading or sharing the address of the firewall interface connectors page now opens that page instead of the network interfaces page.
20261018-12: Add: in Artica Proxy, A new "HaCluster Windows console" page issues certificates that let a Windows workstation supervise the load-balancing cluster in real time and drain, disable, take out of service or re-enable its nodes, and nothing else.
20261018-12: Add: in Artica, The firewall can reject and log traffic routed between interfaces when no connector allows it; published NAT services, replies and WireGuard tunnels stay allowed.
20261018-12: Add: in Artica, Firewall rules can carry a description and be grouped into collapsible sections.
20261018-12: Add: in Artica, An Accept firewall rule can limit the simultaneous connections and the new connections per second or per minute of each source address.
20261015-17: Fix: in Artica, Network addresses are configured right at boot again instead of up to two minutes later, which could make services bound to an address fail to start.
20261015-17: Fix: in Artica, Services that were marked as enabled but never started at boot because of a broken activation link now start automatically.
20261015-17: Add: in Artica, Messages held in the mail quarantine are now stored encrypted on disk, and messages stored by previous versions are encrypted automatically.
20261015-17: Add: in Artica RDS Proxy, The two-factor authentication messages shown in the remote desktop session are now displayed in French when the session language is French, unless custom messages are set in the console.
20261015-17: Fix: in Artica, GlusterFS bricks and mounts now come back by themselves after a reboot or a brick crash instead of staying offline until a manual restart.
20261015-17: Fix: in Artica, The /etc/hosts file no longer accumulates duplicate entries for the server name, and a damaged file is now repaired automatically within five minutes.
20261015-17: Add: in Artica, The mail quarantine can now hold messages whose displayed sender address does not match the sender of the SMTP session, a common sign of impersonation, unless the displayed domain is authenticated by DMARC or DKIM.
20261015-17: Add: in Artica, The firewall can test a packet: give a source, a destination and a port, and see which rule decides, from the rules actually applied.
20261015-17: Add: in Artica, A firewall rule can be temporary: it is disabled automatically when its expiry date is reached.
20261015-17: Add: in Artica, The mail quarantine report can now be sent once a week, every Monday at 08:00.
20261015-17: Add: in Artica, When a user reports a fraudulent message by forwarding it to spam@, the security officer addresses set in the quarantine settings receive an alert with the reported message attached.
20261015-17: Fix: in Artica, Restoring the PowerDNS tables of a snapshot now reports an error when MySQL tools are missing, and the MySQL password no longer appears in temporary scripts or process lists.
20261015-17: Fix: in Artica, Clearing a setting from the command line now really removes its previous value instead of leaving it active.
20261015-17: Fix: in Artica RDS Proxy, After an update of the RDP proxy package, the new version is reported immediately instead of up to six hours later, so the update is no longer offered again.
20261015-17: Fix: in Artica, A system snapshot restore no longer stops at the PowerDNS step when MySQL is not running on the restored node.
20261015-17: Fix: in Artica, After a system snapshot restore, services and the Web console use the restored settings immediately instead of the previous ones until the next restart.
20261015-17: Fix: in Artica, Restoring a system snapshot no longer uninstalls the OpenLDAP directory service when it is enabled, and reinstalls it when the snapshot has it enabled.
20261015-17: Fix: in Artica, A firewall change saved at the same moment as the periodic configuration check now always waits for your confirmation instead of being kept automatically.
20261015-17: Fix: in Artica, A firewall rollback that cannot complete now applies what was restored, is retried at most three times and is reported once, instead of sending a notification every minute.
20261015-17: Add: in Artica RDS Proxy, The two-factor enrollment screen now shows a QR code to scan with the authenticator app, the key remains displayed for manual entry.
20261015-17: Fix: in Artica, Deleting a snapshot stored in Azure Blob storage from the snapshots page now removes it from the container instead of failing with "No FILE".
20261015-17: Add: in Artica, The remote snapshot storage settings (NAS or Azure Blob) are now replicated to the cluster slave nodes.
20261015-17: Fix: in Artica, Restoring a system snapshot no longer stops at the PostgreSQL step when tables are linked by foreign keys, such as the mail gateway tables.
20261015-17: Add: in Artica, The firewall keeps the history of its configuration: you can compare two versions and restore a previous one.
20261015-17: Add: in Artica, A firewall change must now be confirmed within a few minutes, otherwise the previous configuration is restored automatically, so a wrong rule can no longer lock you out.
20261015-17: Add: in Artica, The Rspamd anti-spam engine can now scan every attachment with ClamAV: infected messages are rejected during the SMTP session and never reach the quarantine.
20261015-17: Fix: in Artica, Messages rejected because of a virus are now listed under the virus category in the mail statistics instead of the blocklist category.
20261015-17: Add: in Artica, System snapshots now include the GlusterFS configuration and restore it on a freshly reinstalled node, never over an existing one.
20261015-17: Fix: in Artica, Snapshots now include the most recent configuration changes, so web filtering rules restored on a new server keep their categories and sources.
20261015-17: Fix: in Artica, Adding, removing or replacing a GlusterFS brick while a rebalance runs is now refused with a clear message instead of an internal error.
20261015-17: Fix: in Artica, The GlusterFS rebalance tab keeps refreshing and keeps its Stop button when one status read fails.
20261015-17: Add: in Artica Proxy, The web portal authentication networks list can now be filled in bulk by pasting many networks at once in an import dialog.
20261015-17: Add: in Artica, The GlusterFS volume page can now rebalance a distributed volume, show its progress and stop it, and offers it after bricks are added.
20261015-17: Fix: in Artica, The GlusterFS rebalance status now reports the files actually moved instead of always showing zero.
20261015-17: Fix: in Artica, Installing or upgrading an add-on package (Synology Active Backup, HAProxy, InfluxDB, python and others) that unpacks files into the system no longer replaces the /bin and /lib directory links with plain folders; on recent Debian releases that could leave the appliance unable to run any command until manual repair.
20261015-17: Fix: in Artica, The HaCluster agent settings page no longer resets the emergency load threshold to 3 when "test every URL" is enabled, which made busy proxies leave the load-balancer every few minutes.
20261015-17: Add: in Artica, A GlusterFS brick can now be replaced from the volume details, for example after a disk failure: the new brick is picked among the server's disks, the volume keeps serving and the self-heal refills it from the other copies.
20261015-17: Fix: in Artica, The HaCluster load-balancer no longer crashes in a loop with HAProxy 3.4.5 and later: the TLS session cache workaround now applies to every affected HAProxy version, not only 3.4.4.
20261015-17: Fix: in Artica, Attaching or renewing the RDS Proxy certificate from the Certificate Center no longer disconnects the open RDP sessions.
20261015-17: Fix: in Artica, Removing the certificate chosen for the RDS Proxy now switches the gateway back to its self-signed certificate instead of keeping the previous one.
20261015-17: Fix: in Artica, The self-signed certificate of the RDS Proxy can now be loaded by the gateway, and the private keys of its certificates are no longer readable by other local users.
20261015-17: Fix: in Artica, Starting the Synology Active Backup agent now removes any snapshot kernel module left over from a previous agent version and rebuilds the module index, so after a Linux kernel update a backup no longer loads an incompatible module and crashes the server.
20261015-17: Fix: in Artica, The RDS Proxy TLS settings, certificate and session options now apply to the next connection as soon as they are saved, instead of waiting for the next service restart.
20261015-17: Add: in Artica, Each network interface linked to the firewall now has an outgoing default policy: with Finally deny all, only the connections accepted by outgoing rules can leave, while replies to established connections keep working.
20261015-17: Add: in Artica, A packet rejected by a Drop firewall rule is now logged with the name of the rule, so the firewall events page shows which rule blocked it instead of Default.
20261015-17: Add: in Artica, The firewall events page has a new Top tab listing the most active rules and the most rejected sources and ports over the last hour, 24 hours or 7 days.
20261015-17: Fix: in Artica, The source networks and excluded destinations of a masquerade entry are now applied and can be edited from the masquerade page; until now all the traffic of the interface was masqueraded.
20261015-17: Fix: in Artica, The packet counters of a firewall rule that logs its traffic no longer count each packet twice.
20261015-17: Add: in Artica, The GlusterFS status page now graphs the space used, the files waiting for self-heal and the connected clients of each volume over a day, a week and a month, and Artica warns when a volume or brick passes 85 % and 95 %, when a brick goes offline and when a self-heal stops progressing.
20261015-17: Fix: in Artica Proxy, The Web-filtering database update now shows the megabytes downloaded for large categories such as Malwares, its progress bar no longer stays at 90% for most of the update, and a download that stops receiving data is abandoned after two minutes instead of blocking the update for up to five hours.
20261015-17: Add: in Artica, A GlusterFS disk wizard lists the blank disks of this server, formats the chosen one in XFS with a single partition, mounts it, creates its brick directory and opens the volume wizard with that brick.
20261015-17: Fix: in Artica, Appliances running a Gold license no longer send the post-installation welcome notification to Artica Tech, so they no longer send any license, statistics or contact data to Artica Tech.
20261015-17: Fix: in Artica, A new RDS Proxy target now defaults to the RDP protocol, and the default error messages shown to refused users are spelled correctly.
20261015-17: Fix: in Artica, Outgoing firewall rules are now applied; until now every new outgoing connection was accepted before reaching them, so an outgoing Drop or Log only rule was shown active but had no effect.
20261015-17: Fix: in Artica, The firewall events page now shows the packets rejected by the firewall and the events of Log only rules, right after an update, and ping events no longer display the ports of the previous event.
20261015-17: Fix: in Artica, The Anti-DDoS option of a network interface, the DNS amplification protection and the Mark packets firewall rules are applied again; private source networks are now only dropped on interfaces set to act as WAN.
20261015-17: Fix: in Artica, Source NAT entries and Route packets to a node NAT entries are applied again by the firewall.
20261015-17: Fix: in Artica, A masquerade entry used by firewall rules now only masquerades the traffic of these rules and respects their exceptions.
20261015-17: Fix: in Artica, Firewall rules using a service whose ports are defined by a variable are applied with the right ports, and a rule whose service has no port is no longer applied to all traffic.
20261015-17: Fix: in Artica, The options, published servers and time restriction tabs of a firewall rule open again, and the time restriction tab no longer accepts malformed input.
20261015-17: Fix: in Artica, The firewall menu no longer shows duplicate entries, its configuration entry is no longer labelled imapd.conf, and the NAT, objects and bandwidth pages no longer display PHP warnings.
20261015-17: Fix: in Artica, The firewall parameters page shows the date of the last configuration in a readable format, and the maximum size of the firewall events log is kept when saved.
20261015-17: Fix: in Artica, The RDS Proxy now applies the handshake timeout, inactivity disconnection, keep-alive, minimum client TLS version, client cipher suites, legacy TLS fallback, ignore-logon-password and disconnect-on-user-change settings of the web console; they were saved but never used.
20261015-17: Add: in Artica, The RDS Proxy settings now offer the interactive login screen option and the option to close refused connections without showing the error, and reject out-of-range timeout values instead of silently ignoring them.
20261015-17: Add: in Artica, The RDS Proxy events page has a new Access events tab listing refused connections and detected patterns with the reason, user, client address and policy, filterable by user and reason.
20261015-17: Fix: in Artica, The RDS Proxy patterns tab now warns that window-title detection only works on Windows 2008 and 2012 targets with the classic theme, not on Windows Server 2016 and later.
20261015-17: Fix: in Artica, Formatting a disk now refuses the system disk, a mounted disk and a disk in use by LVM or RAID before anything is erased, and preparing a GlusterFS disk only proceeds if the disk is still completely blank.
20261015-17: Add: in Artica, The GlusterFS volume wizard now lists the disks of this server: a mounted disk fills the brick path in one click, and a blank disk can be prepared for GlusterFS (formatted in XFS and mounted) from the wizard itself.
20261015-17: Fix: in Artica, A GlusterFS brick is no longer created on the system disk when the disk declared for it in /etc/fstab is not mounted: the request is refused with the mount point to fix.
20261015-17: Fix: in Artica, Formatting a new disk no longer reports a success when the file system could not be created, and a freshly partitioned disk is no longer formatted before the system has made its partition available.
20261015-17: Fix: in Artica, XFS disks can be mounted again on servers where the system optimization had disabled the XFS driver, as soon as GlusterFS is installed or an XFS disk is declared.
20261015-17: Add: in Artica, When the AI assistant proposes to open GlusterFS to a client network wider than /8, such as 0.0.0.0/0, the approval screen now warns that every address in it will reach GlusterFS.
20261015-17: Fix: in Artica, GlusterFS requests refused by GlusterFS itself (volume already existing, brick on the system partition, volume still started) now return a clear refusal instead of an internal error, and deleting a busy GlusterFS mount no longer removes it from the boot sequence.
20261015-17: Fix: in Artica Proxy, Installing the proxy no longer schedules a removed notification script to run every minute.
20261015-17: Add: in Artica, Each RDS Proxy policy can now allow or block the clipboard (each direction and files), drives (read and write), printers, smart cards, serial ports and sound.
20261015-17: Add: in Artica, The RDS Proxy can now disconnect or report a recorded session when a window title matches a pattern, for one policy or for all, with a system notification.
20261015-17: Add: in Artica, The AI assistant can now administer GlusterFS on approval: add or remove a node, create or delete a volume, add bricks, move data off bricks before removing them in a second approval, create or delete a mount and set the firewall client networks, each change proven and undone when possible.
20261014-17: Fix: in Artica, A disk attached while the server is running, such as a virtual disk added to a running virtual machine, now appears on the hard disks page when clicking Refresh, which rescans the disk controllers with a progress bar, without rebooting.
20261014-17: Fix: in Artica, Firewall rules set to log their traffic now actually write it to the system log.
20261014-17: Fix: in Artica, Choosing Azure Blob as the remote storage of snapshots now opens the form where the SAS URL is entered, instead of only reloading the page.
20261014-17: Fix: in Artica, Restoring a snapshot now restores the PostgreSQL data too; the restore used to stop with a "could not translate host name" error.
20261014-17: Fix: in Artica, Backing up and restoring the PostgreSQL database on a remote PostgreSQL server now uses the configured server address.
20261014-17: Add: in Artica, The snapshots list shows the newest snapshot first and tells whether each snapshot is stored on Azure Blob, on the NAS or only on the local disk.
20261014-17: Fix: in Artica, After a snapshot restore, the snapshots list keeps a description for every snapshot, and descriptions show the local time instead of UTC.
20261014-17: Add: in Artica, The RDS Proxy targets tab now shows summary tiles, quick filters, the policies granting access to each target and its NLA mode, and tests each target's connection after the page is displayed, with the measured TCP connect time.
20261014-17: Fix: in Artica, The firewall is no longer rebuilt a second time by an obsolete script at startup and after proxy changes, which could duplicate its rules.
20261014-17: Fix: in Artica, The firewall rules page and the kernel modules list now read their data directly from the Artica service.
20261014-17: Fix: in Artica, The firewall now keeps its protection rules in a fixed order, whatever order the security modules start in.
