20261014-17: Fix: in Artica, The link balancer never balanced any traffic because it relied on a tool that is not installed; it is switched off during the update and can be switched on again from its page.
20261014-17: Fix: in Artica, Reloading the management service no longer runs its 10- and 20-second tasks twice.
20261014-17: Fix: in Artica, A network connector saved by an older version no longer prevents the following connectors from being applied.
20261014-17: Fix: in Artica, Deleting a network connector no longer deletes every global firewall rule.
20261014-17: Fix: in Artica, Network connectors, their masquerade sources and the firewall settings of network interfaces are now checked before being saved and applied automatically, without an Apply button.
20261014-17: Fix: in Artica, Saving a network setting of an interface no longer reverts its firewall settings changed from another page.
20261014-17: Fix: in Artica, Turning masquerading off on a network interface now also stops the connectors and masquerade rules that leave through it.
20261014-17: Fix: in Artica, The IDS interface settings page no longer lets crafted input alter the IDS database.
20261014-17: Fix: in Artica, Saving a CognixSys rule can no longer crash the management service.
20261014-17: Fix: in Artica, Firewall services, bandwidth limits, published addresses and CognixSys rules are now checked before being saved and applied immediately, without an Apply or Compile button.
20261014-17: Fix: in Artica, A firewall service still used by a rule can no longer be deleted.
20261013-17: Fix: in Artica, NAT and masquerade rules are now checked before being saved and applied automatically, without an Apply button.
20261013-17: Fix: in Artica, A NAT rule or a masquerade still used by firewall rules can no longer be deleted, and changing the type of a NAT rule keeps its firewall rules attached.
20261013-17: Fix: in Artica, The destination of a local redirection NAT rule is displayed correctly in the firewall rules page.
20261013-17: Fix: in Artica, Firewall rules, their options, schedules, deep packet inspection protocols and services are now checked before being saved and are applied automatically, without an Apply button.
20261013-17: Fix: in Artica, Deleting a firewall rule no longer leaves its deep packet inspection entries behind.
20261013-17: Add: in Artica, Firewall rules can use the Log only and Return actions, and the rules page shows why a rule cannot be applied.
20261013-17: Fix: in Artica, Firewall rules with the Log or Return action, and rules attached to a masquerade, are now applied instead of being silently ignored.
20261013-17: Fix: in Artica, The firewall watchdog no longer rebuilds the whole firewall when a rule is refused by the kernel; the administrator is notified with the kernel error instead.
20261013-17: Add: in Artica, The firewall rules page shows whether changes are waiting, being applied or applied, and lists the rules refused by the kernel.
20261013-17: Fix: in Artica, Several firewall pages of the web console no longer allow database or system command injection through crafted requests, and they now verify the firewall administrator privilege on the server side.
20261013-17: Fix: in Artica, Firewall rules that send traffic to another gateway (next hop) or to a transparent proxy use the configured port again instead of always falling back to 8080.
20261013-17: Fix: in Artica, Firewall rules defined for all interfaces are no longer copied into every NAT rule, and redirect NAT rules are accepted by the kernel firewall again.
20261013-17: Fix: in Artica, The trusted network is now accepted on the default firewall chain, and rules defined for all interfaces are no longer inserted twice.
20261013-17: Fix: in Artica, The firewall watchdog no longer rebuilds the whole firewall in a loop because of rules whose action cannot be applied (link balancing, log, return, masquerade rules); the administrator is notified instead, and simultaneous rebuilds are now serialized.
20261013-17: Fix: in Artica, Bandwidth limits changed in the traffic shaping page are applied and removed immediately again, including when an entry is deleted.
20261013-17: Add: in Artica, Links in incoming mail are now checked against the Artica cloud categories, short links are followed to their final site and random-looking domains are flagged; a message with a phishing, malware or spyware link is tagged or held in quarantine, and the domains and categories found appear in a new statistics page and in the daily report (Corporate license).
20261013-13: Fix: in Artica, Task progress bars now show the action being performed (restarting, installing, reconfiguring a service…) instead of a generic "Running" title.
20261013-13: Fix: in Artica Proxy, A cluster master no longer publishes a proxy configuration that the proxy itself refuses; the nodes keep the last valid package until the configuration is repaired.
20261013-13: Fix: in Artica Proxy, A cluster node now checks a received proxy configuration before keeping it and restores its previous configuration if the proxy refuses it, instead of losing its workers one by one and being unable to restart hours later.
20261013-13: Fix: in Artica Proxy, A proxy reload is no longer reported as successful when the automatic repair left a configuration the proxy still refuses, and a repaired configuration is now actually loaded.
20261013-13: Fix: in Artica, Phishing sites hosted on website builders such as weebly.com or godaddysites.com are now filed under Phishing, including when the platform carries several categories.
20261013-13: Fix: in Artica, Phishing sites hosted on shared platforms such as vercel.app, github.io or blogspot.com are now filed under Phishing instead of being skipped because the platform itself is already categorized.
20261013-13: Add: in Artica, The categories service now imports the phishunt.io, OpenPhish and PhishTank phishing feeds every 12 hours and files their new, uncategorized domains under Phishing; sites already categorized are left untouched.
20261013-13: Fix: in Artica, On the DNS servers page, the progress bar of a service restart is no longer erased by the automatic status refresh before the task ends.
20261013-13: Fix: in Artica, The quarantine report now tells users to click Release or Receive when it lists newsletters and notifications, matching the button shown on those messages.
20261013-13: Fix: in Artica, The mail quarantine list labels the source of held messages Anti-spam instead of Spam, so a held newsletter is no longer shown as spam.
20261013-13: Add: in Artica, Task progress bars now show a card with the task name, the current step, a large percentage and a clear success or failure state.
20261013-13: Fix: in Artica, The audit service no longer switches the whole appliance to single-user mode when the disk is nearly full: it now suspends audit logging and the appliance keeps running, and an audit service found stopped is started again automatically.
20261013-13: Fix: in Artica, A Service Pack refused during installation because one of its files is missing or corrupted now restores the files it had already replaced and removes its temporary copies, and the files left by an interrupted installation are cleaned up automatically.
20261013-13: Fix: in Artica, Old audit logs are now purged automatically, keeping only the two most recent archives, instead of accumulating in /var/log/audit until the disk is full.
20261013-13: Fix: in Artica, The RDS Proxy now reads its generated configuration, so users are no longer refused with "authentication service unavailable" at the login screen.
20261013-13: Fix: in Artica, The RDS Proxy login screen now applies the logo and colors chosen in the login page template and shows the Artica logo by default instead of the Wallix one.
