20261011-17: Add: in Artica, The AI assistant can search, create, edit and delete OpenLDAP accounts and their group memberships, always after approval; the password is typed in the approval window and never reaches the model.
20261011-17: Add: in Artica, A deleted OpenLDAP account can be restored within 24 hours with its password, user number and groups.
20261011-17: Add: in Artica, The message window of the Postfix queue was redesigned: delivery diagnostic with the reason for each recipient, size, arrival, encoding and origin, sender and recipient, MIME headers, raw queue content and delivery history, with buttons to retry, hold, release, delete or download the message as an .eml file.
20261011-17: Fix: in Artica, Viewing a queued message no longer runs the message content as code in the console when the message contains HTML, and the queue actions now check the administrator rights of the session.
20261011-17: Fix: in Artica, Changing the Postfix host name on a secondary instance now applies it to that instance instead of the main one.
20261011-17: Fix: in Artica Proxy, Revoked Windows console client certificates are no longer accepted again after the listener or the Artica service restarts.
20261011-17: Add: in Artica, The AI assistant can now report the memory and the goroutines of the Artica API service, explain what consumes its memory and how far it is from an automatic restart.
20261011-17: Add: in Artica, The AI assistant can release the reclaimable memory of the Artica API service after approval, at most once every five minutes.
20261011-17: Add: in Artica LDAP Windows console, On a read-only directory, an account can still be opened to view its details and its groups.
20261011-17: Add: in Artica, The AI assistant can now list the Windows console client certificates and, after your approval, revoke one, lift a revocation, remove a revoked or expired certificate or restart the Windows console listener; it checks each result and never issues certificates or handles their .p12 files, which stay on the LDAP Windows console page.
20261011-17: Add: in Artica, The status tiles of the Active Directory, Kea DHCP, PowerDNS, Memcached, ModSecurity, Nginx firewall, Siege and web-filtering categories pages now use the same tile design as the rest of the console.
20261011-17: Add: in Artica LDAP Windows console, The -help option (also -h, -? and /?) shows a full help on the options, in the language chosen with -lang.
20261011-17: Add: in Artica LDAP Windows console, The program and its windows now carry the Artica Web Console icon.
20261011-17: Fix: in Artica LDAP Windows console, A search typed with stars, such as *dupont*, now finds the same accounts as the plain text.
20261011-17: Fix: in Artica, The OpenLDAP member search treats a star in the searched text as a wildcard instead of looking for a literal star.
20261011-17: Fix: in Artica, After an update installs a new version of the REST API service, the Web Console configuration is now rebuilt automatically so new console pages work immediately.
20261011-17: Add: in Artica LDAP Windows console, The account list shows each account's groups instead of its job title.
20261011-17: Add: in Artica, The OpenLDAP member search returns the groups of each member found, in a single directory query per page.
20261011-17: Fix: in Artica LDAP Windows console, Clicking the red cross in the account list now asks to delete the account instead of doing nothing.
20261011-17: Add: in Artica, The AI assistant can attach a certificate of the certificate center to a service (web console, proxy SSL decryption ports, OpenVPN, OpenLDAP, DNSDist, RDP proxy, FTP, HotSpot, Proxy PAC, DoH proxy, web filtering error page, Nagios, repository mirror) after your approval: it reloads only that service, checks that the new certificate is really served, and puts the previous web console certificate back automatically if you do not confirm the change in time.
20261011-17: Fix: in Artica, The Previous and Next buttons of the LDAP Windows console now refresh every line of the account list instead of only the last one.
20261011-17: Add: in Artica, The LDAP Windows console can log out and forget its certificate, then import another one without being restarted.
20261011-17: Add: in Artica, The LDAP Windows console edits group membership in a list with a Browse button that searches the groups of the organization, instead of a text field.
20261011-17: Add: in Artica, The display name of a directory account can now be changed after creation, from the LDAP Windows console and the REST API.
20261011-17: Add: in Artica, The account list of the LDAP Windows console ends with a red cross that deletes the account after confirmation.
20261011-17: Add: in Artica, Every change made to the LDAP directory through the REST API, including from the LDAP Windows console, is now recorded in the administrators audit log with the certificate holder and the workstation address.
20261011-17: Add: in Artica Proxy, The Negotiate authenticator statistics page now shows its period selector and a refresh button in the page header instead of above the charts.
20261011-17: Fix: in Artica, The Enable button of the LDAP Windows console page and its revoke, restore and remove actions now work instead of doing nothing.
20261011-17: Fix: in Artica Proxy, Revoking, restoring or removing a certificate on the Windows console page now works instead of doing nothing.
20261011-17: Fix: in Artica, The LDAP Windows console page now shows certificate dates in a readable format and labels the issue date.
20261011-17: Fix: in Artica, A shared folder that refuses some groups on a file-sharing instance using the local LDAP server now keeps refusing the root account.
20261011-17: Add: in Artica, The translation server now builds the compiled language files itself, so installing a language pack no longer depends on the contents of a directory on the build machine.
20261011-17: Fix: in Artica, A label defined on several pages now takes its value from one explicit rule instead of the order the filesystem happened to return, and a page where the label is still in English can no longer override a page where it is translated.
20261011-17: Add: in Artica, The OpenLDAP cluster tab now lists the replication settings by theme (replication, server mode, client mode), each edited in its own dialog, and the saved password is no longer shown.
20261011-17: Add: in Artica, Parameter lists across the console now use the new tile design: each setting is its own card with a tinted icon, its value in a tag and a discreet edit button.
20261011-17: Add: in Artica, The OpenLDAP server parameters are now grouped by theme: network, directory, security and service.
20261011-17: Add: in Artica, A new LDAP Windows console page under OpenLDAP issues, downloads, revokes and removes the certificates of the LDAP Windows console, can enable its mutual TLS listener, and links to the console download.
20261011-17: Add: in Artica, The daily SMTP report e-mail has a clearer layout, and its list of top refused clients now shows each address with its host name, flagging addresses whose reverse DNS is missing or not confirmed.
20261011-17: Add: in Artica, The LDAP Windows console now follows the Windows display language (French or English, English for any other language) and accepts a -lang switch to force it.
20261011-17: Fix: in Artica, The French texts of the LDAP Windows console are now written with their accents.
20261011-17: Fix: in Artica, The DKIM private keys generated for the Artica milter signing rules are now readable by the system administrator only; keys created by earlier versions are restricted the next time the milter loads them.
20261010-17: Fix: in Artica, The sender challenge and its answer are now signed with the DKIM key of the Artica milter rule for the quarantine release domain (or its parent domain), so they are no longer sent unsigned on appliances that sign mail with the Artica milter.
20261010-17: Add: in Artica, A wizard creates a file-sharing instance and a shared folder that use the local LDAP server, and enables that server if needed.
20261010-17: Fix: in Artica, Members of the local LDAP directory can now sign in to file-sharing instances that use this directory.
20261010-17: Fix: in Artica, The LDAP Windows console now opens its windows instead of failing at startup with "a dialog box could not be displayed".
20261010-17: Fix: in Artica, The mail quarantine and the sender challenge no longer show as active while the Rspamd quarantine score does not let Rspamd hold any message; the console now says which setting to change.
20261010-17: Fix: in Artica, Installing a Service Pack no longer leaves its extracted files behind, which used about 800 MB of disk space after each update.
20261010-17: Fix: in Artica, A Service Pack is no longer installed when the disk does not have room for it; the update stops with a message naming the partition instead of filling the disk.
20261010-17: Fix: in Artica, The statistics database no longer receives two simultaneous start attempts from the monitor and the watchdog.
20261010-17: Fix: in Artica, When the statistics database cannot start because the disk is full, the event now says so instead of only reporting that the service did not come back.
20261010-17: Add: in Artica, A database whose first bytes were overwritten by another program's traffic is now detected and restored exactly, on its own, at startup and every five minutes; the web filtering rules are then rebuilt so they apply again.
20261010-17: Fix: in Artica, The database recovery tool can now salvage a database whose header was damaged, which it previously reported as not being a database.
20261010-17: Fix: in Artica, A database restored by the recovery tool is no longer left readable by every local user.
20261010-17: Add: in Artica, The AI assistant can now renew a Let's Encrypt certificate on its own before it expires, at most once a day per certificate, reload the web console and the reverse-proxy sites that use it, and check that the new certificate is really served.
20261010-17: Add: in Artica, The appliance now exposes a paginated directory search over every searchable attribute, so a remote console can find an account by e-mail address, telephone number or UID without downloading the directory.
20261010-17: Add: in Artica, The mutual-TLS gateway now limits a certificate to the part of the API its rights name: a directory certificate reaches the LDAP routes only, and a proxy certificate everything else.
20261010-17: Add: in Artica, The appliance now tells a directory client when it is a replication consumer, so a remote console refuses changes that the master would silently overwrite instead of letting them disappear.
20261010-17: Fix: in Artica Proxy, Issuing a Windows console certificate with no right selected is now refused, because such a certificate was granted the whole administration API.
20261010-17: Add: in Artica Proxy, The Windows console certificate page can now grant the LDAP directory right, which opens the Artica LDAP Windows console and cannot be combined with a proxy right.
20261009-17: Fix: in Artica, The sender challenge e-mail is now signed with the appliance's DKIM key, so the sender's mail provider no longer files it as spam or rejects it.
20261009-17: Add: in Artica, The AI assistant can now create a root authority, a server certificate signed by it or a signing request, complete that request with the signed certificate and delete an unused certificate, each change being verified and undoable, while private keys never leave the appliance.
20261009-17: Fix: in Artica, Settings written to an additional Postfix instance outside a full reconfiguration are now applied to that instance instead of failing silently.
20261009-17: Fix: in Artica, The queue count shown for an additional Postfix instance in the OAuth status is now read from the right instance.
20261009-17: Fix: in Artica, Deleting a Postfix instance now also removes its trusted networks and milter rules created from the console.
20261009-17: Fix: in Artica, The regular-expression rewriting preview now rejects an invalid pattern on recent Postfix versions instead of accepting a rule that Postfix ignores.
20261009-17: Fix: in Artica, A file-sharing instance that uses the local LDAP server as its members database now starts and serves files instead of restarting in a loop.
20261009-17: Fix: in Artica, Learned-correspondent bypasses no longer reveal the other recipients of a message in its headers.
20261009-17: Add: in Artica, The mail quarantine can challenge unknown senders: the sender of a clean, authenticated message receives an image code and their message is delivered as soon as they reply with it.
20261009-17: Add: in Artica, A sender who answers the challenge correctly becomes a legitimate correspondent of the recipient and is never challenged again.
20261009-17: Add: in Artica, Messages whose sender does not answer the challenge in time, or types wrong codes, move to the ordinary quarantine report instead of being lost.
20261009-17: Add: in Artica, A new Challenges tab in the quarantine shows open challenges and lets administrators release the messages or close a challenge.
20261009-17: Add: in Artica, Every sender challenge event is sent to Artica SIEM in the mail filtering stream.
20261009-17: Add: in Artica, The AI assistant now reads the real certificate center: inventory, expiry dates, private key consistency and which services use each certificate, without ever seeing a private key.
20261008-17: Add: in Artica, Replies from people your users wrote to are no longer quarantined or rejected as spam when their sender is authenticated; automatic replies, mailing lists and bulk sends are never learned.
20261008-17: Add: in Artica, Administrators can exclude domains or addresses from correspondent learning and see, user by user, which correspondents were learned.
20261008-17: Add: in Artica, Every quarantine event (held, released, blocked, deleted, purged) and every message let through by a learned correspondent is sent to Artica SIEM.
20261008-17: Fix: in Artica, Header rules defined in the SMTP rules console now take effect.
20261008-17: Add: in Artica SIEM, New mail-filtering event family with search and top views.
20261008-17: Fix: in Artica, Hosts in a trusted network are no longer banned by CrowdSec, whatever the order in which the firewall rules were applied.
20261008-17: Fix: in Artica, A trusted network written with a /14 or /6 dotted netmask no longer stops the loading of the trusted networks list, which silently left the following networks untrusted.
20261008-17: Fix: in Artica, Refreshing the trusted networks no longer removes the per-interface trusted rules and the IP reputation whitelist until the next firewall reconfiguration.
20261008-17: Fix: in Artica, The trusted networks list is now replaced atomically, so trusted hosts are never briefly exposed to blocking rules during a refresh.
20261008-17: Fix: in Artica, A new version of the Artica REST service is now picked up within a minute instead of several, including when the service is failing to start, and a version that does not answer after the upgrade is rolled back automatically.
20261008-17: Fix: in Artica Reverse Proxy, The watchdog no longer mistakes one of the daemon's helper processes for the daemon itself, which could leave a stopped daemon unattended or stop the wrong process.
20261008-17: Fix: in Artica Reverse Proxy, The WordPress inbound firewall list now really blocks the listed addresses; its rule referenced the wrong address list and never matched any connection.
20261008-17: Fix: in Artica Reverse Proxy, Rebuilding the web server firewall no longer duplicates all of its rules each time; the rules are now replaced in a single step.
20261008-17: Fix: in Artica Reverse Proxy, Stopping the web server firewall no longer rewrites the whole system firewall.
20261008-17: Fix: in Artica, With the firewall and the web server firewall both enabled, the per-interface web server filtering rules are no longer rejected at each firewall reconfiguration.
20261008-17: Fix: in Artica, The CrowdSec and SSH brute-force firewall rules are now installed in a single step, so one rejected rule can no longer leave the protection half-built.
20261008-17: Fix: in Artica, CrowdSec and SSH brute-force bans now block IPv6 attackers too; IPv6 addresses could never be added to their blacklists and were never filtered.
20261008-17: Fix: in Artica, Removing firewall rules (VPN, masquerade, mirroring, transparent proxy, CrowdSec, SSH, HAProxy) no longer rewrites the whole firewall, so rules added at the same moment by other services are no longer lost.
20261008-17: Fix: in Artica, CrowdSec firewall rules are applied immediately after a firewall reconfiguration instead of up to three minutes later.
20261008-17: Fix: in Artica, SSH brute-force protection now works when the SSH server listens on more than one port.
20261008-17: Fix: in Artica, The firewall no longer creates a stray ":DIVERT" chain each time it is reset.
20261008-17: Fix: in Artica, The firewall scripts generated for OpenVPN remote sites no longer contain a malformed forwarding rule.
20261008-17: Add: in Artica, The firewall now reports whether the system uses the nf_tables or the legacy iptables backend.
20261008-17: Fix: in Artica, The web console no longer fails with a PHP error when one of its backend include files was installed with an owner the web server cannot read; the daemons now give it back to the web server automatically.
20261008-17: Fix: in Artica, SMTP authentication against Active Directory now uses the selected directory connection; it silently fell back to the local LDAP server.
20261008-17: Fix: in Artica, The "Ask Artica AI" link moved from the top bar to the right-hand actions panel, so the top menu no longer breaks when many services are installed.
20261008-17: Fix: in Artica, The "Verify recipients on target server" option of an SMTP route now really refuses mail for unknown recipients; it was ignored until now.
20261008-17: Add: in Artica, An SMTP route can now validate its recipients in Active Directory, so mail for an address that does not exist is refused during the SMTP session instead of bouncing to a forged sender.
20261008-17: Fix: in Artica Reverse Proxy, A Let's Encrypt request by the AI assistant that fails before anything is ordered is now reported as refused rather than failed, and the whole request is bounded by its declared time limit.
20261008-17: Fix: in Artica Reverse Proxy, A Let's Encrypt certificate requested by the AI assistant is no longer ordered for a site without an HTTPS port, and the automatic renewal no longer orders a duplicate of a certificate still being issued.
20261008-17: Fix: in Artica Proxy, The memory pools setting is no longer overwritten with the memory limit each time the proxy configuration is built.
20261008-17: Fix: in Artica Proxy, The proxy configuration file is now replaced in one step, and two reconfigurations never run at the same time: a proxy process could stop on a half-written configuration line.
20261008-17: Fix: in Artica Proxy, HyperCache no longer uses refresh options that the proxy reports as obsolete.
20261008-17: Fix: in Artica Proxy, An empty memory cache mode no longer writes an invalid line in the proxy configuration, and a low disk usage mark above the high mark is no longer accepted.
20261008-17: Add: in Artica Proxy, The cache level page was redesigned: its settings are grouped in cards, each group is edited in its own dialog, values are checked before saving, and options given by the cache level are shown apart from the ones chosen by the administrator.
20261008-17: Fix: in Artica Proxy, The cache level and the freshness options now really reach the proxy: the default refresh rule never carried them, so the low, medium and strong cache levels behaved the same.
20261008-17: Fix: in Artica Proxy, In multi-CPU mode, the Caches Center no longer marks every disk cache as unsupported: only a cache assigned to a process the proxy does not run is, and the message gives that process.
20261008-17: Fix: in Artica, The web console reads again which settings exist since they became readable by the system only: the cache status page showed no cache, proxy actions were missing, and some settings were reset to their default value on each page.
20261008-17: Fix: in Artica Reverse Proxy, Let's Encrypt certificates requested by the AI assistant now get a name no other certificate can share, one request runs at a time, a failed request leaves no certificate behind, and the request is refused when Let's Encrypt is set to use port 80 itself, which would stop the reverse proxy.
20261007-17: Fix: in Artica Proxy, With several proxy workers (multi-CPU mode), the caches of the Caches Center are used again: each disk cache goes to the worker it is assigned to, rock caches are shared by all workers, and the cache status page no longer reports them as not supported.
20261007-17: Add: in Artica Reverse Proxy, The AI assistant can now request a Let's Encrypt certificate for a published site and attach it after approval; the request waits for the certificate, never deletes an existing one, and the attachment can be undone.
20261007-17: Fix: in Artica, Free disks offered for a proxy cache or a btrfs volume now include SSD and NVMe disks, such as virtual disks on an NVMe controller.
20261007-17: Fix: in Artica Proxy, The new cache disk wizard lists the free disks again: it relied on a disk scan that no longer exists and never found any disk.
20261007-17: Fix: in Artica Proxy, Adding a cache folder now applies the configuration right away: the folder used to show as active while the proxy never stored anything in it until the configuration was applied by hand.
20261007-17: Fix: in Artica Proxy, The button that temporarily disables or enables caching in the proxy Actions window now works: it used to open a page that did not exist.
20261007-17: Fix: in Artica, A translated label is no longer lost from the web console when the label registered just before it has no text at all.
20261007-17: Add: in Artica Reverse Proxy, The AI assistant can now enable or disable the web application firewall of a published site, choose its detection or blocking mode, add or remove a rule exception, and attach an existing certificate, after approval; every change is checked before it is installed and can be undone.
20261007-17: Fix: in Artica Proxy, The button that pauses or resumes HyperCache deduplication in the proxy Actions window now works: it used to open a page that did not exist.
20261007-17: Fix: in Artica Proxy, The HyperCache rule restore route now refuses rule identifiers far beyond those of the table, which could have blocked every later rule addition.
20261007-17: Fix: in Artica Proxy, Undoing a HyperCache rule change no longer reports a failure when an Artica update added a new default rule in the meantime.
20261007-17: Fix: in Artica Proxy, The AI assistant now refuses at once to enable a HyperCache rule that the deduplication helper bans, instead of failing after a timeout.
20261007-17: Fix: in Artica Proxy, A HyperCache deduplication rule that the AI assistant writes in place of an Artica default rule now takes the exact place of that default rule in the evaluation order.
20261007-17: Add: in Artica, Quarantine report recipients can release and allow a sender, or block it, directly from their report; allowed senders are delivered at once only when their identity is authenticated.
20261007-17: Add: in Artica, Users can forward a message as an attachment to spam@ or white@ on the release domain to block or allow its sender, and optionally train the anti-spam engine.
20261007-17: Add: in Artica, Messages released from quarantine carry who released them and when, with an optional warning banner that is never added to signed or encrypted mail.
20261007-17: Add: in Artica, The quarantine console can release or delete up to 50 messages at once and manage every user's allowed and blocked senders.
20261007-17: Add: in Artica Proxy, The AI assistant can now add, change, enable, disable, reorder and remove HyperCache deduplication rules after an administrator approves it, and proves that the proxy loaded them.
20261007-17: Add: in Artica Proxy, HyperCache refuses deduplication rules that could let one website take the cached content of another.
20261007-17: Add: in Artica Reverse Proxy, The AI assistant can now add, modify, drain, restore and delete the backends of a published site after approval; every change is checked by nginx before it is installed and can be undone.
20261007-17: Fix: in Artica, DNS Firewall queries on the DNS root no longer produce a warning in the daemon log.
20261007-17: Fix: in Artica, The hardware information sent with the license request is read correctly again instead of failing with an invalid data error.
20261007-17: Fix: in Artica, The certificate database is migrated to case-insensitive certificate names on appliances installed with the original schema, which also stops a warning repeated hundreds of times a day.
20261007-17: Fix: in Artica, The deprecated Tailon service no longer leaves a monitoring rule behind that relaunched it every two minutes.
20261007-17: Add: in Artica, The AI assistant can now enable, disable, pause and resume HyperCache deduplication after an administrator approves it, with an automatic return to the previous setting if the proxy rejects the change.
20261007-17: Fix: in Artica Reverse Proxy, A temporary error while reading the sites database no longer deletes the configuration of every published site.
20261007-17: Fix: in Artica, The memory watchdog of the Artica daemon now runs even when the system is overloaded, so a daemon whose memory use overloads the appliance is restarted instead of staying stuck.
20261007-17: Fix: in Artica, The DNS Firewall statistics are saved to the database again every 10 minutes; their in-memory buffer was never emptied and grew by hundreds of megabytes, which made the Artica daemon consume excessive CPU.
20261007-17: Add: in Artica Reverse Proxy, The AI assistant can now create, modify, enable, disable and delete published sites after approval; every change is checked by nginx before it is installed and can be undone.
20261007-17: Fix: in Artica, The Artica daemon no longer burns several CPU cores in continuous memory garbage collection when its memory usage reaches its internal ceiling; it now hands over to the memory watchdog instead.
20261007-17: Add: in Artica, The AI assistant can now apply HyperCache and take it out of its emergency mode, refusing while the cause is not fixed and putting the emergency back when the helpers do not start.
20261007-17: Fix: in Artica, A change of the super-administrator credentials no longer leaves them in clear text in a file of the web console; a file left by an earlier version is deleted when the service starts.
20261007-17: Fix: in Artica, The REST API no longer lets an account overwrite the authentication link of another account.
20261007-17: Add: in Artica Reverse Proxy, The AI assistant can now report the availability and SLA of the reverse-proxy backends, the WAF events of a published site and the expiry of the certificates the sites really serve.
20261007-17: Fix: in Artica, The appliance console screen now advertises the web interface address of the network card it actually listens on, instead of the first detected card.
20261007-17: Fix: in Artica, Only the super-administrator session can now change the super-administrator name or password; any other logged-in account was able to do it.
20261007-17: Fix: in Artica, A console account can no longer overwrite the authentication link of another account.
20261007-17: Fix: in Artica, A quarantine release reply that the anti-spam filter finds suspicious is now processed instead of being held in the quarantine itself.
20261007-17: Add: in Artica, The quarantine report e-mail now has a clearer layout, with a Release button for each message and a short explanation of how to release one.
20261007-17: Fix: in Artica, Messages released or deleted from the quarantine console now record the administrator who did it.
20261007-17: Add: in Artica Reverse Proxy, The AI assistant can now reload, start, restart and stop nginx, restart the reverse-proxy daemon and rebuild a published site, each change being checked on the real service; reload, start, restart and a site rebuild can run on their own when allowed.
20261007-17: Add: in Artica, The AI assistant can now read the real state of HyperCache (why it is inactive, helper version and updates, helpers running, emergency mode and when it can be left) and its deduplication rules.
20261007-17: Fix: in Artica Proxy, The Squid cache manager is now strictly loopback-only, closing cache-purge and manager-info access from any non-local address.
20261007-17: Add: in Artica Reverse Proxy, The AI assistant now reads the real state of nginx, the published sites, their backends, nginx memory and the configurations nginx refused.
20261007-17: Fix: in Artica Reverse Proxy, The AI assistant no longer reports the reverse-proxy status as unavailable, and its backend connectivity test now uses the backends declared for the published sites.
20261007-17: Add: in Artica, The AI assistant now knows how HyperCache works (deduplication, emergency mode, engine updates, troubleshooting) and can explain it in the chat.
20261007-17: Fix: in Artica, The AI assistant now picks the documentation that matches the question, including the relevant passage, instead of three arbitrary documents.
20261007-17: Fix: in Artica, The maintenance tasks that run every five minutes (proxy watchdogs, HyperCache engine update, log and service checks) no longer start five minutes late.
20261007-17: Add: in Artica, Messages scored as probable spam can now be held in a quarantine instead of being rejected, and each user receives a periodic report of their held messages.
20261007-17: Add: in Artica, Users can release a quarantined message by replying to their quarantine report; the reply must come from their own mailbox.
20261007-17: Add: in Artica, Administrators can list, download, release and delete spam and DLP quarantined messages from a single page.
20261007-17: Fix: in Artica Proxy, HyperCache is now configured by the Artica daemon: a configuration refused by the proxy is rolled back instead of being kept, and an updated HyperCache engine is now really used, because its processes are restarted after the update.
20261007-17: Fix: in Artica Proxy, HyperCache no longer gives the same cache key to every image that has a query string or to every jQuery version, which could make the proxy serve one site's image or script in place of another's.
20261007-17: Fix: in Artica Proxy, HyperCache now checks domain names in the host part of the address only, so a crafted address on another site can no longer have its content stored under the cache key of Microsoft, Windows Update or another trusted source.
20261007-17: Fix: in Artica Proxy, HyperCache no longer merges the cache of different customers of shared CDNs (CloudFront, Amazon S3, Akamai, Blogspot) and no longer deduplicates web pages or API answers, only static files.
20261007-17: Fix: in Artica Proxy, The HyperCache helper no longer stops on a short or malformed request or on a Netflix image, which made Squid restart it and drop the requests it was handling.
20261007-17: Add: in Artica Proxy, The HyperCache helper now uses about 40 times less CPU, no longer depends on the memcached service, and ignores invalid rules with a log line instead of producing wrong cache keys.
20261007-17: Fix: in Artica, A proxy member of a load-balancing cluster no longer reports every hour that the cluster DNS service uninstall was aborted, and no longer resets the DNS relay order pushed by its load-balancer.
20261007-17: Add: in Artica, The hard disk details dialog has been redesigned with tabs for hardware, partitions with their usage, SMART health and live disk activity, plus direct SMART test, disconnect and close buttons.
20261007-17: Add: in Artica, The web console now checks on the server that an account holds the privilege of a page before accepting a change from it; this first version only records the attempts it would refuse, so that the rules can be checked before they are enforced.
20261007-17: Fix: in Artica, The web console no longer rebuilds PHP objects from data sent by the browser, which closes a way for a logged-in user to delete files on the appliance.
20261007-17: Fix: in Artica, The "Ask Artica AI" entry of the top bar is now a text link and no longer overlaps the CPU gauge: when the bar is too crowded for the screen width, it now wraps onto two lines.
20261007-17: Fix: in Artica SIEM, Echelon IP reputation lookups are now sent in full batches under hourly and daily budgets that respect the provider's 2,000 requests per day limit.
20261007-17: Add: in Artica SIEM, New Echelon tag blocklists source: the threat lists are downloaded once an hour and matched locally instead of querying each address.
20261006-17: Add: in Artica, The hard disks page now shows one card per drive with its usage, mount points, SMART health and temperature, plus summary tiles and type, state and sort filters.
20261006-17: Fix: in Artica Proxy, Emptying a cache from the caches center now stops the proxy before erasing its content and never erases a directory that is not a proxy cache.
20261006-17: Fix: in Artica Proxy, The "Analyze caches" task of the stored objects page works again and can be scheduled daily from its settings.
20261006-17: Fix: in Artica Proxy, Disabling the proxy cache feature no longer stops with an internal error before restarting the proxy.
20261006-17: Fix: in Artica, The "empty" button of the reverse-proxy caches center is removed: it emptied the proxy cache that had the same number instead of the reverse-proxy cache.
20261006-17: Fix: in Artica Proxy, Cache usage figures, cache emptying, the new cache disk wizard and the stored objects analysis are now performed by the Artica daemon instead of separate background scripts.
20261006-17: Fix: in Artica Proxy, Enabling or disabling HyperCache dedup no longer fails with "failed to open /run/squid/squid.pid": the proxy is reloaded even when its PID file was lost, and started when it was not running.
20261006-17: Fix: in Artica Proxy, The caches center now manages disk caches through the Artica daemon: names with quotes no longer break the save, deleted caches are reliably marked for removal, and the order arrows keep a consistent order.
20261006-17: Fix: in Artica Proxy, The caches center shows the real usage percentage of each disk cache instead of a permanent 0%.
20261006-17: Fix: in Artica Proxy, Changing the outgoing interface of the internal port in the listening ports page no longer fails with "invalid id": the ports rebuild, check and reconfigure actions were no longer reachable.
20261006-17: Fix: in Artica, The AI assistant now carries out the cluster node operations allowed in its Autopilot list, such as disabling a node, instead of only proposing them for approval.
20261006-17: Fix: in Artica, The Autopilot list only offers skills that can really run without an administrator, shows for each one whether it runs at every pass or only when the assistant decides, and warns that a restart allowed this way is repeated every 10 seconds.
20261006-17: Fix: in Artica, The Autopilot no longer runs proxy configuration changes other than reload and cache purge, nor any operation of risk level 3 or above, even when they are listed.
20261006-17: Fix: in Artica, The AI assistant's answers now state which actions the Autopilot carried out or refused, instead of a fixed advisor-mode notice.
20261006-17: Fix: in Artica Proxy, The DNS service of the load-balancer gave its health checks only 3 milliseconds instead of 3 seconds, so after a reboot it marked every proxy DNS cache as down (red DNS status) and stopped answering.
20261006-17: Fix: in Artica, Saving the Web console settings (such as the XSS protection) no longer fails with "Could not find configuration" when the console uses its default certificate; the certificate is only checked when it is changed.
20261006-17: Fix: in Artica Proxy, On the load-balancer status page, the back-end servers tile now shows its listener and server count in a readable colour instead of white text on a light background.
20261006-17: Fix: in Artica Proxy, After a reboot, the load-balancer cluster service no longer stays bound to the local loopback when the network comes up late, which left every node stuck in synchronisation with a connection refused.
20261006-17: Fix: in Artica Proxy, On a load-balancer that serves DNS for the farm, the DNS cache page and the features list now show the HaCluster DNS service that really answers, instead of a disabled DNS cache with an install button.
20261006-17: Add: in Artica, The installation ISO now installs the iw and wpasupplicant tools so that a wireless network card can be configured on the installed system.
20261006-17: Add: in Artica, The DNS network restrictions list uses the new table design, shows the built-in private ranges as defaults and only offers deletion to DNS administrators.
20261006-17: Fix: in Artica Proxy, On a load-balancer that serves DNS for the farm, installing the local DNS cache is now refused with an explanation, instead of being installed and removed a few seconds later while DNS was briefly cut.
20261006-17: Fix: in Artica, The S.M.A.R.T. disk page now displays a proper "Wear" column title instead of a raw placeholder.
20261005-17: Add: in Artica, The SMART daemon page shows the service status on the left and its self-test schedule as a configuration card on the right; clicking that card opens the schedule settings.
20261005-17: Add: in Artica, The Your Networks page (firewall whitelist) has a redesigned table with searchable rows, status pills for trusted, VPN and DNS, action icons and summary cards for IDS, ARP discovery and access control.
20261005-17: Fix: in Artica, Reading disk health no longer closes files belonging to other tasks of the system daemon, which could leave disk pages and other requests waiting forever.
20261005-17: Fix: in Artica, NVMe disks now report their temperature in degrees Celsius instead of Kelvin, and unmounted partitions no longer show the size and usage of an unrelated system filesystem.
20261005-17: Add: in Artica, The storage management page now opens a detailed window for each disk: health, temperature, power-on time, wear, bad sectors and kernel I/O errors as tiles, full identity and SMART fields, and every partition with Mount and Unmount buttons.
20261005-17: Fix: in Artica, The storage management page now shows its "Format disk" button and its SATA command queuing (NCQ) settings in plain language instead of raw placeholders.
20261005-17: Fix: in Artica, The storage management page no longer shows "daemon unreachable" every few seconds: when a disk scan is slow the previous values stay on screen, flagged as such, while the scan completes.
20261005-17: Fix: in Artica Proxy, When the load-balancer serves DNS for the farm, its DNS service no longer uninstalls itself after a reboot while the proxies have not reported yet, which left the load-balancer without any DNS answer.
20261005-17: Fix: in Artica, Toggling a notification rule option can no longer be abused to alter an arbitrary column of the console database, and editing an existing rule now refreshes the list after saving.
20261005-17: Add: in Artica, The notification rules and notification events tables now use the modern table design, with a search box on the events list.
20261005-17: Fix: in Artica, The Network traffic analysis page now explains why the module is unavailable in proxy or HA cluster mode instead of showing a raw placeholder.
20261005-17: Fix: in Artica Proxy, Names that only exist because a workstation appended the local search domain (such as speed.cloudflare.com.yourdomain) are no longer sent to categorization, which wasted a lookup on every occurrence.
20261005-17: Add: in Artica Proxy, The proxy now warns when a DNS server used by the proxy or by the Web filtering engine does not answer, and says so explicitly when that address is a parent proxy.
20261005-17: Add: in Artica Proxy, The Internet access check of the load-balancer can be disabled from the HaCluster client settings.
20261005-17: Add: in Artica, Red, orange, grey, green, blue and cyan status tiles across the console now use a light tinted design with a watermark icon, coloured title and matching buttons; the green follows the appliance brand colours.
20261005-17: Add: in Artica, The System information page now shows the logo of the detected hypervisor (VMware, Hyper-V, XenServer, Nutanix, VirtualBox, KVM/QEMU, AWS, Google Cloud), and XenServer virtual machines get their picture again.
20261005-17: Add: in Artica, Service status cards across the console now use the same clean white design as the SMTP service status page, with real memory history bars and the appliance brand colours.
20261005-17: Fix: in Artica Proxy, The Wazuh events settings dialog is now translated into French.
20261005-17: Fix: in Artica, Installing or uninstalling a feature from Your System > Features now asks for confirmation before starting, so an accidental click can no longer launch the task.
20261005-17: Add: in Artica Proxy, Proxy access events can now be written to a JSON file collected by a local Wazuh agent, either in full or limited to security-relevant events.
20261005-17: Fix: in Artica, The request simulation page works again after a Service Pack upgrade: the check runs inside the Artica service instead of an external program, and a report is shown even when one of the DNS servers tested does not answer.
20261005-17: Fix: in Artica, Creating a DNS Firewall rule with the web browsing protection, web browsing cleaning, SafeSearch or Active Directory offloading wizard no longer fails with an "invalid json" error.
20261005-17: Add: in Artica, The progress of hotfix and Service Pack installations now shows the extraction percentage while the archive is being uncompressed.
20261005-17: Fix: in Artica, The progress bar of a software installation now follows the package download, with the amount already downloaded, instead of staying still until the download ends.
20261005-17: Fix: in Artica Proxy, Applying the Central Cache (Rock Store) settings is now performed by the Artica daemon: the proxy is restarted only when the Rock Store is created or resized, and a disabled Rock Store is removed from disk only if it really is a proxy cache directory.
20261005-17: Add: in Artica Proxy, The Central Cache (Rock Store) page now shows live proxy performance (requests and bandwidth served from cache, cache response time, Rock Store fill) and presents the Rock Store settings as clear capacity tiles.
20261005-17: Add: in Artica Proxy, The caching status page shows each disk cache as a card with its usage gauge, free space, partition and format, followed by the partitions holding the caches and the total cache capacity in the header.
20261005-17: Fix: in Artica Proxy, The caching status page no longer shows every disk cache as "Waiting": the usage of each cache is displayed again.
20261005-17: Fix: in Artica, The network interfaces page no longer keeps warning that network bridges were created when gateway mode is forced off and no bridge exists.
20261005-17: Fix: in Artica Proxy, A disk cache removed from the caches center now frees its disk space, including caches created by the wizards on additional disks; a directory that is not a proxy cache is never erased.
20261005-17: Fix: in Artica, Links to the DNS records page can no longer inject scripts into the console through the record type or a cached name.
20261005-17: Fix: in Artica, Restart and reconfiguration buttons of the DNS pages now require the DNS administrator privilege.
20261005-17: Fix: in Artica, DNS cache pages now say that Artica must be updated when its REST service is too old, instead of showing a raw error.
20261005-17: Fix: in Artica Proxy, The "Apply configuration" button of the disk caches center works again: caches are rebuilt, new cache directories created and the proxy restarted by the Artica daemon.
20261005-17: Fix: in Artica Proxy, Enabling or disabling HyperCache and changing the cache level now reload the proxy instead of restarting it.
20261005-17: Fix: in Artica AI, Disk cache changes made by the assistant now create the new cache directories before the proxy restarts.
20261005-17: Fix: in Artica, The DNS servers panel now requires the DNS administrator privilege for every change, saves only its own settings after checking them, and restarts the local DNS cache only on an explicit action.
20261005-17: Add: in Artica, The REST API can set a TSIG key typed by the administrator on a local domain, keeping the DHCP server aligned, checking it is really served and allowing the change to be undone, without ever writing the key in a log or a reply.
20261005-17: Fix: in Artica, DNS cache settings changed in the console (cache, security, DNS over TLS and HTTPS, interfaces, EDNS, Redis, SafeSearch) are now validated, checked by the DNS cache and rolled back if refused, and only DNS administrators can change them.
20261005-17: Fix: in Artica, DNS policy zones (RPZ) created, changed, reordered, enabled, disabled, refreshed or deleted in the console are now checked and applied by the DNS cache before being kept, and the DNS filtering whitelist page now fills the DNS cache whitelist and shows what it cannot override.
20261005-17: Fix: in Artica, Local DNS domains created, enabled, disabled or deleted in the console are now applied at once and checked by the DNS cache, and a domain that still holds records is no longer deleted with them silently.
20261005-17: Add: in Artica, The local DNS domains page generates TSIG keys inside the DNS cache, keeps the DHCP server key aligned, and shows only the key fingerprint, whether it matches the DHCP server and whether the DDNS agent runs.
20261005-17: Fix: in Artica, DNS forward zones created, changed or deleted in the console are now validated and applied at once by the DNS cache, and groups of domains, transparent and DNSSEC zones are saved safely and reloaded after each change.
20261005-17: Fix: in Artica, DNS cache records changed in the console are now validated, applied at once and checked by the DNS cache before being kept.
20261005-17: Add: in Artica, The AI assistant can list the DNS policy zones (RPZ) of the DNS cache and, after approval, add, change, reorder, enable, disable, refresh or delete them and manage the DNS whitelist, never on its own, and every such change except a list refresh can be undone.
20261005-17: Fix: in Artica, The scheduled refresh of DNS policy zones (RPZ) can no longer install a list that blocks the appliance itself, nor leave a list the DNS cache refused on disk where the next reload would stop the service.
20261005-17: Fix: in Artica, Removing the last DNS policy zone (RPZ) no longer stops the DNS cache.
20261005-17: Add: in Artica, The REST API can create, change, reorder, enable, disable and delete DNS policy zones (RPZ) of the DNS cache, checks each change with the DNS cache before applying it, and undoes it otherwise.
20261005-17: Fix: in Artica, The DNS filtering whitelist is applied again by the DNS cache: its entries had no effect since the DNS cache replaced the former filtering service.
20261005-17: Add: in Artica, The SMTP service status page has a new layout showing the deferred queue, the queue watchdog state, the main refusal causes and the Artica reputation switches at a glance.
20261005-17: Fix: in Artica, The dynamic DNS agent now starts with its current engine version: its configuration used an option that version no longer accepts, so dynamic DNS updates from the DHCP server were never served.
20261005-17: Fix: in Artica, A local domain with dynamic DNS updates now loads when the dynamic DNS agent listens on all addresses: its zone lacked the address of its own name server and was refused.
20261005-17: Add: in Artica, The AI assistant can enable dynamic DNS updates on a local domain and rotate its TSIG key after approval, without ever seeing the key, and a domain removal it performs can now be undone.
20261005-17: Fix: in Artica, On a DNS cluster slave the AI assistant no longer changes DNS cache settings that the next synchronisation would overwrite: it names the master and its console where to make the change.
20261005-17: Add: in Artica, Two Enterprise-license options use the Artica IP reputation service to exempt servers rated good from greylisting, the RBL Pack and the DNSBL lists (your own access lists still apply) and to refuse servers rated bad at connection time.
20261005-17: Add: in Artica, The former "Artica Tech RBL" option of the IP reputation page is replaced by the Artica reputation tile of the Postfix status page; appliances that had it enabled must switch the new options on from that tile.
20261005-17: Add: in Artica, The Postfix status page shows an Artica reputation tile with the number of servers allowed and blocked over the last 24 hours.
20261005-17: Fix: in Artica, A server whitelisted by the Artica reputation is no longer rejected by the RBL Pack or the DNSBL lists before the whitelist is checked.
20261005-17: Fix: in Artica, Messages accepted thanks to the Artica reputation are no longer counted as refused messages in the mail statistics.
20261005-17: Add: in Artica, The REST API can enable dynamic DNS updates on a local domain, generate a new TSIG key for it while keeping the DHCP server aligned, and undo a key change or a domain removal.
20261005-17: Fix: in Artica, Importing a reverse-proxy backup now requires the Web master privilege and only accepts a file that was really uploaded.
20261005-17: Fix: in Artica Reverse-Proxy, Restoring a configuration backup can no longer run a system command hidden in the backup file name, and importing, restoring, downloading or deleting a backup can no longer reach any file outside the backup and upload directories.
20261005-17: Fix: in Artica, The backup restore and image install task links refuse file names carrying shell characters, the website check of the proxy troubleshooting refuses IPv6 addresses it cannot test, and two simultaneous uploads with the same name can no longer overwrite each other.
20261005-17: Fix: in Artica, Uploaded files whose name contains spaces, parentheses or accents are accepted again by the keytab, legal logs and category imports, and the wifi and cluster node log pages can no longer be used to run system commands.
20261005-17: Fix: in Artica, A delegated administrator can no longer run system commands through the progress tasks of the Web console (log download, export, wifi scan, cluster node sync, imports and certificate tasks): every value is checked and passed to the system as plain data.
20261005-17: Fix: in Artica, The model server settings of the AI appliance now explain each value, and the page warns when the context length is too short for the Artica AI assistant.
20261005-17: Fix: in Artica, The progress page of the initial setup wizard can no longer be used without authentication to stop the firewall or restart the end of the installation, and it does nothing at all once the wizard has been completed.
20261005-17: Add: in Artica, The server card of the system information page now uses a light design and draws each physical drive with its type, size and current temperature.
20261005-17: Fix: in Artica, The task links of the Web console (service restarts, configuration builds and their progress bars) are now signed for the session that displayed them, so a crafted or altered link can no longer run a task or inject script, even for a logged-in administrator.
20261005-17: Add: in Artica, The system information page shows the manufacturer logo of physical servers (Dell, HP, Lenovo, Supermicro, Fujitsu, Cisco and other common brands).
20261005-17: Add: in Artica, Questions asked to the Artica AI assistant in the Web console terminal no longer stop after 5 minutes: the answer is prepared in the background and shown as soon as it is ready.
20261004-17: Add: in Artica, The system information page has been redesigned: summary cards for processor, memory, system and network, a server card showing the manufacturer and model of physical machines, and grouped sections for hardware, operating system and security options.
20261004-17: Add: in Artica, The hardware inventory now also reports the chassis type, serial number and BIOS version of physical servers.
20261004-17: Fix: in Artica, A remote RPZ server can no longer inject configuration into the DNS cache through its category index, and a remote policy list the DNS cache would refuse is no longer installed.
20261004-17: Fix: in Artica, The Artica AI assistant no longer reports a running proxy service as stopped because of a misleading field name in the service status.
20261004-17: Add: in Artica, The disk I/O metrics page has been redesigned like the system metrics page: summary cards with the most active process, a period selector in the header including 30 days, and chart cards for system activity, top processes and per-process history.
20261004-17: Fix: in Artica, A DNS policy zone (RPZ) can no longer inject configuration into the DNS cache or write files outside its folder, and a policy the DNS cache would refuse is no longer installed.
20261004-17: Fix: in Artica, The secret of a DNS dynamic update key is no longer written in clear text in the administration journal nor displayed again in the local domains page.
20261004-17: Fix: in Artica, Dynamic DNS updates of a local domain can no longer be enabled with an empty or default TSIG key, and only DNS administrators can change local domains.
20261004-17: Fix: in Artica, The DNS policy zones (RPZ) page refuses a name, file, address or CNAME that could alter the DNS cache configuration, and only DNS administrators can change the remote RPZ service or download a policy.
20261004-17: Add: in Artica, The system metrics page has been redesigned: four summary cards (database, CPU and memory, collector status, load average), a period selector in the header and one chart card per metric.
20261004-17: Add: in Artica, On physical servers, the disk health tools (smartmontools) are now installed automatically so that disk self-tests and disk failure detection work without manual setup.
20261004-17: Add: in Artica, The Artica AI assistant answers much faster with an AI appliance: it prepares the model when it starts and keeps it ready every 10 minutes, and its instructions are now reused from one question to the next instead of being read again each time.
20261004-17: Fix: in Artica, The Artica AI assistant now accepts small formatting slips of local language models instead of ending the investigation with a protocol error.
20261004-17: Fix: in Artica, The AI appliance now keeps its model in memory for 7 days by default, so the first question after a quiet weekend no longer waits for the model to reload.
20261004-17: Fix: in Artica, The installation ISO now always ships the latest Debian 13 kernel fetched during its build, instead of an older kernel left over from a previous build.
20261004-17: Add: in Artica, The installation ISO now carries every Debian 13 firmware package in its most recent version (backports included), so the installer and the installed system recognize recent network and storage hardware.
20261004-17: Fix: in Artica, The AI appliance now serves its model with a 32768-token context by default, so the investigations of the Artica AI assistant no longer end in a protocol error because their instructions were cut.
20261004-17: Fix: in Artica, The AI appliance status page now shows the host name, the IP addresses and the port to enter on the client appliances, matching the fields of their quick connection.
20261004-17: Fix: in Artica, The Artica AI status page now shows a connection to an AI appliance of the network as such, instead of the remote language model warning.
20261004-17: Fix: in Artica, The Artica AI assistant now reads the proxy cache manager counters instead of reporting this check as failed.
20261004-17: Fix: in Artica, The Artica AI language model settings now explain why the provider refuses to list its models (no API key saved yet, or the saved key was refused) instead of a bare HTTP 401.
20261004-17: Add: in Artica, The SMART monitoring page now detects failing disks that SMART reports as healthy: on physical machines it watches link resets, command timeouts, kernel read and write errors, file system errors and file systems switched to read-only every 5 minutes, and still sends an urgent alert by e-mail and to the SIEM when the system disk can no longer write.
20261004-17: Add: in Artica, The disk usage analyzer was redesigned: cards and a banner show the size, free space, reserved space and inode usage of the file system being browsed, with warnings at 85% and 95%.
20261004-17: Add: in Artica, The disk usage analyzer lists the file system type, permissions, owner and last modification date of every folder, and flags mount points and folders deleted since the scan.
20261004-17: Fix: in Artica, A disk usage scan now starts from the folder entered in the scan dialog instead of always scanning the whole system.
20261004-17: Fix: in Artica, Folder names containing quotes no longer break the navigation of the disk usage analyzer.
20261004-17: Fix: in Artica, The Nagios agent (NCPA) now starts again when its own process identifier file was left empty or corrupted, instead of refusing to start forever.
20261004-17: Fix: in Artica Proxy, A proxy without load-balanced parent proxies no longer has its parent load-balancing service restarted endlessly by the monitoring.
20261004-17: Add: in Artica, The storage page can disable SATA command queuing (NCQ) on a disk that freezes on queued commands; the option only appears when the disk supports it and the kernel log shows failures, applies immediately and is kept at every boot.
20261004-17: Add: in Artica AI, The assistant now reads the SATA command queuing state of each disk and recommends disabling it when a disk freezes on queued writes, the usual cause of a system partition switching to read-only while SMART reports no error.
20261004-17: Add: in Artica, The SMART monitoring page can now install and run the smartd service: on physical machines it checks every disk every 30 minutes, runs a daily short and a weekly long self-test, and reports new disk errors and failing sectors as Artica notifications without repeating alerts already sent by the hourly SMART check.
20261004-17: Fix: in Artica, The Activity tab of the AI appliance page shows the last request as a plain date and time, and labels authorized clients as allowed.
20261004-17: Fix: in Artica, The header buttons of the AI appliance page match the selected tab: New client no longer stays on the Status, Settings and Activity tabs.
20261004-17: Fix: in Artica, The services status reports the installed version of the AI appliance model server instead of 0.0.0.
20261004-17: Fix: in Artica, The remaining time of a download on the AI appliance page reads like ~2 min instead of 2m0s.
20261004-17: Fix: in Artica, The PostgreSQL watchdog now restarts the database through the lightweight service launcher, so repeated restart attempts can no longer pile up and exhaust memory when the system disk becomes read-only.
20261004-17: Fix: in Artica, DNS-over-TLS and DNS-over-HTTPS can now be enabled on the DNS cache: the generated configuration placed their options inside a forwarding zone, so the DNS cache refused it.
20261004-17: Fix: in Artica, Enabling DNS-over-TLS or DNS-over-HTTPS on the DNS cache with a certificate that does not exist in the certificates center is now refused before anything is written.
20261004-17: Fix: in Artica, When the DNS cache refuses a new setting and puts the previous values back, the AI assistant now says so instead of reporting that nothing was changed.
20261004-17: Fix: in Artica, During the installation of the AI appliance, the remaining time shown after a network interruption is computed from the moment the download resumes, instead of including the pause.
20261004-17: Fix: in Artica, The file sharing service no longer tries to restart the host Samba services every few seconds when the appliance has no host Samba configuration, and it waits longer between attempts when a Samba service keeps failing to start.
20261004-17: Add: in Artica, The language model settings of the AI assistant offer a quick connection to an Artica AI appliance (LocalIA): enter its address, port and certificate authority, and the endpoint, model, timeout and certificate are set in one save.
20261004-17: Fix: in Artica Proxy, The nightly re-categorization of proxy statistics no longer reports an error for a recorded website name that is not a valid host name.
20261004-17: Fix: in Artica Proxy, The proxy log helper no longer stops the proxy when its event queue directory cannot be created or its statistics module fails to start; it keeps the proxy running and recovers on its own.
20261004-17: Fix: in Artica, Storage changes made by the AI assistant are now refused when they could not be undone the same way (unmounting a hand-made mount, turning swap off while other swap is off), are followed even when the launch request times out, and long changes show their target and progress text.
20261004-17: Fix: in Artica, The AI appliance opens its service to the other appliances only once the model is installed, instead of as soon as the installation reaches the service setup.
20261004-17: Fix: in Artica, During the installation of the AI appliance, the download bar now says when no data has been received for a while instead of showing its last speed, and it no longer goes back when a part of the model is downloaded again.
20261004-17: Fix: in Artica Proxy, After a boot where the load-balancer started before its network address was ready, the HaCluster status no longer stays in error once the service runs; the load-balancer also waits for its listening addresses before starting.
20261004-17: Fix: in Artica, The Nagios agent (NCPA) is no longer restarted every minute and a half by the monitoring while it is running; its process is now found whatever its version.
20261004-17: Add: in Artica, The output of the Nagios agent (NCPA) at startup is now kept in a log file, included in the support package, to diagnose an agent that does not start.
20261004-17: Add: in Artica, The support package now includes the Nagios agent (NCPA) logs and process identifier files, to diagnose an agent that the monitoring keeps restarting.
20261004-17: Fix: in Artica, The su command no longer loses its setuid bit every few minutes, which made it unusable for non-root administrators part of the time.
20261004-17: Fix: in Artica, The firewall no longer rebuilds its trusted-network and Artica access rules every few minutes because it could not recognize its own rule.
20261004-17: Fix: in Artica, The firewall no longer adds a new copy of the loopback rule at each check; existing duplicates are removed automatically.
20261004-17: Fix: in Artica, Emptying the swap is skipped when the free memory cannot absorb it, instead of triggering the out-of-memory killer.
20261004-17: Fix: in Artica, The Suricata IDS now runs in its own system group: when it runs out of memory, it no longer causes the Artica service to be stopped.
20261004-17: Fix: in Artica, The SSH authorized keys of Active Directory accounts no longer fail to get their owner group every few minutes.
20261004-17: Fix: in Artica Proxy, Applying a change in the HaCluster status page no longer restarts the load-balancer twice; the configuration is reloaded only when it really changed.
20261004-17: Fix: in Artica Proxy, When the load-balancer serves DNS from the farm, notifying the nodes no longer installs then removes the local DNS cache each time.
20261004-17: Fix: in Artica Proxy, The HaCluster DNS relay can no longer be started twice at the same time.
20261004-17: Fix: in Artica Proxy, The logs of the HaCluster DNS relay are no longer rejected by the system logger at startup.
20261004-17: Fix: in Artica Proxy, The HaCluster load-balancer no longer fails to open its administration socket at boot.
20261004-17: Fix: in Artica Proxy, Cluster slave proxies no longer keep the master's outgoing address after a replication, which made their internal web requests fail and could set them down.
20261004-17: Fix: in Artica Proxy, Saving a setting with an unchanged value no longer reloads the Web filtering connector; on cluster proxies this happened three times every two minutes.
20261004-17: Fix: in Artica Proxy, The HaCluster real-time requests view no longer shows the category of the previous request on a request without category.
20261004-17: Fix: in Artica Proxy, The HaCluster backends page no longer logs missing include warnings.
20261003-17: Fix: in Artica Proxy, The proxy log helper no longer stops the proxy when it cannot read its settings file; it waits, discarding log lines, and resumes on its own once the file is readable again.
20261003-17: Add: in Artica, New versions of the software packages managed by Artica are now listed in a single "Artica packages" table under Update, where each one can be updated, ignored or restored.
20261003-17: Add: in Artica, The notification bell shows one "You have x packages managed by Artica to update" entry instead of one entry per package, and it comes back when a new version is published.
20261003-17: Fix: in Artica, The Docker new-version notice no longer reports the DNS cache service version under the name of the Zabbix agent.
20261003-17: Add: in Artica, An approved AI transaction that was not executed yet can now be cancelled from the transaction history.
20261003-17: Add: in Artica, The "AI appliance" page shows what to enter on the client appliances and offers its certificate authority as a file to download.
20261003-17: Add: in Artica, The "AI appliance" page lets an administrator allow client appliances by address or network, change the HTTPS port and the model server settings, and see the requests received by address.
20261003-17: Add: in Artica, The local AI server is published over HTTPS to the other Artica appliances, only to the addresses an administrator allows, with a certificate authority of its own.
20261003-17: Add: in Artica, Installing the AI appliance removes the Artica AI client from the same machine, and the client can no longer be installed there.
20261003-17: Add: in Artica SIEM, A new ClickHouse storage page shows where the statistics database keeps its data and can move it onto a dedicated empty disk, with an automatic rollback on failure.
20261003-17: Fix: in Artica Proxy, The cluster configuration package no longer carries the proxy log helper settings of the master: on the receiving proxies the helper could no longer read them and the proxy service restarted in a loop.
20261003-17: Fix: in Artica Proxy, Installing or updating the eCAP antivirus module no longer crashes the running proxy: its library was rewritten twice, in place, while the proxy was using it.
20261003-17: Fix: in Artica, Saving a DNS policy zone (RPZ) can no longer alter other policies through a crafted value, and only DNS administrators can change these policies.
20261003-17: Fix: in Artica Proxy, Installing the categories service no longer renumbers personal categories used by Web filtering rules or ACL objects, which silently stopped blocking them; the installation is refused with the list of references to remove, and unused categories are renumbered safely.
20261003-17: Add: in Artica, The DNS policy zones (RPZ) table uses the new table design, with every action on the right of each row.
20261003-17: Fix: in Artica, Changing the order of the DNS policy zones (RPZ) now rebuilds the zones immediately.
20261003-17: Fix: in Artica, Enabling a DNS policy zone (RPZ) that has a download error no longer shows it as active.
20261003-17: Fix: in Artica Proxy, Uninstalling the Web filtering service no longer deletes the contents of a databases folder moved to another disk through a symbolic link; the folder and the link are kept for a later reinstallation.
20261003-17: Fix: in Artica Proxy, The HA cluster agent no longer garbles error messages containing a percent sign when a local service call fails.
20261003-17: Fix: in Artica Proxy, The Statistics page opened from the HaCluster menu now shows its title header and buttons.
20261003-17: Fix: in Artica Proxy, The ranking and legend tables of the proxy statistics dashboard now show their column headers.
20261003-17: Fix: in Artica Proxy, With "Do not test the web sites", the load-balancer itself no longer contacts outside sites either: it only checks that each proxy port and its own port answer.
20261003-17: Fix: in Artica, The preview of multi-line text fields in forms no longer shows "<br>" instead of line breaks.
20261003-17: Add: in Artica Proxy, The AI assistant can put Web filtering into emergency mode and take it out after approval, and proves on the proxy itself that filtering stopped or resumed.
20261003-17: Add: in Artica Proxy, The REST API can turn Web filtering emergency mode on and off and proves that the proxy really stopped or resumed filtering.
20261003-17: Fix: in Artica Proxy, Enabling the Go Shield connector no longer disables the Web filtering service.
20261003-17: Fix: in Artica Proxy, The connector emergency mode is no longer overwritten by the normal configuration.
20261003-17: Fix: in Artica Proxy, Turning Web filtering into emergency mode now really disconnects the proxy from the filter.
20261003-17: Fix: in Artica, Building a support package with anonymization enabled is now about fifteen times faster on appliances with large log files.
20261003-17: Fix: in Artica, The anonymized support package now also hides DHCP client identifiers, HAProxy passwords, Samba passwords containing spaces, NTLM and Kerberos authentication tokens, MAC addresses embedded in IPv6 addresses and VLAN-tagged firewall logs, reverse DNS zones, addresses in packet captures and raw binary keys stored in databases.
20261003-17: Add: in Artica, The support package can now be anonymized: IP and MAC addresses are replaced by consistent pseudonyms, passwords, private keys and tokens are removed, and a correspondence table kept on the appliance translates the addresses quoted by the support team.
20261003-17: Add: in Artica SIEM, A new Connection tracking page shows the trends of connection-state logs over time and their breakdown by state, destination port, protocol and server.
20261003-17: Fix: in Artica Proxy, The HaCluster agent no longer asks the proxy to rebuild its authentication settings at every configuration push when Basic authentication is simply not used.
20261003-17: Fix: in Artica Proxy, When all the test URLs must be checked, the HaCluster agent now tests them together and considers the proxy healthy as soon as one answers, instead of waiting for each unreachable site in turn.
20261003-17: Add: in Artica Proxy, A new option of the HaCluster agent lets the cluster proxies stop testing the availability of web sites, so that an unreachable site no longer takes a proxy out of the load-balancer.
20261003-17: Fix: in Artica, Importing a certificate exported from another Artica appliance (certificate and private key in one file) now keeps its private key, so a root certificate is recognised as a root again and can be selected in the HaCluster SSL settings.
20261003-17: Fix: in Artica Proxy, Rebuilding the proxy authentication no longer reloads the proxy every time when the authentication whitelist holds several entries; on cluster nodes this caused a reload about every minute, restarting hundreds of authentication helpers and driving the load very high.
20261003-17: Fix: in Artica Proxy, The DNS servers entered in the HaCluster "DNS used by the farm" settings are now saved; changing the primary or secondary DNS server previously had no effect.
20261003-17: Add: in Artica SIEM, Connection-tracking (conntrack) system logs are now kept in detail for 3 days and summarised per hour and per day, so their trends remain available while they no longer fill the disk.
20261003-17: Add: in Artica, The AI assistant can read and change the DNS cache settings (cache lifetimes, DNSSEC, SafeSearch, EDNS, listening interfaces, DNS-over-TLS and DNS-over-HTTPS, outgoing interface, Redis, DNSCrypt, DNS firewall) after approval; it never opens the resolver to the world, refuses a change that would cut the load-balancer members, and puts the previous settings back when the DNS cache rejects the new ones or does not restart.
20261003-17: Fix: in Artica, Enabling DNS-over-HTTPS on the DNS cache now really works: the service no longer looks for certificate files named after the certificate content, and no longer needs a second certificate that it never used.
20261003-17: Fix: in Artica Proxy, Before installing a new Web filtering configuration, every newly used category database is now checked by the filtering service itself, and the check runs with the proxy user's rights from a protected location, so a damaged or future-dated database can no longer make the service let every request through.
20261003-17: Fix: in Artica Proxy, When the load-balancer serves DNS from the farm, the farm DNS servers can no longer point to the load-balancer itself or to 127.0.0.1; the console refuses them and shows a "DNS loop" warning, and the proxies ignore them, instead of sending every DNS query round in circles between the load-balancer and the proxies.
20261003-17: Add: in Artica Proxy, The AI assistant can create, change, reorder and delete Web filtering rules after approval, and undoes its change when the result cannot be proven.
20261003-17: Fix: in Artica Proxy, A filtering configuration that the Web filtering service would reject is no longer installed, so the service keeps filtering with the previous rules instead of letting every request through.
20261003-17: Add: in Artica Proxy, The REST API can create, change, reorder and delete Web filtering rules for the AI assistant.
20261003-17: Add: in Artica, While it investigates an incident, the AI assistant can add a missing DNS cache record or disable a faulty one without waiting for approval, only for names of the local domains, when the administrator allows it in the Autopilot settings and within a limit of 5 changes per incident.
20261003-17: Fix: in Artica Proxy, When the load-balancer serves DNS, the proxies no longer remove the local DNS cache it relies on, which left every DNS backend down and took all the proxies out of the cluster.
20261003-17: Fix: in Artica Proxy, The HaCluster health agent now tests its URLs through the local proxy service, on the same path as the users, instead of going out directly; an authentication request from the proxy counts as a success.
20261003-17: Fix: in Artica, DNS cache MX and SRV records created in the console are now written in the form the DNS cache accepts; they previously prevented it from loading its configuration. TXT records keep their spaces instead of being split into words.
20261003-17: Fix: in Artica, A disabled DNS cache record or local domain is no longer served.
20261003-17: Fix: in Artica, Removing one DNS cache record no longer stops the other records of the same name from being served.
20261003-17: Add: in Artica, The AI assistant can list and, after an administrator approves the change, add, change, disable or remove local DNS records, local domains and forward zones of the DNS cache.
20261003-17: Fix: in Artica Proxy, The HaCluster health agent on the proxies now uses the list of test URLs defined on the load-balancer instead of always testing the default Internet addresses.
20261003-17: Add: in Artica Proxy, The AI assistant can create personal Web filtering categories, add, remove or move their sites, compile and delete them, after approval, with an automatic undo when the compilation fails.
20261003-17: Add: in Artica Proxy, The REST API can create, fill, compile and delete personal Web filtering categories for the AI assistant, without emptying an existing category or leaving a deleted one behind.
20261003-17: Add: in Artica, The AI assistant can now mount and unmount a data partition, expand a partition, and turn the swap off, on, or remove its partitions, each time after an explicit approval.
20261003-17: Add: in Artica, Changes that cannot be undone are announced as such before they are approved, and long operations show their progress in the history.
20261003-17: Add: in Artica, A new "AI appliance" page checks the hardware, installs the local AI server and shows two progress bars, one for the whole installation and one for the current download or task.
20261003-17: Add: in Artica, The "AI appliance" page shows the state of the local AI server, its measured speed, and lets an administrator restart it, measure its speed again or uninstall it.
20261002-17: Fix: in Artica, When an action run by the AI assistant succeeds with a warning (for example a DNS cache that runs but resolves nothing), the warning is now shown after the execution and in the transaction history instead of being visible only in the transaction files.
20261003-17: Fix: in Artica Proxy, Restarting the Web filtering connector through the AI assistant is now refused for 30 seconds after a GoShield restart, because the proxy reload could stop the GoShield server that had just started.
20261003-17: Fix: in Artica Proxy, A GoShield restart requested by the AI assistant is reported successful only once the new GoShield server answers its API.
20261003-17: Fix: in Artica Proxy, Web filtering operations run by the AI assistant now fail and name the component when another filtering component stopped during the operation, instead of reporting success.
20261003-17: Fix: in Artica Proxy, The AI assistant now warns that an official categories update reporting no change may also mean that every download failed.
20261003-17: Add: in Artica, The AI assistant can restart the Web filtering services, rebuild their configuration and update the official category databases, with a proof of the outcome.
20261003-17: Fix: in Artica, Restricting the Web console to some network interfaces now really takes effect; the console kept listening on every interface, which also prevented the load-balancer error page from starting on the same port.
20261003-17: Add: in Artica, The REST API can restart the Web filtering services, rebuild their configuration and update the official category databases for the AI assistant, and reports the real outcome.
20261002-17: Fix: in Artica SIEM, Searching system logs now ignores case for accented characters too, so "CAFÉ" finds "café".
20261002-17: Fix: in Artica SIEM, Firewall alert rules based on a threshold or a template now record and notify their alerts; they were silently failing to be saved.
20261002-17: Fix: in Artica, The status collector no longer restarts the DNS cache service by itself nor raises a duplicate "service stopped" alert; the Artica daemon is the only watchdog of that service.
20261002-17: Add: in Artica, After the DNS cache service is installed, started or restarted by the AI assistant, a real name is resolved through it; an installation that resolves nothing is removed and reported.
20261002-17: Fix: in Artica Proxy, A whitelist entry changed or removed is now shown at once, instead of the former list being served for a short while.
20261002-17: Fix: in Artica, On an appliance managed by the Debian Agent, the AI assistant no longer installs or removes the DNS cache service locally; this is done from the central console.
20261002-17: Add: in Artica, The appliance can now install a local AI server (Ollama with the Qwen 2.5 model) after checking that the machine is powerful enough, including on virtual machines.
20261002-17: Add: in Artica, The download of the local AI server and of its model resumes where it stopped after a network interruption or a service restart.
20261002-17: Fix: in Artica Proxy, Changing the HaCluster relay port on the master is now applied on every node.
20261002-17: Add: in Artica, The AI assistant can now read the state of the Web filtering services, their events and statistics, the filtering rules and the categories.
20261002-17: Add: in Artica, The REST API now exposes a read-only view of the Web filtering services, rules and personal categories for the AI assistant.
20261002-17: Add: in Artica, The AI assistant can now report the disk inventory, the SMART and RAID health, the swap usage and whether a partition can be expanded.
20261002-17: Add: in Artica, The AI assistant now watches disk space and disk health, and collects a diagnostic when a filesystem fills up or a disk degrades.
20261002-17: Fix: in Artica, The AI assistant no longer offers to approve and execute a plan that only reads information.
20261002-17: Fix: in Artica SIEM, Reverse-proxy, DNS and system metrics batches sent by several appliances are now grouped by the statistics database for up to one second before being written, which reduces disk activity.
20261002-17: Add: in Artica, The DNS cache service can be paused: once stopped on purpose it stays stopped until it is started again or the appliance reboots, instead of being restarted by the watchdog.
20261002-17: Add: in Artica, The AI assistant can read the state of the DNS cache service and what depends on it.
20261002-17: Fix: in Artica Proxy, On HaCluster servers, applying kernel settings no longer reconfigures the network card when its offload features are already enabled.
20261002-17: Fix: in Artica Proxy, The Proxy PAC service events now include the rule builds and the remote PAC synchronizations, which were only written to the system log.
20261002-17: Fix: in Artica Proxy, The Proxy PAC service status now reports the real version of the service instead of 0.0.0.
20261002-17: Add: in Artica, The "Remote terminal" page of the Artica AI section now offers the Windows application "Artica AI Terminal" as a direct download.
20261002-17: Fix: in Artica, Approving an AI plan now executes exactly the plan that was displayed; if a newer answer replaced it meanwhile, the approval is refused.
20261002-17: Fix: in Artica, Creating a HaCluster node with the AI assistant now refuses an address already used by another node and reports certificate or load-balancer warnings.
20261002-17: Fix: in Artica Proxy, Enabling TCP BBR for a HaCluster no longer leaves the console waiting, the setting is applied in the background and its progress is shown.
20261002-17: Fix: in Artica Proxy, The TCP BBR status of a HaCluster node now says when the node agent is too old, instead of showing a synchronization that never ends.
20261002-17: Add: in Artica, A new Windows application, Artica AI Terminal, lets an administrator chat with the Artica AI assistant from a workstation through the remote terminal port, using a workstation certificate and a console account, and it remembers the last connection.
20261002-17: Fix: in Artica Proxy, The built-script view of a proxy.pac rule now shows the PAC actually served, including the copy synchronized from a central server.
20261002-17: Add: in Artica AI, The assistant can now read the Proxy PAC service (state, rules, served script, events, requests and statistics), rebuild the PAC files, synchronize a remote PAC and restart the service.
20261002-17: Add: in Artica, A mounted data partition can now be unmounted from the storage API, which also removes the boot entry created when it was mounted.
20261002-17: Fix: in Artica, Expanding the system partition no longer reports a success when the operation failed.
20261002-17: Fix: in Artica, Mounting a partition no longer fails with an internal error on a filesystem without identifier, and no longer leaves a boot entry behind when the mount fails.
20261002-17: Fix: in Artica, Removing the swap partitions now also removes their boot entries when they are referenced by identifier.
20261002-17: Fix: in Artica Proxy, The HaCluster agent no longer asks the proxy to rebuild its authentication every 35 seconds on clusters that do not use Active Directory.
20261002-17: Fix: in Artica Proxy, When Active Directory authentication is missing on a HaCluster node, the agent now spaces out its repair attempts instead of repeating them endlessly.
20261002-17: Fix: in Artica, A Gold license pushed by the HaCluster load-balancer is now applied on the node, the request was previously refused.
20261002-17: Fix: in Artica SIEM, Proxy and firewall events are now written to the statistics database in batches of a few seconds instead of many tiny writes, which reduces disk activity.
20261002-17: Fix: in Artica Proxy, A HaCluster node whose proxy listen ports carry another node's address is now repaired when its agent asks for it, instead of staying down.
20261002-17: Fix: in Artica Proxy, Rebuilding the proxy listen ports no longer reloads the proxy when nothing changed, and restarts it when a listen address changed.
20261002-17: Fix: in Artica Proxy, The HaCluster agent now reports an error when a repair request is refused by the local service, instead of considering it done.
20261002-17: Fix: in Artica Proxy, Setting a HaCluster node weight to 0 now also stops the node from serving clients through the no-authentication port.
20261002-17: Fix: in Artica, When the AI assistant undoes a HaCluster operation, a node that was draining goes back to draining, an unchanged rule is left untouched, and the cluster capacity checks still apply.
20261002-17: Fix: in Artica, The AI assistant no longer reveals node credentials in error messages when they appear encoded in a request.
20261002-17: Fix: in Artica Proxy, On a cluster slave, proxy listen ports bound to a network interface are now rebuilt with the local address after each synchronization, instead of keeping the address of the master, which made the proxy restart in a loop and the load-balancer see the backend going up and down.
20261002-17: Add: in Artica, A new "Remote terminal" page in the Artica AI section lets an administrator open or close the remote terminal port, choose the addresses allowed to reach it, and issue or revoke one certificate per workstation; each certificate file is delivered once, protected by a password.
20261002-17: Fix: in Artica, On a cluster slave, a replicated table whose data arrives incomplete or invalid is no longer emptied; the previous content is kept until a valid copy is received.
20261002-17: Fix: in Artica, On a cluster slave, DNS forward zones are now restored into the database the DNS cache actually reads, and a restored table always triggers a rebuild of the DNS cache configuration.
20261002-17: Fix: in Artica, Response Policy Zones (RPZ) policies defined on the cluster master are now replicated to the slaves.
20261002-17: Fix: in Artica, On a HaCluster or cluster master that does not publish DNS cache data, the periodic request of each backend no longer logs "cannot open file unbound.json: no such file or directory"; the master now answers that the data is simply not available.
20261002-17: Fix: in Artica SIEM, When the Echelon reputation service answers with a non-JSON error (for example a hosting provider page), the log now shows the reason returned instead of a bare HTTP code.
20261002-17: Add: in Artica, The AI assistant can bring a network interface down or change its address; the change stays provisional and is undone automatically unless an administrator confirms it within five minutes.
20261002-17: Add: in Artica, The AI transactions page shows a countdown and a Confirm button while a network change is waiting for its confirmation.
20261002-17: Add: in Artica, The AI assistant can now check console accounts for its remote terminal: the web console verifies the password, the Artica AI privilege and the two-factor policy on behalf of the AI service.
20261002-17: Fix: in Artica SIEM, Restarting the service no longer reports hourly DNS, system metrics, 404 inventory and reverse-proxy threat summaries as lost when those hours simply had no data.
20261002-17: Fix: in Artica, The AI assistant now requires the permissions of every step of a plan to execute an approved change, not only the right to execute.
20261002-17: Fix: in Artica SIEM, Restarting the service no longer reports threat-detection time slots as lost when they had simply produced no alert.
20261002-17: Add: in Artica, The AI assistant can now propose network changes for approval: rebuild or bring up an interface, start or stop a VLAN, add or remove a static route, and reconfigure the network, each one verified on the real state.
20261002-17: Add: in Artica, The network service can now add or remove a single static route and change the saved address of an interface without rebuilding the whole network.
20261002-17: Fix: in Artica Proxy, Creating a disk cache through the REST API no longer fails with a database error, and the cache size is now read and written by it while older clients keep the stored size.
20261002-17: Fix: in Artica, The AI assistant terminal is now refreshed in the browser right after an update, without having to clear the browser cache.
20261002-17: Add: in Artica Proxy, After approval, the Artica AI assistant can now manage the parent proxies (rules, peers and their credentials typed by the operator), the listening ports and the disk caches of the local proxy, and purge a site or a URL from the cache.
20261002-17: Add: in Artica Proxy, The REST API can now really purge cached objects of a site or a URL, restart the proxy synchronously after a port or cache change, and edit one parent proxy without rebuilding the whole parent list.
20261002-17: Fix: in Artica Proxy, Disabling an ACL object through the REST API no longer enables it.
20261002-17: Fix: in Artica SIEM, The IP reputation engine now reads the stored reputation of observed addresses in one batch per cycle instead of one database query per address, which greatly reduces the CPU used by the statistics database.
20261002-17: Fix: in Artica SIEM, The IP reputation engine no longer rescans the whole list of observed addresses every minute when a threat feed entry merely expires.
20261002-17: Add: in Artica, The AI assistant terminal now shows the answer last and hides the details (facts, checks performed, plan, objects found in the console) unless the new /verbose command is turned on.
20261002-17: Add: in Artica, The AI assistant can now read the system performance (load, CPU, memory, disk speed and disk usage) and the state and throughput of the network interfaces.
20261002-17: Fix: in Artica Proxy, The HaCluster nodes now only accept configuration and orders from the cluster master, authenticated by its certificate, and lock themselves automatically on the cluster authority once the standby load-balancer is upgraded too.
20261002-17: Fix: in Artica Proxy, The HaCluster agent no longer exposes the node private key, Active Directory settings or administrator accounts through its local API.
20261002-17: Fix: in Artica Proxy, The HaCluster master no longer sends its certificate database to the nodes when SSL decryption is enabled.
20261002-17: Fix: in Artica Proxy, Removing a node from the HaCluster farm now really disconnects it.
20261002-17: Add: in Artica Proxy, After approval, the Artica AI assistant can now create, change, enable, move or delete the access rules and ACL objects of the local proxy, its SSL inspection rules and whitelist, and its authentication schemes, each change being checked by reading it back and undone when it fails.
20261002-17: Add: in Artica Proxy, A synchronous proxy reconfiguration (rebuild, check and reload) is available to the REST API and reports its errors.
20261002-17: Fix: in Artica AI, An installation that fails no longer leaves the service marked as installed, so the menu and the Ask ArticaAI button do not appear for a service that is not there.
20261002-17: Add: in Artica AI, An incident now shows its support ticket, and a support ticket can be opened from the incident with a draft that can be edited before sending.
20261002-17: Add: in Artica AI, The number of support tickets the agent may open on its own each day can now be set in the Agent settings.
20261002-17: Fix: in Artica AI, The left menu and the top bar are now refreshed as soon as the service is installed or uninstalled.
20261002-17: Fix: in Artica, The web console no longer fills the PHP log with "Creation of dynamic property" warnings about Docker privileges on every page load.
20261002-17: Fix: in Artica AI, The assistant page no longer fails when an answer lists facts, inferences or hypotheses, and statements the agent could not verify are flagged as such.
20261002-17: Fix: in Artica, The top bar and the left menu no longer fail with an Internal Server Error when checking whether Artica AI is installed.
20261001-17: Fix: in Artica Proxy, Installing a Kerberos keytab no longer writes an unusable /etc/krb5.conf when the Kerberos realm is not set: the realm is taken from the keytab or the domain controller name, and the file is left untouched if it cannot be determined.
20261001-17: Fix: in Artica, The web console no longer fails to start when the system Kerberos configuration (/etc/krb5.conf) is broken or unreadable, since the console does not use Kerberos.
20261001-17: Fix: in Artica, The web console now recovers by itself when its configuration file was locked against changes and no longer allows the console to start, and it reports when a locked configuration prevents settings from being applied.
20261001-17: Fix: in Artica, The web console no longer triggers the nginx warning about the deprecated "listen ... http2" directive on recent versions.
20261001-17: Fix: in Artica Proxy, The Artica AI assistant no longer reports the proxy as stopped when it runs, Artica starting it outside of the squid system service.
20261001-17: Add: in Artica, The AI assistant can now tell whether a given site or address is whitelisted on a cluster node, following the same matching rules as the node proxy, without reading the whole list.
20261001-17: Add: in Artica, The AI assistant page marks the statements that could not be verified against the data read, and lists the names and addresses concerned.
20261001-17: Add: in Artica Proxy, A proxy.pac rule can now download its content from a central PAC server at a configurable interval and keeps serving the last valid copy when that server cannot be reached.
20261001-17: Fix: in Artica Proxy, A malformed website name (with spaces or a percent sign) is no longer sent to the categorization service, where it failed and was logged as a service error.
20261001-17: Fix: in Artica, The AI assistant no longer presents as facts domains or addresses that it never actually read; such statements are checked against what the tools returned and are shown as unverified hypotheses.
20261001-17: Fix: in Artica, The AI assistant no longer drops a question when it asks for two readings at once; the first one is performed.
20261001-17: Add: in Artica, The AI assistant now reports how many whitelist entries and ACL rules a cluster node holds, active or not, even when the list is too long to read in full.
20261001-17: Add: in Artica Proxy, The Artica AI assistant can now read the state, the statistics (top sites, users, bandwidth) and the configuration of the local proxy, and, after approval, add, change or remove whitelist entries and cache exclusions or reload the proxy, each change being checked and undone if it fails.
20261001-17: Add: in Artica, The shared folders of a file sharing instance now offer a "Wizards" button: its first wizard creates a public shared folder, open to everyone in read and write without a password, from a single name.
20261001-17: Fix: in Artica, The AI assistant no longer gives up with a protocol error when its answer about a long list (whitelist, ACL rules) exceeds the length of a single reply; it is asked to answer again, shorter.
20261001-17: Add: in Artica, The AI assistant now accepts a cluster node by its name (proxy1, proxyNoAuth1 or its hostname) as well as by its number.
20261001-17: Add: in Artica, The HaCluster load balancer can now send orders to each node over a new authenticated channel (mutual TLS with the cluster certificates, closed list of operations): node whitelist, ACL rules, ACL compilation and proxy reload.
20261001-17: Fix: in Artica, Reloading the proxies of all HaCluster nodes now really reloads Squid on each node; the previous order targeted a service the nodes never had.
20261001-17: Add: in Artica, The AI assistant can read and change, node by node, the whitelist and the ACL rules of a HaCluster, and edit the replicated ACL groups; each change is checked on the node and undone if its compilation fails.
20261001-17: Add: in Artica AI, Support tickets can now be listed, read, created with the diagnostic package and answered from the assistant, with or without a language model.
20261001-17: Add: in Artica AI, An incident left unresolved by the agent can now open a support ticket on its own when the administrator allows it in the Autopilot.
20261001-17: Add: in Artica, The support portal can now be reached by Artica AI to create a ticket, post a reply and send the diagnostic package.
20261001-17: Add: in Artica, When Artica AI is installed, the search field of the top bar becomes an "Ask ArticaAI" button: the AI terminal answers the question and also lists the matching console objects (computers, proxy objects, DNS records, members...), which open with a click; the /search command searches the console only.
20261001-17: Add: in Artica, The console search now answers directly without a progress bar, groups the results by type, reports the sources that did not answer, and no longer mixes up the results of two administrators searching at the same time.
