20260927-17: Fix: in Artica, The DHCP reservations and leases pages no longer accept search text that could alter their database query, and searching reservations no longer lists computers that have no reservation.
20260927-17: Fix: in Artica, Editing a computer now records its "updated" time in the same time zone as every other change.
20260927-17: Add: in Artica, The DHCP reservations page uses the new table design and flags reservations that the DHCP server does not serve, addresses inside the dynamic pool and duplicate addresses.
20260927-17: Add: in Artica, The DHCP leases page uses the new table design, shows active and expired leases and warns when the list is out of date compared with the DHCP server.
20260927-17: Fix: in Artica, The DHCP "Last computers" and "DHCP requests" pages no longer accept search text that could alter their database query, and show a clear message instead of the raw SQL on error.
20260927-17: Add: in Artica, The DHCP "Last computers", "DHCP requests" and "DHCP events" pages use the new table design, with relative last-seen times, greyed-out computers not seen for 30 days and flagged reassigned addresses.
20260927-17: Add: in Artica, The DHCP events page now pages through every event of the period instead of showing only the latest 250.
20260927-17: Add: in Artica, The DHCP statistics dashboard has been redesigned: six indicator tiles with peak, trend and pool usage, a requests-over-time chart, a message-type breakdown and the most active, most assigned and rejected addresses side by side.
20260927-17: Fix: in Artica, The log storage check no longer loads a whole compressed log in memory when its first line is very long.
20260927-17: Add: in Artica Reverse Proxy, the Docker Relay agent installs its own systemd service with the new install-service command, as the enrollment instructions now say.
20260927-17: Fix: in Artica Reverse Proxy, the Docker Relay pages now show the labels and never-enrolled badges (they were invisible), align the container and backend pickers with the other fields, preselect the only agent when attaching a Docker Relay backend to a web site, and show traffic in the same units as quotas.
20260927-17: Fix: in Artica, The network traffic statistics database is now limited to 1 GB and compacted at startup, so it no longer makes the Artica service restart every few minutes.
20260927-17: Fix: in Artica, The DHCP statistics pages now say that the Artica service is not answering instead of asking to enable the DHCP server.
20260927-17: Add: in Artica, The document search now also finds words from their first three letters (typing "zorg" finds "rapport-zorglub42.txt"), and the search box completes file names as you type.
20260927-17: Add: in Artica, The Docker Manager can open an interactive terminal inside a running container, in its own browser tab, from the containers list.
20260927-17: Add: in Artica, The DHCP statistics now track the occupancy of each DHCP pool over time and display it on the dashboard.
20260927-17: Add: in Artica, The DHCP service now notifies the administrator when a device renews its address in a loop, when a pool is almost full or runs out of free leases, and when many requests are refused.
20260927-17: Fix: in Artica, The Docker containers list no longer shows two columns with the same title.
20260925-17: Add: in Artica, The Wazuh agent is now available as a ready-to-install package for Debian 12 and Debian 13, built from the official Wazuh release and checked against the checksum Wazuh publishes.
20260927-17: Add: in Artica, The Docker Manager lists (containers, images, volumes, networks, sessions, downloads, audit, events, performance) use the new table design.
20260927-17: Fix: in Artica, The Docker Manager descrFiptions are now written as short sentences, one per line, in every language.
20260927-17: Fix: in Artica, Reloading or bookmarking a Docker Manager page now reopens that page instead of showing a "not found" error.
20260927-17: Add: in Artica, The Docker menu in the left panel now opens its pages directly instead of through an extra sub-level.
20260927-17: Fix: in Artica Reverse Proxy, Docker Relay label publishing no longer stops for a whole Docker host when two containers share a long name, keeps working on hosts with very many containers, reports adopted backends correctly, and shows label values written between braces exactly as typed.
20260927-17: Add: in Artica, The Windows client adds an "Artica" search engine to web browsers: type "@artica" and a few words in Firefox (or add it to Chrome and Edge from the page the tray icon opens) to search the server's documents and open a result in one click.
20260927-17: Fix: in Artica, When the Docker Manager service fails to start, the real reason is now written to the monitoring log instead of being lost.
20260927-17: Add: in Artica, The Docker Manager service now records its process ID in /run/artica-docker.pid and can run as a true background daemon that reports whether it started successfully.
20260927-17: Add: in Artica Reverse Proxy, Docker Relay can now compress the traffic between Docker hosts and the reverse proxy, automatically skipping content that is already compressed, and shows the bandwidth saved for each backend.
20260927-17: Fix: in Artica, The whole Web console now refuses requests that do not come from the console itself: a link or a page on another site, or on another service of the appliance, can no longer make an administrator change a setting, while links to console pages still open them.
20260927-17: Fix: in Artica, The Samba package for Debian 12 now includes the Active Directory PAM module (pam_winbind), which was missing from it.
20260927-17: Add: in Artica Reverse Proxy, Each Docker Relay agent and backend now has graphs of its download and upload rates over the last hour, day, week and month, and of its monthly data consumption against its quota.
20260927-17: Fix: in Artica, Google Home, Nest and other devices no longer renew their DHCP address every few minutes: the DHCP server now answers renewals directly instead of broadcasting, unless "Always broadcast" is explicitly enabled.
20260927-17: Fix: in Artica, Samba file sharing and Active Directory tools no longer crash ("Bad talloc magic value") after the operating system installs its own Samba libraries: Artica's Samba now keeps all its libraries in a directory of its own.
20260927-17: Fix: in Artica, A Samba binary that cannot start no longer triggers the same error in the system log every 3 minutes; the check is retried after 6 hours or as soon as Samba is updated.
20260927-17: Fix: in Artica, Applying the DHCP configuration or the network settings no longer stops the DHCP service; it is now restarted with the new configuration.
20260927-17: Fix: in Artica, Devices that do not send a host name when they obtain a DHCP address are now recorded in the list of recent computers and the network inventory.
20260927-17: Fix: in Artica, The DHCP statistics collector can no longer slow down the DHCP service when it stops reading: excess log lines are now dropped instead of holding up the system logger.
20260927-17: Fix: in Artica, A device whose name contains words such as "conflict" or "denied" is no longer counted as a client refused by the DHCP server.
20260927-17: Fix: in Artica, The DHCP statistics collector now recovers by itself after an internal error instead of silently stopping while still showing as running.
20260927-17: Fix: in Artica, The DHCP statistics database now stays within its size limit: per-device hourly details are kept 14 days at most and the size limit never deletes the current day.
20260927-17: Add: in Artica Reverse Proxy, Docker Relay agents and backends can now be given upload and download speed limits and a monthly data quota, beyond which their traffic is slowed down until the next period.
20260927-17: Fix: in Artica, Error messages from 75 pages of the Web console (DHCP, DNS, proxy, keepalived, certificates, cluster, Kerberos, network interfaces and others) now show the value at fault as plain text and keep their accents, so a name, a database error or a reply from a remote node can no longer inject code into the console.
20260927-17: Fix: in Artica, The RDP Proxy policies page opens again (it failed to load since 2026-09-17), and the Kerberos connection test now shows its error message when the domain controller refuses the login.
20260927-17: Add: in Artica, The DHCP service now has a statistics dashboard showing requests over time, the most active devices, the most assigned addresses, the breakdown of DHCP message types and the clients refused by the server.
20260927-17: Add: in Artica, The DHCP events page now reads a real-time collector and can be filtered by device, address, message type and period.
20260927-17: Fix: in Artica, The DHCP status graphs now count every DHCP message, not only address confirmations, and no longer depend on image generation.
20260927-17: Fix: in Artica, Error messages displayed after saving a form in the Web console can no longer run code carried by the value that caused the error (for example a name typed in a field or an error returned by a service): the value is now always shown as plain text.
20260927-17: Fix: in Artica, Error messages shown after saving a form in the Web console now keep their accented letters and are no longer broken into lines wherever the letters "cr" appear (for example "secret" or "description").
20260927-17: Add: in Artica, The Docker Manager status page now lets administrators allow image downloads and builds from registries other than Docker Hub (for example a company registry), entry by entry.
20260927-17: Fix: in Artica, Starting, stopping and monitoring services can no longer mistake an administrator's shell or a log viewer that merely mentions a service for the service itself, which could kill that shell or leave the service down.
20260926-17: Fix: in Artica Proxy, www.apple.com is reachable again from the hotspot network; it was answered by the hotspot for every device, logged-in ones included.
20260926-17: Fix: in Artica, Reloading the DHCP service now restarts it with its rebuilt configuration instead of doing nothing, and it can no longer stop an unrelated process that merely mentions its PID file.
20260926-17: Fix: in Artica Proxy, Expired self-registered hotspot sessions are removed per device, without logging the same user out of their other devices.
20260926-17: Fix: in Artica, The Docker Manager no longer hands its operators the full Docker engine configuration (proxy settings, registry configuration, cluster addresses, labels): only the details shown on the Engine page are returned.
20260926-17: Fix: in Artica, A Docker Manager operator allowed to build images can now cancel their own build even without the image download permission, and cancelling a build now requires the build permission.
20260926-17: Fix: in Artica Proxy, A device whose hotspot voucher has expired can log in to the portal again instead of being refused with "your account is disabled" forever.
20260926-17: Fix: in Artica Proxy, Hotspot login error messages are now shown in the visitor's language instead of as raw codes.
20260926-17: Fix: in Artica, The Docker Manager pages now refuse requests that do not come from the console itself, so a link or a page on another site, or on another service of the appliance, can no longer make an administrator start an image download or any other Docker operation.
20260926-17: Fix: in Artica, The Docker Manager audit trail no longer grows without limit: it is rotated and compressed automatically, and the audit page opens quickly however long the history is.
20260926-17: Fix: in Artica Proxy, Hotspot users of the local LDAP directory can log in to the portal again, and their passwords are no longer written to the hotspot debug logs.
20260926-17: Add: in Artica, The Windows client can now search the server's documents from its tray icon and open a result directly, with suggestions while typing.
20260926-17: Fix: in Artica, Docker Manager operators now see only their own image downloads and console sessions, and can no longer open or close those of another operator, unless they are Docker administrators.
20260926-17: Fix: in Artica, A second Docker Manager process can no longer take over the socket of the running one, and stalled connections to the service are now closed after a few seconds.
20260926-17: Fix: in Artica, Stopping or upgrading the Docker Manager service now lets running operations finish, records interrupted image downloads as stopped, and no longer leaves its socket behind.
20260926-17: Add: in Artica Proxy, The hotspot status page has a new "Reconfigure all" button that rebuilds the captive-portal detection, the proxy rules for users not logged in yet and restarts the portal, with a progress bar; existing hotspots should run it once after the update.
20260926-17: Fix: in Artica Proxy, Changing only the final access rules now reloads the proxy as expected instead of leaving the previous rules active.
20260926-17: Fix: in Artica, Error messages of the Docker Manager are now translated and name the value at fault (registry, tag, folder, missing permission) instead of showing technical English codes.
20260926-17: Fix: in Artica Proxy, Hotspot users who are not logged in yet no longer get a "connection not secure" (ERR_SSL_PROTOCOL_ERROR) error on HTTPS sites: the connection is closed cleanly so the browser can bring up the login portal.
20260926-17: Fix: in Artica Proxy, The hotspot login portal now appears in Microsoft Edge, and devices that have already logged in are no longer told by Windows, Edge, Android, Apple or Firefox that they are still behind a login page.
20260926-17: Fix: in Artica, The DHCP server no longer starts answering on the uplink network of a multi-interface appliance when DHCP is enabled before any interface is configured, and a network card with its own DHCP settings now replaces the default service on that card.
20260926-17: Fix: in Artica, A Docker account allowed only to search images can now search Docker Hub and browse its tags.
20260926-17: Fix: in Artica, The Docker Manager can no longer be used to make the server connect to arbitrary internal addresses: image downloads and builds are limited to Docker Hub, and builds may not fetch files from URLs.
20260926-17: Fix: in Artica, The Docker Manager now shows the right repository and tag for images from a registry with a port (registry:5000/app:1.0) and no longer checks such images for updates against Docker Hub.
20260926-17: Fix: in Artica, Administrator audit trail entries written by the system service in the same second as another one are no longer lost.
20260926-17: Add: in Artica, Every Docker Manager operation (containers, console commands, log downloads, images, volumes, networks, sessions, service install, restart and uninstall) is now recorded in the administrator audit trail, from the Web console and from the Docker Manager service itself, including failed and refused attempts.
20260926-17: Add: in Artica, The Docker volumes page shows which containers use each volume.
20260926-17: Fix: in Artica, The Docker Manager now refuses to remove a volume, a network or an image still used by a container, even a stopped one, and names the containers to remove first.
20260926-17: Add: in Artica, The Windows client status window now shows this computer, your account and the last synchronization of each folder in a clear window, with a button to copy everything for support.
20260926-17: Fix: in Artica, The slow storage alert no longer fires on a short burst of scheduled disk activity: a disk must now be slow on two consecutive checks, measured with its real response time and only when it is actually busy.
20260926-17: Add: in Artica, The Windows client now has a Synchronization window to see the status of each synchronized folder, add or remove your own folders, pause a folder, sync now and review conflicts.
20260926-17: Fix: in Artica, The default SSH cipher list no longer offers the obsolete 3DES and CBC ciphers; appliances that had saved the former default switch to modern ciphers automatically.
20260926-17: Add: in Artica, The kernel is now hardened according to the ANSSI Linux configuration guide (kernel pointers hidden, BPF JIT hardened, kexec disabled, stricter FIFO protection), and existing appliances receive these settings automatically within minutes.
20260926-17: Fix: in Artica, The system configuration no longer declares IP forwarding as enabled on appliances that are not gateways.
20260926-17: Fix: in Artica, The Docker performance page no longer displays memory and traffic values as meaningless numbers.
20260926-17: Add: in Artica, The Docker events page now shows the history of the last hour, 6 hours or 24 hours with container and image names, instead of only the events of the few seconds it took to load.
20260926-17: Fix: in Artica, The Docker Manager now reports the real CPU usage of containers on current Debian systems, where it always showed 0%.
20260926-17: Add: in Artica, The Docker container console can now run commands inside a container and shows their output and exit code; each command is stopped after its timeout (60 seconds at most) and recorded in the Docker audit log.
20260926-17: Fix: in Artica, All Docker Manager pages are now translated and follow the standard console layout (search, header buttons, confirmation windows).
20260926-17: Add: in Artica, The Docker permissions page shows which account the Docker Manager sees for you, whether it is allowed, and explains how to grant access.
20260926-17: Fix: in Artica, The Docker performance page no longer times out when many containers are running: statistics are loaded progressively.
20260926-17: Add: in Artica, Docker networks can now be disconnected from a container, and connecting one offers the list of containers instead of a free text field.
20260926-17: Add: in Artica, The Docker containers page can remove a running container after an explicit warning, resume a paused container, and opens a detail window with logs, statistics and processes.
20260926-17: Fix: in Artica, The Docker container console now states clearly that interactive execution is not available instead of pretending a command ran.
20260926-17: Fix: in Artica, The Docker Manager pages now escape container, image and volume names everywhere, so a crafted name can no longer inject code into the page.
20260926-17: Fix: in Artica Proxy, The PostgreSQL connection manager no longer reuses connections that PgBouncer has already closed for inactivity, which made it rebuild its connection pool every few minutes.
20260926-17: Fix: in Artica Proxy, The nightly proxy statistics no longer fail with a closed database connection when the PostgreSQL connection pool is renewed during their computation.
20260926-17: Fix: in Artica, Containers created from the Docker Manager now really get the memory and CPU limits, restart policy, published ports and security options chosen when they were created.
20260926-17: Fix: in Artica, Opening a container that no longer exists in the Docker Manager now reports that it was not found instead of an engine error.
20260926-17: Fix: in Artica, The Docker Manager daemon no longer refuses to start after an interruption left its job history file damaged.
20260926-17: Fix: in Artica, An image download or build that the Docker engine refuses (authentication, network or corrupt layer) is now reported as failed instead of completed.
20260926-17: Fix: in Artica, The Docker Manager no longer shows container environment variable values (such as passwords) when a container is inspected.
20260926-17: Fix: in Artica, The Docker Manager no longer lets a container be mounted onto sensitive host paths (such as the Docker socket) through ".." sequences, symbolic links or the volumes field.
20260926-17: Add: in Artica, The Docker Manager page now has a Status tab showing the service state and version, with buttons to install, restart or uninstall the Docker Manager.
20260926-17: Add: in Artica, A Docker menu now gives administrators access to the Docker Manager pages (containers, images, volumes, networks, sessions, performance, events, audit) when Docker is enabled.
20260926-17: Fix: in Artica, The Docker Manager pages can no longer crash when loaded alongside the existing Docker status components.
20260926-17: Fix: in Artica, Installing the Docker Manager pages no longer replaces the Docker library used by the system status and web server status pages.
20260925-17: Fix: in Artica SMTP, The mail log tracker no longer grows in memory while messages wait in the deferred queue: each new delivery attempt now updates a single entry instead of adding one, which had driven the service beyond 6 GB of memory when a relay stayed unreachable.
20260925-17: Fix: in Artica, The What's new page now lists the latest changes first and shows their date in the version column.
20260925-17: Fix: in Artica SIEM, The statistics database is now restarted automatically when its logging stops working after the disk has been full, instead of consuming up to two CPU cores until someone restarts it by hand.
20260925-17: Fix: in Artica SIEM, The statistics database no longer writes its logs at trace level, which produced hundreds of kilobytes of messages per second.
20260925-17: Fix: in Artica SIEM, The service no longer reports hundreds of thousands of lost statistics buckets at each startup when the system metrics, 404 or reverse-proxy threat tables are still empty.
20260925-17: Fix: in Artica, The PostgreSQL connection manager no longer leaks a connection pool each time a health check fails.
20260925-17: Fix: in Artica Proxy, The nightly Kerberos renewal no longer reports an error on appliances where Kerberos authentication is not configured.
20260924-17: Fix: in Artica Proxy, Two proxy reloads requested a few seconds apart no longer kill Squid worker processes: reloads are now spaced at least 10 seconds apart.
20260924-17: Fix: in Artica Proxy, The periodic re-check of uncategorized websites no longer fails with timeouts against the categorization service, so unknown websites are really checked again.
20260924-17: Fix: in Artica Proxy, The transparent SOCKS redirector now installs the system library it actually needs on Debian 10, so it can start.
20260924-17: Fix: in Artica SIEM, The statistics database now really applies Artica's own settings, which were ignored because the service was started without its configuration file.
20260924-17: Fix: in Artica SIEM, A statistics table that can no longer be loaded after an unclean shutdown (empty damaged parts) is now repaired automatically instead of staying unavailable.
